"{\"title\":\"Generative AI for Learning and Development Professional Certificate by LinkedIn Learning\",\"courses\":[{\"course_title\":\"A Practical Guide to Upskilling Your Organization on AI\",\"course_admin_id\":2014059,\"metadata\":{\"Locale\":\"en_US\",\"Course ID\":2014059,\"Project ID\":null,\"Course Name\":\"A Practical Guide to Upskilling Your Organization on AI\",\"Course Name EN\":\"A Practical Guide to Upskilling Your Organization on AI\",\"Activation Status\":\"ACTIVE\",\"Display to Public\":\"Yes\",\"Display to QA\":\"No\",\"Course Description\":\"&lt;p&gt;LinkedIn Learning is investing in artificial intelligence across all roles and subjects to serve your entire organization, offering over 800 AI courses. Our \u201cone library\u201d investment provides general fluency across all professionals and technical levels while meeting skill and role-specific needs for individual contributors and leaders across your organization. In this course, learn how to leverage LinkedIn Learning's AI content offering in your organization, based on learner expertise and AI-readiness. Instead of a one-size fits all approach, LinkedIn Learning\u2019s AI Content Framework offers training across five levels\u2014understanding, applying, building, model maintaining and training, and deep specialization\u2014to optimize your organization\u2019s AI journey.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This course is part of a &lt;a href=https://www.linkedin.com/learning/paths/generative-ai-for-learning-and-development-professional-certificate-by-linkedin-learning target=_blank&gt;Professional Certificate&lt;/a&gt; from LinkedIn Learning.&lt;/p&gt;\",\"Course Short Description\":\"Learn how to leverage LinkedIn Learning's AI upskilling framework in your organization.\",\"Content Type\":\"SKILLS\",\"Localization Type\":\"ORIGINAL\",\"Original Course Locale\":null,\"Original Course ID\":null,\"Equivalent English Course\":null,\"Instructor ID\":\"21874000, 21872001\",\"Instructor Name\":\"Megan Leatham, Brandi Shailer\",\"Instructor Transliterated Name\":\", \",\"Instructor Short Bio\":\"Manager of Content at LinkedIn Learning|Senior Manager of Content at LinkedIn Learning\",\"Author Payment Category\":\"NONE, NONE\",\"Delivery Mode\":\"ALL_AT_ONCE\",\"Series End Date\":null,\"Course Release Date\":\"2024-05-03\",\"Course Updated Date\":\"2025-04-02\",\"Course Archive Date\":null,\"Course Retire Date\":null,\"Replacement Course\":null,\"Has Assessment\":\"No\",\"Has Challenge/Solution\":\"Yes\",\"LIL URL\":\"https://www.linkedin.com/learning/a-practical-guide-to-upskilling-your-organization-on-ai\",\"Series\":\"One-Off\",\"Limited Series\":null,\"Manager Level\":\"General\",\"LI Level\":\"General\",\"LI Level EN\":\"General\",\"Sensitivity\":null,\"Internal Library\":\"Business\",\"Internal Subject\":\"Artificial Intelligence for Business\",\"Primary Software\":null,\"Media Type\":\"Video\",\"Has CEU\":\"No\",\"Has Exercise Files\":\"Yes\",\"Visible Duration\":1397.0,\"Visible Video Count\":12.0,\"Learning Objectives\":null,\"Contract Type\":\"EMPLOYEE, EMPLOYEE\",\"Certifications\":null,\"Framework Topic\":\"AI Framework Level 4: Training and Maintaining Models\",\"Automatic Caption Translations\":\"Global Captions\",\"Automatic Metadata Translations\":\"Global Metadata\",\"Gen AI Feature Flag\":null,\"Hands-On Practice\":null,\"Hands-On Practice Library\":null,\"Unlocked for Viva Learning\":\"Global Captions\",\"Free Course\":null,\"Certification Library\":null,\"Github Codespace\":null,\"Skills Count\":3,\"Skills\":\"AI for Recruiting,Artificial Intelligence for Business,Employee Learning & Development\",\"Skills EN\":\"AI for Recruiting,Artificial Intelligence for Business,Employee Learning & Development\",\"Content Manager\":\"Marjorie Page\",\"Acquisition Manager\":\"Marjorie Page\",\"Framework Subject\":\"AI Framework Level 4: Training and Maintaining Models\"},\"sections\":[{\"duration\":85,\"entries\":[{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:2015268\",\"duration\":85,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":null,\"name\":\"How is AI reshaping the skills today's organizations need?\",\"fileName\":\"2014059_en_US_00_01_VT\",\"demo\":true,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":119,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Learn how AI is reshaping the skills, functions, and L&D strategies that today's organizations need. Job postings on LinkedIn mentioning GPT or ChatGPT skills increased by 21x since November 2022.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":5350017,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":true,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- Right now, most LinkedIn members are in jobs\\nwhere they could automate at least\\na quarter of their routine tasks.\\nI mean, think about the impact this has on productivity\\nfor you, your department, your business,\\ncreative and technical professionals,\\nyour whole organization.\\n- Yeah, and with the release of generative AI tools,\\nAI is everywhere, as a result, one thing is for certain,\\nwe are witnessing a shift in skills,\\nhow we hire and how we define productivity.\\n\\nAI is changing the world right before our eyes.\\nAnd we all know we should do something, but what?\\n- Well thinking about and teaching about AI upskilling,\\nit's what we've done at LinkedIn Learning for over a decade.\\nWe work with some of the world's\\ngreatest AI experts and organizations.\\nWe're informed by over 1 billion LinkedIn members\\nand organizations contributing to LinkedIn's economic graph.\\nAnd we employ world-class learning experts who think about\\nand stay on top of the trends every day.\\n\\n- We are ready with a vision, a point of view, a framework,\\nand a plan to partner with you in this moment.\\n- So let's do this.\\nWe'll see you in the next videos\\nto start building your AI upskilling plan.\\n\"}],\"name\":\"Introduction\",\"size\":5350017,\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentChapter:2014335\"},{\"duration\":243,\"entries\":[{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:3911013\",\"duration\":109,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Your organization's AI upskilling opportunity\",\"fileName\":\"2014059_en_US_01_01_VT\",\"demo\":true,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":792,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"While upskilling an organization on AI can be overwhelming, it is possible, especially with a valued partner like LinkedIn. It's important to acknowledge the challenges inherent in AI adoption as well as the opportunities that working with an industry-leading partner can bring as you embark on the journey.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":5426768,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- Investing and upskilling\\nwill keep your employees around longer\\nand retention is a big deal for every organization\\nbecause retention leads to long-term business success,\\nand the connection between learning, growth,\\nand retention is clear.\\n76% of employees report staying longer\\nif their company is invested in learning and development,\\nbut 50% of those people think they need\\nto change companies to grow.\\n\\nUpskilling has become essential,\\nand upskilling in AI is becoming more critical than ever.\\nAn organization's upskilling needs can get complex quickly.\\nOnce you consider whether the right people\\nare in the right roles, what human skills\\nand what AI skills are required for those roles?\\nLet's think about this for a minute.\\nAn entry-level sales rep\\nis going to need very different skills\\ncompared to a seasoned sales manager\\nwho's running the whole division, right?\\nAnd then you have a data analyst crunching numbers\\nbehind the scenes who needs an entirely different skillset.\\n\\nIt's not a one-size-fits-all for every role.\\nAnd then comes a question, so how ready are you?\\nWhat's your organization's AI readiness?\\nAssessing AI readiness across the org is key\\nto designing an AI strategy aligned to the three stages\\nof AI adoption and implementation.\\nEmerging, accelerating, and leading.\\nThis could get overwhelming quickly,\\nbut it doesn't have to.\\nYou can upskill your entire organization with LinkedIn.\\n\\nWe are your trusted partner with a wealth of resources\\nand expertise to help guide you through it.\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4026148\",\"duration\":134,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"How LinkedIn\u2019s AI content gives you an advantage\",\"fileName\":\"2014059_en_US_01_02_FY25Q4_VT\",\"demo\":true,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":135,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"editingNotes\":\"Cut audio only 00:44-00:45 to remove \\\"hundreds of.\\\" The resulting line would be: \\\"Our expanding library of high-quality AI courses....\\\"\",\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false,\"updateType\":\"UPDATED\"},\"description\":null,\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":7362960,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- At LinkedIn, our goal is\\nto be your partner in upskilling your org on AI.\\nTo do that, we are building the world's leading enterprise\\nAI learning portfolio\\norganized into an upskilling framework.\\nPicture this,\\nan AI learning center offering everything from understanding\\nthe basics to advanced AI models.\\nThe framework is like having a personal tutor\\nsitting right by your side ready to guide you\\nthrough this maze of complex information.\\n\\nWhat makes it so special is our mix\\nof vetted industry experts, insider knowledge,\\nand a whole lot of dedication to being the best.\\nOur expanding libraries of high quality AI courses\\nstretches across seven languages\\nwith over 20 additional languages and subtitles.\\nLeveraging your LinkedIn content portfolio can future proof\\nyour business at every level of your organization.\\nAnd our goal is to really help you do this\\nby doing three things.\\n\\nFirst, we provide relevant and specific content.\\nThis means AI content\\nspecifically for you as an L&D professional\\nto keep you on trend and ahead of it.\\nCheck out the learning path of becoming\\nan AI powered L&D professional\\nto get started and see for yourself.\\nSecond, we keep our AI content fresh.\\nWe are auditing, reviewing, and updating our content quickly\\nand responsibly.\\nOur content changes at the pace of AI\\nand we have a team of content strategists\\nmonitoring these changes to keep pace as AI evolves.\\n\\nThe one constant with AI, is change.\\nAnd three, we do the research, the data analysis,\\nand the curriculum planning for you.\\nWe'll take the heavy lifting off your plate\\nand delivered packaged ready-made curriculums\\nthat promote skill building across roles.\\nWe know this increases retention\\nand positive career outcomes.\\nAll in all, we are your partner in delivering AI upskilling\\nto the entire org so that you can maintain\\nand expand your competitive advantage.\\n\\n\"}],\"name\":\"1. Beginning Your Organization\u2019s AI Journey Now\",\"size\":12789728,\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentChapter:2014336\"},{\"duration\":668,\"entries\":[{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:3905193\",\"duration\":185,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"What is the LinkedIn AI Content Framework?\",\"fileName\":\"2014059_en_US_02_01_VT\",\"demo\":true,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":750,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Learn about the different levels of the LinkedIn AI Content Framework. Each department in your organization may be at a different level of AI readiness; therefore, you should not use a one-size-fits-all approach to upskilling.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":8486519,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- Every department in your organization is likely\\nto be at a different level of AI readiness,\\nwhich is why we've created the Upskilling Framework.\\nNo matter what state\\nof the AI journey your organization is at,\\nthis framework will better serve\\nevery employee's AI learning journey\\nbecause it is a journey, not a destination.\\nThe AI Upskilling Framework will help your organization\\nkeep pace with change by helping you create\\na strategy to upskill and retain your employees.\\n\\nOrganizations need the right AI skills content\\nfor the right people to facilitate learning.\\nAnd LinkedIn Learning's Upskilling Framework\\ndoes this for you.\\nThis structured matrix-like learning model,\\nprovides custom curated content\\nto upskill specific roles or skills in AI.\\nThis curation serves learners and learning\\nand development professionals time\\nby pre-selecting the most relevant up-to-date\\nengaging AI skill-based content\\nthat can quickly be deployed no matter\\nwhat systems you're working in, like in LMS.\\n\\nWhen we created our AI learning Upskilling Framework,\\nwe considered a few things.\\nFirst, AI readiness can vary across\\nindustries and departments.\\nIt's truly not a one size fits all approach\\nto upskilling all roles.\\nIt just doesn't work.\\nSo to address this issue,\\nwe provided a layered approach\\nto upskilling your organization on AI.\\nThink Bloom's Taxonomy,\\nwhere there are specific learning outcomes\\nattached to each level.\\nWithin the AI Upskilling Framework,\\nthere are five levels.\\n\\nThey are progressing from understanding AI to applying,\\nto building, to maintaining, to training,\\nand at the very top specialized AI skills.\\nSecond, different audiences need different things\\nfrom our Upskilling Framework tailored\\nto what they need in their roles.\\nFor example, individual learners want to upskill\\nto field job satisfaction and future proof their careers.\\nWhile L&D professionals need\\nto design targeted global training programs\\nthat align with organizational goals\\nto address AI skill gaps.\\n\\nAnd finally, senior leaders seek\\nholistic global learning programs\\nto cut costs and enhance efficiency across the organization.\\nThird, role progression is ideal\\nand often necessary for retention.\\nAs you can see in the framework, content is organized\\nby depth of knowledge required.\\nAt the lower level is foundational AI knowledge needed\\nby all roles for fluency.\\nAt the highest level is deep understanding needed\\nfor specialized technical roles in industries.\\n\\nWe created this framework\\nto take your organization on individual learning journeys,\\ndepending on AI readiness, career goals,\\nand role progression through five levels\\nof the Upskilling Framework.\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:3908098\",\"duration\":81,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"AI Content Framework level 1: Understanding\",\"fileName\":\"2014059_en_US_02_02_VT\",\"demo\":true,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":260,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":true},\"description\":\"Applying level one of the LinkedIn AI Content Framework can ensure that everyone in the org has the same understanding of key definitions and language to talk about AI.  Level one of the AI Content Framework builds AI fluency and awareness based on your org's level of AI or generative AI understanding assessed during your AI upskilling needs assessment.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":3892198,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- How could you possibly curate content\\nfor your entire organization to become AI-fluent\\nand stay ahead of all the trends?\\nWhere do you even start when you want to learn more about AI?\\nIt all seems daunting, right?\\nWell, let's look at level one of our upskilling framework\\nfor the answer.\\nOur level one content is baseline understanding\\nfor every professional.\\nIt's a ready-to-deploy solution\\nwhether someone's a business leader,\\na creative mind, a technical professional,\\nor just looking to boost their skills.\\n\\nIt's a foundational groundwork your team needs to succeed.\\nThis level consists of courses, learning paths,\\nand certificates.\\nYou'll find topics like what is AI,\\nethical and responsible AI, tools and software awareness,\\nbusiness strategy implications for leaders and managers,\\nand how technology trends have business impact.\\nRegardless of role, this level upskills professionals\\nfrom understanding the basics to building AI fluency.\\n\\nStaying on top of AI and responsible business practices\\nis crucial and challenging, and layer one\\nof our framework is the solution.\\nOur content will keep you and your team ahead of the game.\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:3911015\",\"duration\":112,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"AI Content Framework level 2: Applying\",\"fileName\":\"2014059_en_US_02_03_VT\",\"demo\":true,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":532,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Applying level two of LinkedIn AI Content Framework increases productivity and informs strategy. Having met the goals of level one,  learners and leaders are ready to practically leverage AI to optimize their workflows through increased productivity and informed strategy.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":5554020,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- Level one of our upskilling framework\\nis all about understanding AI.\\nOnce learners gain that basic AI fluency,\\nthey progress to level two, which is all about taking action\\nor applying those AI skills.\\nAnd though it's challenging to meet the needs\\nof all learners the higher up the pyramid we go,\\nour content curation has you covered.\\nLevel two content is for everyone:\\nleaders, managers, specialists at all levels\\nwho use AI to boost productivity\\nor manage teams that do.\\n\\nThese courses meet learners where they're at\\nand they show them how to work with AI\\nand accelerate their work,\\nleaving more time for critical human skills\\nto drive transformation.\\nLevel two courses teach foundational skills\\nlike prompt engineering and how to think critically using AI\\nand cover how to apply AI for human skills\\nlike communication, conflict resolution, and resilience.\\nAnd there is a wealth of content\\nfor those in leadership and strategy roles\\non everything from building collaborative team culture\\nwith AI to harnessing AI for business strategy.\\n\\nWe offer role-specific guidance.\\nIn level two, you'll find courses\\nlike generative AI for project management,\\ncreating a collaborative team culture with AI,\\nand building a GenAI tech strategy.\\nAnd if your company uses Microsoft 365,\\nwe offer best-in-class coverage for Microsoft Copilot.\\nPlus, we offer tailored learning paths\\nsuch as develop your prompt engineering skills,\\ngetting started with custom GPTs\\nand building AI aptitude as an aspiring manager.\\n\\nOur level two content helps your learners apply AI skills\\nacross multiple roles and boost productivity.\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4028168\",\"duration\":102,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"AI Content Framework level 3: Building\",\"fileName\":\"2014059_en_US_02_04_FY25Q4_VT\",\"demo\":true,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":102,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"editingNotes\":\"From 00:29\u201300:42 add new slide 1. From 01:02-01:05 add new slide 2.\",\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false,\"updateType\":\"UPDATED\"},\"description\":\"\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":4200248,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- Some people in your organization\\nalready have foundational AI skills.\\nThey may even have experience with prompt engineering.\\nThey're ready to actually customize things,\\nmake things relevant for the business you're doing today.\\nThat person may even be you.\\nFor those learners,\\nwe have our Building layer of the framework.\\nIn the Building layer,\\nyou'll find courses and learning paths\\nfor those who are ready to take that next step.\\nWhat skills will learners be honing?\\nThink APIs, including the OpenAI API,\\ncustom GPTs, tools like Hugging Face,\\nSemantic Kernel, Gemini.\\n\\nThey may even dabble into databases.\\nWe have options like our 11 course series\\non the OpenAI API,\\nso developers can start working with leading tools today.\\nBut you don't have to be a developer.\\nThere's plenty of low and no-code options.\\nYour power users will find courses like,\\nBuild Your Own GPTs.\\nAnd you'll find numerous courses\\ndedicated to hands-on practice and building AI projects.\\nThis is the layer\\nwhere you move your skill building\\nfrom using AI to creating with AI.\\n\\nNow, the higher up the pyramid we go,\\nthe more challenging the content\\nmay be to curate without deep technical knowledge.\\nSo lean on resources like our content mapping to help you.\\nYou'll have a turnkey way to grab\\nthe growing course list by topic and by role.\\nSo whether learners are seasoned developers\\nor just starting out,\\nwe've got something to fuel curiosity and enhance skills.\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:3907140\",\"duration\":77,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"AI Content Framework level 4: Training and maintaining models\",\"fileName\":\"2014059_en_US_02_05_VT\",\"demo\":true,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":371,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":true},\"description\":\"Explore level four of the LinkedIn AI Content Framework. The level readies you for developing AI tools and training AI models. With levels one through three in process or complete, upskilling your technical learners on applications of AI and ML models, deep learning, and fine-tuning models is the next step in your org's AI journey.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":3772279,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- Get ready to roll up your sleeves and elevate some skills.\\nIn layer four, you'll find courses focused on foundational\\nand advanced AI and machine learning principles.\\nThis content is primarily for AI\\nand machine learning engineers\\nand some data scientists who are ready to dive deep\\ninto the world of training and maintaining models.\\nNow, whether you're building a team\\nof aspiring machine learning engineers,\\nor they've been in the field a while\\nand need advanced-level training,\\nthere's something here for your team.\\n\\nNow, what can learners expect?\\nAspiring machine learning engineers\\ncan explore foundational topics,\\nlike our five-course series, \\\"Machine Learning with Python,\\\"\\nor dive into AI specialties\\nlike \\\"Deep Learning and Neural Networks.\\\"\\nThey can hone their advanced skills for training,\\nmaintaining and optimizing models.\\nSo for topics, think reinforcement learning, computer vision\\nand popular machine learning libraries\\nlike PyTorch, TensorFlow and NumPy.\\n\\nAnd of course, we've built plenty\\nof learning paths to guide you.\\nNow, whether your team wants to specialize\\nin machine learning, deep learning\\nor NLP, natural language processing,\\nwe've got you covered.\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:2014334\",\"duration\":111,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"AI Content Framework level 5: Deeply specializing\",\"fileName\":\"2014059_en_US_02_06_VT\",\"demo\":true,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":366,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":true},\"description\":\"Explore level five of the LinkedIn AI Content Framework. Depending on your industry, you may have technical roles responsible for developing new AI products, redesigning existing products, and performing research and testing on product concepts. The goal of level five is to upskill advanced AI specialists and those in R&D (research and development) on advanced topics machine learning research and cybersecurity.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":5819132,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- Okay, so what about specialized skills?\\nAI directly impacts deeply technical and specialized roles.\\nThink DevOps, data scientists, researchers.\\nAnd the evolution of AI has brought in new, important terms\\nlike AIOps, MLOps, LLMOps.\\nWe've got the alphabet soup covered for you.\\nPlus, we'll cover AI security and AI cloud solutions,\\nincluding AWS Azure and Google Cloud platform.\\n\\nIf your team is eyeing certifications,\\nwe're ready to prepare your learners for success.\\nIf certification is important to your organization\\nor their career ladders,\\nyou'll find dozens of AI\\nand machine learning certification prep courses\\nall curated for you.\\nHave an employee aiming to add a shiny new certificate\\nto their profile?\\nYou'll find courses\\nlike Prepare for the AWS\\nCertified Machine Learning Specialty Exam,\\nas well as Prepare for the Google Cloud\\nProfessional Machine Learning Engineer Certificate,\\nalong with many more.\\n\\nNow, what about those who aren't so certification-hungry?\\nFor those learners, we've curated specific learning paths\\nto guide them through their journey.\\nYou'll find paths like Develop Your AI Skills\\nwith Google Gemini and Google Cloud Platform,\\nDevelop Your AI skills as a Cybersecurity Professional,\\nor Foundational AI Skills for Azure Administration.\\nSo whether your team is seeking\\nto deepen their expertise in MLOps\\nfortify their AI security knowledge,\\nor prepare for certifications,\\nour offerings will take care of everything.\\n\\nThis level will make sure you have what your team needs.\\n\"}],\"name\":\"2. The AI Upskilling Framework\",\"size\":31724396,\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentChapter:3911016\"},{\"duration\":307,\"entries\":[{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:3910064\",\"duration\":170,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Build your AI upskilling strategy\",\"fileName\":\"2014059_en_US_03_01_VT\",\"demo\":true,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":516,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":true},\"description\":\"Identify where your org is on the AI-readiness journey and align with stakeholders like business leaders, CTOs, CIOs, CDOs, and more who are integral to building and executing your AI upskilling strategy. Oversight of AI within an organization's structure can vary depending on the company's size, industry, and specific needs.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":6925956,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- Now that you have a grasp of the AI upskilling framework,\\nhow do you turn it into action?\\nAs a learning and development professional,\\nit's time for you to speak the language of AI.\\nSo where do you begin if you're not an AI expert?\\nRight here with the basics.\\nStart with our learning path on becoming\\nan AI-powered learning and development professional,\\nwhere you'll understand key concepts and terminology.\\nUnderstanding these key AI concepts\\nis like learning the alphabet before writing a novel.\\n\\nIt's the foundation you'll stand on\\nas you build your own skills.\\nAnd remember, you don't need to be an AI expert,\\nbut developing a strategic understanding is essential.\\nFocus on your fluency.\\nJust learn the language, just enough to engage\\nin strategic conversations with your stakeholders.\\nNow, whether your organization is just experimenting\\nwith AI in its early stages, standardizing AI adoption,\\nor you're leading the charge with AI\\nas a core business strategy,\\naligning with your stakeholders here is crucial.\\n\\nSo you're going to want to identify the decision makers\\nwho will champion your AI initiatives.\\nNow, this collaboration often involves\\ngetting with the business leaders, your CTO,\\nyour CIO, potentially a CDO,\\nand together you'll assess your organizational AI needs\\nand the skills gaps you need to fill.\\nYou'll understand your current state\\nand envision your ideal state.\\nYou'll work with these stakeholders to identify\\nand understand the different needs\\nin different parts of your organization.\\n\\nIf you need a place to start,\\nconsider the AI upskilling framework levels\\nso you can approach different parts of your organization\\nfrom general and functional skill gaps\\nto technical skill gaps.\\nSet clear objectives and KPIs\\nto measure your progress and your success.\\nAlign your AI upskilling objectives\\nwith your overall business strategy and goals.\\nPrioritize those objectives based on\\ntheir potential impact and their feasibility.\\n\\nFinally, identify your target audience\\nand prioritize key roles and skills.\\nConsider the current skill levels\\nand the desired proficiency in AI\\nand plan for role-based upskilling,\\ntailored to the needs of different teams.\\nIt's about empowering the right people\\nwith the right AI skills to drive initiatives\\nand foster a culture of learning and innovation.\\nRemember, you don't have to do it all at once.\\n\\nUpskilling your organization on AI is a journey.\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:3904276\",\"duration\":137,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Build customized, role-based, AI learning journeys\",\"fileName\":\"2014059_en_US_03_02_VT\",\"demo\":true,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":613,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"handoutNotes\":\"AI Upskilling Framework Content Mapping\",\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":true},\"description\":\"Map key roles against the AI Content Framework to recommend LinkedIn-built learning paths to specific groups within the org. This is a powerful way to tailor your AI upskilling content to roles and levels of AI-readiness.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":5178457,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- You can define your organization's upskilling\\nby thinking about four key factors\\nto decide what learning content you'll need.\\nFirst, what is the job function?\\nAre you serving a marketing professional, a developer, a VP?\\nSecond, what is the industry vertical?\\nThe needs are different if your organization\\nis in the healthcare industry versus finance.\\nThird, what job levels are you trying to serve?\\nIs it individual contributors?\\nDo they need hands-on training?\\nOr are you trying to help the C-suite,\\nwho may need a higher level of understanding\\nand strategy for AI?\\nFourth, what are the specific skills or tools\\nyour organization needs to learn?\\nAre you investing in tools, like a new copilot,\\nand your organization's asking for help upskilling?\\nIf so, you'll need to find content\\nto help them learn those specific tools.\\n\\nOnce you've pinpointed the key AI skills and roles,\\nit's time to harness the power of LinkedIn learning.\\nUtilize the AI upskilling framework content mapping,\\nprovided in this course, to lay out a strategic plan\\nto recommend courses and LinkedIn built learning paths\\nto target specific groups.\\nThis will ensure each path aligns\\nwith your organization's roles and your growth objectives.\\nDive deeper by customizing learning paths\\nwith a mix of LinkedIn learning courses\\nand your own content, even select third party resources.\\n\\nAnd this blend will give you a unique, rich,\\ndiverse learning experience that caters to the varied\\nlearning styles and needs of your organization.\\nYou can even further enhance learning\\nwith customized role guides.\\nDevelop AI specific role guides\\nthat outline the AI competencies required for each position.\\nYou can then add LinkedIn learning content,\\nor custom content specific to the role guide you customize.\\n\\nFinally, utilize LinkedIn's campaign features\\nto help drive engagement.\\nFor more on how to do each of these steps,\\nand other features you can utilize,\\nsee our admin guide course.\\n\"}],\"name\":\"3. From Framework to Action\",\"size\":12104413,\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentChapter:3905194\"},{\"duration\":394,\"entries\":[{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:3910063\",\"duration\":94,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":null,\"name\":\"What's next?\",\"fileName\":\"2014059_en_US_04_01_VT\",\"demo\":true,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":222,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Learn about the specific actions you can take immediately after watching the course.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":4326747,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- Now that we've discussed\\nthe AI Upskilling Framework in detail,\\nyou know that we have content\\nthat maps to each of the levels,\\nand how to apply these levels\\nto take action in the real world.\\nSo what's next?\\n- Well, here's a recommendation on where to start,\\nbecause oftentimes this is where the real work begins.\\nStart with an assessment\\nof your organization's AI readiness.\\nThis includes identifying what AI tools\\nyour organization will be leveraging.\\nDetermine how you'll ramp across the organization.\\n\\nAre you going to upskill just one role?\\nThe whole organization?\\nLeverage the AI Upskilling Framework\\nto create and customize your learning journey,\\nand empower your managers with the identified roles\\nand change management tools and support\\nto create a culture of learning,\\nand create an action plan and a timeline.\\nRemember, the landscape of AI is ever evolving.\\nYour upskilling strategy should be too.\\nKeep monitoring your team's progress\\nand keep iterating your approach.\\n\\n- By consistently measuring\\nand evaluating your AI upskilling efforts,\\nyou create a culture of continuous improvement.\\nIt's about being proactive, adaptive, and results-driven.\\nLead your organization to AI mastery, one skill at a time.\\nRemember, LinkedIn is your partner\\nin upskilling your entire organization.\\nWe are here for you, and in it together.\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4027141\",\"duration\":0,\"visible\":false,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":null,\"name\":\"FAKEVIDEO: AI glossary\",\"fileName\":\"2014059_en_US_04_02_FAKEVIDEO_FY25Q4\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":300,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false,\"updateType\":\"ADDED\"},\"description\":null,\"captionsStatus\":\"NOT_AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"NOT_ATTEMPTED\",\"size\":0,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"NEW\",\"transcript\":null},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentArticle:14004\",\"duration\":300,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"AI glossary\"}],\"name\":\"4. Conclusion\",\"size\":4326747,\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentChapter:3907141\"}],\"size\":66295301,\"duration\":1697,\"zeroBased\":false},{\"course_title\":\"The Future of Workforce Learning: AI-Powered Personalization for Skill Development\",\"course_admin_id\":3884342,\"metadata\":{\"Locale\":\"en_US\",\"Course ID\":3884342,\"Project ID\":null,\"Course Name\":\"The Future of Workforce Learning: AI-Powered Personalization for Skill Development\",\"Course Name EN\":\"The Future of Workforce Learning: AI-Powered Personalization for Skill Development\",\"Activation Status\":\"ACTIVE\",\"Display to Public\":\"Yes\",\"Display to QA\":\"No\",\"Course Description\":\"&lt;p&gt;This course explores the transformative role of artificial intelligence (AI) in reshaping workforce learning and development strategies. Learning and development leader Susan Makinda introduces you to the potential of AI to create personalized learning experiences, focusing on enhancing skill development tailored to individual and organizational needs. After this course, you'll have a comprehensive understanding of how AI can revolutionize professional development and learning experiences.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This course is part of a &lt;a href=https://www.linkedin.com/learning/paths/generative-ai-for-learning-and-development-professional-certificate-by-linkedin-learning target=_blank&gt;Professional Certificate&lt;/a&gt; from LinkedIn Learning.&lt;/p&gt;\",\"Course Short Description\":\"Learn innovative strategies and technologies to equip your organization to tap into AI for professional development.\",\"Content Type\":\"SKILLS\",\"Localization Type\":\"ORIGINAL\",\"Original Course Locale\":null,\"Original Course ID\":null,\"Equivalent English Course\":null,\"Instructor ID\":\"21401000, 20891001\",\"Instructor Name\":\"Madecraft Licensor, Susan  Makinda\",\"Instructor Transliterated Name\":\", \",\"Instructor Short Bio\":\"Full-Service Learning Content Company|Learning and Development Leader\",\"Author Payment Category\":\"LICENSED, NONE\",\"Delivery Mode\":\"ALL_AT_ONCE\",\"Series End Date\":null,\"Course Release Date\":\"2024-08-08\",\"Course Updated Date\":null,\"Course Archive Date\":null,\"Course Retire Date\":null,\"Replacement Course\":null,\"Has Assessment\":\"No\",\"Has Challenge/Solution\":\"Yes\",\"LIL URL\":\"https://www.linkedin.com/learning/the-future-of-workforce-learning-ai-powered-personalization-for-skill-development,https://www.linkedin.com/learning/the-future-of-workforce-learning-ai-powered-personalization-for-skill-development-licensed-tlp\",\"Series\":\"Limited Series\",\"Limited Series\":null,\"Manager Level\":\"General\",\"LI Level\":\"General\",\"LI Level EN\":\"General\",\"Sensitivity\":null,\"Internal Library\":\"Business\",\"Internal Subject\":\"HR\",\"Primary Software\":null,\"Media Type\":\"Video\",\"Has CEU\":\"No\",\"Has Exercise Files\":\"Yes\",\"Visible Duration\":2184.0,\"Visible Video Count\":14.0,\"Learning Objectives\":\"Identify skills that can grow with AI.,Personalize learning with AI.,Implement an AI learning strategy.,Analyze learning outcomes.,Predict AI-powered learning trends.\",\"Contract Type\":\"LICENSED, NO_CONTRACT\",\"Certifications\":null,\"Framework Topic\":\"AI Upskilling Framework\",\"Automatic Caption Translations\":\"Global Captions\",\"Automatic Metadata Translations\":\"Global Metadata\",\"Gen AI Feature Flag\":null,\"Hands-On Practice\":null,\"Hands-On Practice Library\":null,\"Unlocked for Viva Learning\":\"Global Captions\",\"Free Course\":null,\"Certification Library\":null,\"Github Codespace\":null,\"Skills Count\":3,\"Skills\":\"AI for HR,Artificial Intelligence for Business,Employee Learning & Development\",\"Skills EN\":\"AI for HR,Artificial Intelligence for Business,Employee Learning & Development\",\"Content Manager\":\"Pete Meyers\",\"Acquisition Manager\":\"Pete Meyers\",\"Framework Subject\":\"AI Framework Level 2: Applying\"},\"sections\":[{\"duration\":83,\"entries\":[{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4262491\",\"duration\":83,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Boost organizational learning with AI\",\"fileName\":\"3884342_en_US_00_01_VT\",\"demo\":true,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":84,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"The landscape of learning is rapidly changing, with new advancements possible through the power of AI. After this course, you'll be able to incorporate and utilize AI to personalize your learning and development programs.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":3132875,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":true,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"Skills that are vital today might be obsolete tomorrow.\\nHow ready is your organization to adapt to the ever changing skills landscape?\\nWell, with individual skill needs evolving rapidly, organizations\\nmust quickly adapt to ensure employees not only perform, but also drive\\norganizational growth.\\nEnter AI, your guide to driving learning forward. Integrating AI\\ninto your learning approach will be a strategic ally for every organization.\\n\\nIt makes learning agile,\\nand personalized to perfectly aligned with current skills and future needs.\\nMy name is Susan Makinda,\\nand as a passionate learning and development leader,\\nI am committed to driving organizational growth\\nthrough innovative learning strategies.\\nIn this course, I'll take you on a journey through the world of AI in learning.\\nI'll talk about ways to use AI to design learning experiences,\\nweave AI into your learning strategy and figure out how to measure the success\\nand impact.\\n\\nListen, AI\\nisn't just a passing trend.\\nIt's here to stay in every industry.\\nToday, I'm going to zero in on unleashing AI\\nskill potential within the learning landscape.\\nReady to jump in? Let's get to it.\\n\"}],\"name\":\"Introduction\",\"size\":3132875,\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentChapter:4272117\"},{\"duration\":485,\"entries\":[{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4270159\",\"duration\":168,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Identify skills that can grow with AI\",\"fileName\":\"3884342_en_US_01_01_VT\",\"demo\":true,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":168,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Many organizations are moving toward skill-based learning. After this lesson, you'll be able to define what skills can grow with the help of AI and analyze the basics of AI and its implications for learning and development.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":6543866,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"Have you noticed how certain skills\\nsuddenly become essential while others fade away?\\nThis fluctuation is driven by new technologies,\\nchanging business needs, and economic shifts.\\nIn the AI-driven world, knowing which skills will be in demand is crucial.\\nIn this lesson, I'll navigate through the skills landscape,\\nshowing how AI can assist your organization in upskilling and training your team.\\nFirst, you'll want to consider\\nan AI approach to support cognitive and technical skill enhancement.\\n\\nAI has the ability to enhance cognitive skills such as problem solving,\\nas well as technical skills such as coding and data analysis.\\nThe exciting part is that AI can help your learners enhance their skills,\\nmaking them more sharper, more advanced\\nthrough personalized learning paths that can mirror real world experiences.\\nA practical approach is to incorporate AI-powered learning platforms\\ninto your learning ecosystem.\\n\\nThese platforms can help provide complex problem solving and coding challenges\\ncustomized to each learner's pace and style.\\nNext up, AI simulations can also help with soft skills development.\\nYou can use AI to create scenarios that simulate real life interactions,\\ngiving your team a playground to develop those ever important skills\\ncommunication, empathy, leadership, you name it.\\nThese interactive simulations offer a dynamic environment for soft\\nskill improvement,\\nwith tailored feedback for various social and professional situations.\\n\\nAnd finally, don't forget about continuous learning and adaptability.\\nAI is here to champion a culture where learning never stops and flexibility\\nis the name of the game.\\nIt does this by serving up the freshest content and learning opportunities\\nthat align with the latest trends and skills out there.\\nSo leverage this to track\\nin-demand skill trends and find new learning opportunities.\\nThis way, your team remains on their toes, eager\\nto learn new skills, and adapt to whatever changes come their way.\\n\\nNow, equipped with this AI-focused skills landscape,\\nyou\u2019re prepared to nurture a workforce\\nthat supports growth and response to emerging demands.\\nI recommend starting with an AI feature that targets a key skill area,\\nallowing you to see AI's transformative impact on skill development firsthand.\\nIn an era where adaptability is essential,\\nintegrating AI into your learning strategies is not just beneficial,\\nbut it's imperative.\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4273008\",\"duration\":159,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Data-driven learning environments\",\"fileName\":\"3884342_en_US_01_02_VT\",\"demo\":true,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":159,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Data is at the heart of AI-driven personalization. After this lesson, you'll be able to explore how data collection and analysis contribute to creating effective learning environments.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":5301880,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"Ever felt like a learning environment was designed just for you,\\nhitting all the right notes and challenging you in just the right ways?\\nThis isn't a happy accident.\\nIt's the result of data-driven magic happening behind the scenes.\\nI'm here to explain how collecting and analyzing\\ndata is key to creating AI-driven, personalized learning environments,\\nhelping you use data to improve your team's learning experiences.\\nThe foundation of personalization is data collection.\\n\\nIt's all about collecting data on learner\\ninteractions, preferences, and performance in various settings.\\nThis data is gathered from tools that track interactions such as quiz responses,\\ntime spent on courses, and preferred learning formats.\\nTools like your learning management system, assessments,\\nfeedback forms, and other engagement tools are great for this.\\nThis is where you start building a foundation for personalization\\nby understanding what your learners uniquely want.\\n\\nMoving\\nThis is where the magic happens.\\nIt involves taking all the data you've gathered about your learners,\\nand letting AI and machine learning algorithms sift through it.\\nThey're like detectives spotting patterns, pinpointing strengths and opportunities\\nwhile getting a sense of what each learner leans towards.\\nThe results? Actionable insights that help tailor learning paths and content\\nfor each learner.\\n\\nLeveraging an AI-powered analytics tool can ensure\\nyour learning strategies are effective\\nwith meeting the diverse needs of your learners.\\nAnd the final piece of this process is continuous improvement through feedback\\nloops.\\nRegular conversations with your learners about their experiences are essential.\\nSo set up ways to hear directly from them through regular feedback sessions\\nand surveys.\\nI'd suggest monthly feedback sessions,\\nbut feel free to tweak this based on your project timelines,\\nteam size, and what you aim to achieve with the feedback.\\n\\nSo keep asking, listening, and tweaking,\\nmaking sure every learning experience gets better and feels more personal\\nwith each update.\\nWith these insights,\\nstart integrating data collection and analysis into your learning programs.\\nBegin with a single course or program and observe how the data-driven\\nadjustments can transform the learning experience.\\nI'm excited about the tailored and engaging learning experiences you'll unlock.\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4261533\",\"duration\":158,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Ethics and privacy in AI-powered learning\",\"fileName\":\"3884342_en_US_01_03_VT\",\"demo\":true,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":158,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Ethical considerations are paramount. After this lesson, you'll be able to navigate the ethical and privacy concerns associated with using AI in learning and development.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":5971170,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"In the rush to embrace AI's potential, it's crucial\\nnot to overlook the ethical and privacy concerns that come with it.\\nHere are some ways for you to ethically navigate\\nthe use of AI in learning and development.\\nThe first ethical practice is to ensure your AI\\ntools, honor your employees privacy and data rights.\\nThese tools must be transparent and allow learners\\nto consent to how their data is being used.\\nTo do this review data privacy clauses in your AI\\nvendor contracts with your legal department, and have your I.T.\\n\\nsecurity team check that these privacy measures are followed.\\nNext, look for any spots where privacy or ethical issues might pop up.\\nThen put those safeguards with your I.T. security team.\\nFor example, if your platform uses AI to track progress,\\nit should anonymize personal data and clarify data usage policies.\\nThis ensures ground rules are set for a game where everyone feels safe to play.\\n\\nThe second\\nethical practice is to manage the collective data with the utmost care,\\nadhering to data protection standards like the European Union's\\nGeneral Data Protection\\nRegulation, which mandates transparency and control over personal data.\\nUS regulations may vary by sector or state, but aim to meet or exceed\\nsuch standards in your practices,\\nensuring your learners understand how their data is protected.\\n\\nThe final ethical practice in using AI\\nto deliver personalized learning experiences\\nis to ensure data is handled transparently and with consent.\\nEmpower your learners to control their personalization level\\nand the data they share, keeping them in charge of their learning journey.\\nYou can do this by providing options for learners to view, control and manage\\ntheir personal data.\\nThis can involve using a platform that allows learners\\nto adjust their personalization settings.\\n\\nNow that you know the ins and outs of handling\\nAI and data privacy the right way in learning spaces,\\nwhy not give your current methods a little checkup and a boost?\\nBy implementing these ethical practices\\nyou'll quickly see your learning experiences\\nspark more engagement built on trust.\\nDoing things ethically isn't just about ticking the boxes, it\u2019s the foundation\\nof a learning environment that's both powerful and respectful.\\n\"}],\"name\":\"1. Exploring AI in Learning\",\"size\":17816916,\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentChapter:4267351\"},{\"duration\":677,\"entries\":[{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4267350\",\"duration\":159,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Personalize learning with AI\",\"fileName\":\"3884342_en_US_02_01_VT\",\"demo\":true,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":160,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Personalization is key to effective learning. After this lesson, you'll be able to apply AI-driven personalization techniques to enhance skill development.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":5191395,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"Navigating the world of learning can sometimes\\nmake people feel like just another face in the crowd.\\nBut thanks to AI, you're now able to craft learning\\nexperience sources that truly resonate with each individual in your organization.\\nHere are some ways I harness AI\\nto turbocharge skill development to match each team\\nmembers learning pace and needs. To start understanding each person's learning\\nstyle is key. With AI\\ntools, you can track how your team interacts\\nwith materials and pinpoint their learning sweet spots.\\n\\nFor example,\\nmost modern learning management systems provide insights on user engagement,\\nhelping you tweak content to better suit various learning preferences.\\nBut how do you really dive into these individual needs?\\nBy diving into the data your AI\\ndriven platform offers on content preferences, engagement patterns\\nand completions rates and feedback\\nyou can uncover invaluable insights into what makes each learner tick.\\nMoving on to dynamic content adaptation, this is where AI really shines\\nwith its knack for tweaking, learning content and paths on the fly,\\nall based on how learners are doing and what they're saying.\\n\\nSo what can you do to bring this to life?\\nDive into your\\nAI-powered learning platform and explore adaptive learning features.\\nGetting familiar with these capabilities\\nallows you to customize content and learning paths\\nthat adapt to your learners progress and needs.\\nConsider a learner breezing through quizzes.\\nAI can up the ante by introducing more advanced materials,\\nkeeping them engaged and on their toes.\\nFinally, equip your organization with AI enhanced assessment tools.\\n\\nThink of them as your digital coaching\\nsidekick, offering feedback to your personalized learning experiences.\\nThese advanced grading tools can suggest\\nspecific topics and skills for your team to improve or explore further.\\nFor example, if your team struggles with risk management\\nin a project management course, AI\\ncan identify this trend and recommend specific materials\\nto improve their understanding and boost their confidence.\\nNow that you know how to enhance your team's\\nlearning with personalized experiences, check\\nif your current learning management system includes these features.\\n\\nIf not, ask your vendor about their roadmap to prepare for AI\\npersonalization opportunities.\\nI guarantee you this will be a game changer for you,\\nyour learners, and your organization.\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4261534\",\"duration\":157,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Implement adaptive learning systems with AI\",\"fileName\":\"3884342_en_US_02_02_VT\",\"demo\":true,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":158,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Adaptive learning systems tailor content to the learner. After this lesson, you'll be able to implement adaptive learning technologies to meet individual learning needs.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":5267663,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"Ever pictured a learning experience that seems to\\njust get you adapting as you progress through topics or encounter a bump?\\nWelcome to the world of AI-driven adaptive learning systems.\\nToday, I'm going to walk you through how adaptive\\nlearning systems use AI to tailor content specifically for your learner.\\nAt its core, adaptive\\nlearning systems are all about using AI to really get a sense of how you're doing,\\nhow you interact with content, how you're performing, and even what you like.\\n\\nIt then takes all that information, and tailors\\nare learning experience in real time.\\nAt the heart of adaptive systems, AI functions\\nlike a personal guide interpreting your learning habits\\nto customize your learning path.\\nIt makes learning seem uniquely designed just for you.\\nLean into AI driven analytics.\\nLet it be your guide to continuously sculpt learning experiences that resonate\\nusing both the big picture and the fine details drawn from various data points.\\n\\nSo how can you bring this into your learning space?\\nExplore integrating an adaptive learning feature\\nto your learning management system.\\nOne tool I would recommend\\n \\nshowcasing a variety of features from assessments to gamification,\\ndesigned to improve knowledge retention.\\nAnother great feature of\\nadaptive learning systems is its ability to help break through learning plateaus.\\nThese systems act like coaches identifying\\nplateaus and introducing new concepts to reignite your learning journey.\\n\\nEncourage your learners to engage\\nwith these systems, using the information presented to them\\nto enhance their strengths and support areas for development.\\nFinally, let's talk about engagement through interactivity.\\nAdaptive learning isn't just about content customization,\\nit's also about engaging presentation.\\nIncorporating interactive elements like simulations and games\\ncan dramatically lift engagement levels, making learning both fun and effective.\\n\\nCollaborate with content creators\\nto weave in interactive features into adaptive learning paths.\\nNow that you're familiar with adaptive learning\\nsystems, it's time to ignite the spark of change.\\nRemember, the journey of personalized learning is ongoing\\nand with AI, you have the compass\\nto guide your learners to new heights of learning excellence.\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4262490\",\"duration\":185,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Explore generative AI learning experiences\",\"fileName\":\"3884342_en_US_02_03_VT\",\"demo\":true,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":186,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Creating custom experiences has never been faster, thanks to generative AI. After this lesson, you'll be able to use generative AI to create personalized experiences to facilitate rapid development of learning.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":6540132,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"According to Gartner, one of the top five priorities for HR\\nleaders is generative AI.\\nThis means use of generated AI\\nwill be a strategic focus for building a skilled workforce.\\nIn today's world, creating learning experiences takes time,\\nresources and planning.\\nBut by embracing the potential of generative AI\\nor gen AI, organizations can simplify this process with speed.\\n\\nIn this lesson, I'll show you how generative AI\\nis reshaping the creation of personalized learning content.\\nYou'll see how to use this innovative tech\\nto speed up the production delivery of customized learning materials.\\nGenerative AI\\ncan generate all sorts of content from text to voice or text to images\\nby learning from vast amounts of data. Envision using a tool that\\nwith a few keywords, instantly creates e-learnings or promotional videos.\\n\\nPreviously, these tasks took hours.\\nNow AI reduces it to minutes saving time and money.\\nWhen you think about rapid content development, this is where Gen AI\\ntruly excels, allowing quick creation of diverse learning materials.\\nIt shortens the time from concept\\nto classroom, letting you swiftly respond to new learning demands or trends.\\nSo how can you leverage this?\\nUse gen AI for fast development of various learning resources,\\nfrom in-depth notes to interactive scenarios,\\nsimplifying content creation.\\n\\nOne of my favorite tools is Well Said, where you can use a learning script\\nto create a voiceover for an e-learning course in minutes.\\nAnother great learning platform in this space is Sana,\\nwhich lets you quickly create engaging learning courses from a PDF\\nsaving time and enhancing the learning experience.\\nNow let's talk about using\\ngen AI to predict skills gaps for just-in-time learning needs.\\nMost often, organizations identify skill strains and gaps during mid-year\\nor annual performance reviews.\\n\\nHowever, a Forbes article suggests that gen AI can analyze performance data\\ncontinuously.\\nThis allows learning teams to proactively develop\\nlearning experiences that address emerging skills.\\nIf your organization regularly gathers skills data using AI,\\nyou can analyze it against your current curriculum\\nthroughout the year to determine if adjustments are needed\\nto better meet your workforce needs.\\nIn this lesson, I've just touched the surface of the potential of using gen AI.\\n\\nKeep exploring opportunities for your organization.\\nStart with rapid content creation and experiment\\nwith available tools to streamline the process\\nwhile enhancing personalized learning experiences.\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4267349\",\"duration\":176,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Create interactive experiences with AI\",\"fileName\":\"3884342_en_US_02_04_VT\",\"demo\":true,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":177,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Immersive technologies offer new ways to learn. After this lesson, you'll be able to leverage AR and VR technologies and gamification to create engaging and effective learning experiences.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":5995547,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"Tired of the same\\nold learning methods that don't quite fit your modern and dynamic world?\\nPicture stepping into a learning journey\\nwhere you're actively shaping an interactive universe.\\nThis is the new wave of immersive learning with AI, where augmented reality,\\nvirtual reality, and gamification\\naren't just buzzwords, but gateways to absorbing knowledge like never before.\\nLet's dive into this landscape together.\\n\\nI'll show you how to harness AR and VR, spiced up with gamification, to craft\\nlearning experiences that captivate your learners.\\nFirst off, AI-enhanced augmented reality.\\nThis is where AR overlays digital details onto your real world view.\\nBut add AI to the mix and it gets a whole lot smarter,\\nrecognizing your surroundings and serving up relevant info on the spot.\\nTo bring this to life,\\nthink of a corporate setting where AR enhances meetings\\nby projecting remote participants as images into a physical room,\\nfostering presence and collaboration.\\n\\nSimultaneously, AI integration intelligently customizes\\ndisplayed information to suit interactions.\\nNext, there's AI-powered virtual reality simulation\\nthat transport you to a digital realm.\\nBut with AI, it transforms into an interactive, evolving world\\ntailored to your learning path.\\nPicture a VR experience where your interactions\\nshape an environment, providing custom challenges and feedback.\\nThink about a corporate leadership training.\\n\\nVR, augmented by AI, can offer immersive simulations for honing in skills\\nlike communication and team management\\nthrough personalized, dynamic scenarios and feedback,\\nfostering effective learning.\\nLast up, gamification with AI.\\nImagine turning learning into a fun game with a story that's all about you.\\nIt watches how you play, learns\\nwhat you like, and changes the game to keep you hooked\\nand learning in a way that's just right for you.\\nConsider using AI-driven gamification for new hires, where it adapts missions\\nto new hires as roles and learning styles, seamlessly weaving them into a team\\nand acquainting them with the company culture.\\n\\nSome of my favorite vendors to explore with AR,\\nVR, and gamification in the learning space are ELB Learning and Strivr.\\nI've also included a list of other vendors you can explore in your resource file.\\nWith these insights, you're ready to embark on creating\\nimmersive, AI-enhanced learning experiences\\nthat make learning not just interactive, but truly impactful.\\nDive in, explore the possibilities, and watch learning transform into an adventure\\nthat everyone wants to be a part of.\\n\\n\"}],\"name\":\"2. Designing AI-Powered Learning Experiences\",\"size\":22994737,\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentChapter:4272118\"},{\"duration\":502,\"entries\":[{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4261532\",\"duration\":179,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Build an AI-ready learning culture\",\"fileName\":\"3884342_en_US_03_01_VT\",\"demo\":true,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":179,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"A receptive culture is crucial for AI integration. After this lesson, you'll be able to foster a culture that embraces AI-driven learning initiatives.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":5309746,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"Organizations leading in innovation attribute their success\\nto a culture that values constant growth and flexibility.\\nThis culture creates a learning environment\\nthat transforms new possibilities into realities.\\nI'll guide you through an approach to cultivate a culture\\nthat embraces AI while fostering a spirit for innovation.\\nStart by promoting AI awareness across the organization.\\nProvide a forum where everyone in your organization learns the basics\\nof AI through a variety of trainings and resources.\\n\\nUnderstanding AI can help everyone feel more comfortable using new AI tools,\\nand less worried about trying new technologies.\\nYou might want to set up workshops, resources they can use any time,\\nor talk to the AI experts to show how I can be really useful.\\nNext, think about the different jobs\\nin your organization that might need special AI training.\\nFor example,\\nyour leaders might need training on how to discuss AI with clients or their teams.\\n\\nYour technical staff\\nmay need deeper training to figure out how to use AI in your organization.\\nIt's important to tailor the AI training to fit the specific needs of each role,\\nso everyone can use AI effectively in their job.\\nAlso, encourage experimentation with AI tools.\\nAllow team members to experiment with selected AI tools\\nand share their feedback.\\nCreate a sandbox environment where they can safely explore\\nthese tools and provide honest feedback through structured channels.\\n\\nThis approach helps everyone feel included as they learn more about AI.\\nIt also ensures selected AI tools are effective for everyone's needs and fosters\\na supportive learning community within their organization.\\nFinally, it's important to match your AI learning efforts with your organization's\\nbroader goals to help improve them performance and foster innovation.\\nBy showing how AI learning supports\\nboth the organization's success and personal development.\\n\\nYou encourage a deeper commitment to these initiatives.\\nTo bring this to life,\\ncollaborate\\nwith various departments to pinpoint areas where I can make a significant impact.\\nEstablish clear,\\nmeasurable objectives for AI learning programs, and maintain open communication\\nabout these goals across the organization.\\nNow that I've gone over some steps\\nto create an AI learning culture, here's a quick tip on getting started quickly.\\n\\nCheck out the AI learning materials that already exist.\\nThere are many resources that have already been published\\nacross multiple content libraries.\\nYou can customize these to upskill your organization.\\nGo search for an existing resource for your type of business today.\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4266357\",\"duration\":155,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Strategies for AI implementation in learning\",\"fileName\":\"3884342_en_US_03_02_VT\",\"demo\":true,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":156,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Effective implementation requires strategic planning. After this lesson, you'll be able to outline strategies for integrating AI technologies into your learning and development programs.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":5010734,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"Integrating AI into learning programs can be like navigating unchartered waters,\\nripe with both opportunities and challenges.\\nI'll share some important strategies to incorporate AI into your programs,\\neffectively aiming to improve outcomes and the learning experience.\\nFirst,\\nset clear goals of how you want\\nAI to improve your learning and development programs.\\nThen think about how AI can help reach those goals.\\nFor example, do you want\\nAI to personalize learning, identify skill gaps, or create content quickly?\\nLook at your current processes, data and technology to see where AI can fit in.\\n\\nNext, decide which AI projects to focus on first by considering their impact\\non the organization, how doable they are, and what resources they need.\\nStart with the ones that are easier to do or will make the biggest difference,\\nlike personalized content or virtual coaching helpers. Plan out\\nhow you will roll out these projects step by step in a phased approach.\\nAfter that, ensure your organization's data and technology are prepared\\nand ready.\\n\\nMake sure your data is good, secure, and has a governance framework in place\\nbefore using it to teach AI.\\nCheck your tech stack with your IT department\\nto see if it can handle AI, and set up tools that fit what you want to do.\\nAnd don't forget to train or hire people who know about\\nAI to help out in your learning and development teams.\\nNext, concentrate on setting up change management\\nstrategies and addressing ethical concerns.\\nCreate a change management plan to help\\nthe organization get ready for AI and deal with any concerns or pushbacks.\\n\\nAlso, set rules for using AI ethically and safely.\\nAnd most importantly, work together across teams and get everyone's support\\nfor AI to work well.\\nLastly, keep track of how well AI is doing.\\nListen to what people think and see how it's helping the business.\\nMake AI better over time\\nusing what you learn\\nand keep trying new things and learning from mistakes to stay ahead.\\nWith this roadmap\\nkeep in mind that this AI journey goes beyond just adopting new technology.\\n\\nIt's about planning for meaningful\\nlearning experiences with AI through a thoughtful and strategic approach.\\nUse these steps to start making your organization\u2019s plan.\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4261531\",\"duration\":168,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Overcome challenges in AI adoption\",\"fileName\":\"3884342_en_US_03_03_VT\",\"demo\":true,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":169,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Adoption challenges are inevitable. After this lesson, you'll be able to identify and overcome common barriers to adopting AI in learning and development.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":5705226,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"One of the most common fears I hear all the time is \u201cAI is going to take my job.\u201d\\nWhich can cause all sorts of feelings as people.\\nIn this lesson, I'll guide you through identifying\\nand removing the common barriers to adopting AI\\nin your learning and development initiatives.\\nResistance to change is natural, particularly with new tech like AI,\\noften leading to skepticism or misunderstanding among stakeholders.\\nOvercoming this requires clear communication, educating stakeholders,\\nand involving them in your AI journey,\\nmaking them active participants in the change.\\n\\nA first practical step to ease AI adoption concerns is to organize\\ninformational sessions, showcasing AI's benefits\\nin the organization, with success stories and direct responses to concerns.\\nTechnical hurdles, such as data privacy issues, integration\\nchallenges, and infrastructure limitations also pose significant barriers.\\nCollaborating with your IT team is crucial here.\\nTogether, you can enhance data protection,\\nselect compatible AI tools, and possibly upgrade your infrastructure.\\n\\nStart with a thorough technical audit to check your data practices\\nto see how new AI tools fit with what you've got,\\nand make sure your tech foundation is AI ready.\\nThen develop a focused plan prioritizing data security with your\\nAI integration approach.\\nAdditionally, consider your team's skills gaps as a potential barrier.\\nUtilizing AI effectively requires skills in data analysis, machine learning,\\nand AI literacy that your team may lack.\\n\\nClosing the skill gap means implementing\\ntargeted training or bringing in AI specialists for a smoother transition.\\nPinpoint the essential AI skills for your team and arrange specialized trainings\\nor workshops, or recruit external AI experts for immediate needs.\\nYou can organize these trainings with external providers\\nwho specialize in AI,\\nhelping your team develop skills that aren't available in-house.\\nThis introduction to overcoming AI adoption\\nchallenges in learning is just the beginning.\\n\\nIt's about preparing for the future and seizing the vast opportunities\\nof AI and learning,\\nrecognizing that everyone is at different stages of AI adoption.\\nNow that you're ready to transform AI option challenges\\ninto opportunities, encourage your team to be curious.\\nThere are plenty of external resources available online to support them wherever\\nthey are in their AI journey.\\n\"}],\"name\":\"3. Implementing AI in Your Learning Strategy\",\"size\":16025706,\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentChapter:4262492\"},{\"duration\":339,\"entries\":[{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4270158\",\"duration\":167,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Analyze learning outcomes\",\"fileName\":\"3884342_en_US_04_01_VT\",\"demo\":true,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":167,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Analytics play a crucial role in measuring success. After this lesson, you'll be able to use learning analytics to evaluate the effectiveness of AI-powered personalization.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":5257811,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"Do you ever wonder if your learning experiences really connect\\nwith each learner?\\nIn today's digital world, the key to measuring success\\nis by using learning analytics.\\nLet me walk you through some ways to leverage learning\\nanalytics to measure the return of investment in\\nAI powered personalization in learning programs.\\nBefore you dive into  AI-powered personalization,\\nmake sure you know where you're starting from by setting up baseline metrics.\\n\\nThese could be things like how many learners finish courses,\\nhow well they do on tasks, how much time they spent learning\\nand how they're doing in their jobs.\\nBy defining these metrics, you can start to track improvements\\nin learning experiences with AI-powered personalization.\\nAnd don't forget to capture your training course from the get go.\\nThis includes everything from creating content to facilitation,\\nas well as the time spent managing administrative\\ntasks like keeping up with compliance requirements.\\n\\nNext, start tracking engagement and learner performance.\\nKeep an eye on how engaged\\nlearners are like, How many are actively using learning materials?\\nHow are they using them? And if they're dropping\\nout of more personalized versus not personalized paths.\\nAlso, look at assessment results and skill levels\\nto see how personalized learning is helping people\\nremember what they've learned and develop their skills.\\nFortunately, most of this data can be found and tracked\\nin existing learning management systems or other integrated tools.\\n\\nA simple approach I recommend exporting your learning data into an AI tool like\\nChatGPT or Microsoft Copilot to summarize trends and assess your progress.\\nJust ensure your organization approves using these tools first\\nbefore you dive in.\\nAfter that,\\nconnect your learning data with key organizational metrics\\nlike productivity or client satisfaction scores\\nto measure the impact of improved skills on the organization.\\n\\nAnd lastly, don't forget to capture any cost savings data.\\nFor example,\\nyou could be measuring the time and money saved by automating tasks\\nlike organizing and delivering content and handling administrative tasks using AI.\\nI encourage you to dive into your learning analytics.\\nStart small, perhaps with a particular program,\\nand let the data refine and amplify your AI\\npersonalization efforts.\\nRemember the true strength of AI lies not just in the tech itself,\\nbut in how its data continuously improves learning and organizational skills.\\n\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4273007\",\"duration\":172,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Predict AI-powered learning trends\",\"fileName\":\"3884342_en_US_04_02_VT\",\"demo\":true,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":172,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"The future holds more innovation. After this lesson, you'll be able to predict future trends in AI-powered learning and prepare for ongoing changes in the organizational learning landscape.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":5483771,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"Picture yourself at the brink of an expansive sea, each wave symbolizing\\nthe relentless advancements in AI, reshaping how the workforce learns.\\nWill you dive into the next wave, or merely observe from afar?\\nI'm here to discuss AI driven learning trends and offer\\ninsights to help you adapt to future changes in organizational learning.\\nLet's start off with AI coaching at your service.\\nEssentially, AI coaching is evolving beyond basic chat bots\\nto sophisticated systems offering real time, personalized support.\\n\\nThey'll clarify concepts,\\nprovide additional resources, and answer questions on the spot,\\nmaking coaching seamless, timely, and enriching the learning experience.\\nIt's like having a coach in your pocket ready to assist anytime, anywhere.\\nAnother trend is next level personalization.\\nWhile you're\\nalready seeing personalization with AI, the surface is barely being scratched.\\nFuture AI will focus on highly customized learning paths that adapt to individual\\nneeds, preferences, and speeds, making content perpetually relevant\\nand captivating.\\n\\nIn this course, I shared how personalization can enhance learning.\\nImagine this concept intensified to a level where every learner feels\\nthat a learning journey was uniquely designed just for them.\\nAnd last up,\\nthe final trend is learning analytics being supercharged by AI.\\nThis is where AI will continuously track all aspects of learner engagement\\nthat go beyond your traditional assessments and evaluations.\\n\\nI believe that you'll be able to leverage dynamic\\nAI algorithms to monitor every single interaction\\nyour learners have, from validating whether individual skill\\ndevelopment supported your organization's growth,\\nto capturing your learners\u2019 emotional responses during a learning experience.\\nWhat I love about this trend is that will enable you\\nto provide critical data of leadership discussions,\\ndemonstrating how learning is crucial for building a skilled workforce.\\nAs the AI landscape continues to evolve, new trends may emerge even as you're\\nexploring this topic.\\n\\nKeep your finger on the pulse of AI advancements\\nthrough publications, blogs, and thought leaders.\\nI recommend tapping into the e-learning industry,\\nthe Josh Bersin Academy, or Learning Solutions by the Learning Guild.\\nWhile it's not imperative to chase every new trend, being in the know is key.\\nThe next groundbreaking\\nidea might just address a challenge you're facing or unveil new prospects.\\n\"}],\"name\":\"4. Measuring Success and Impact\",\"size\":10741582,\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentChapter:4259532\"},{\"duration\":98,\"entries\":[{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4272116\",\"duration\":98,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Integrate AI into the future of workforce learning\",\"fileName\":\"3884342_en_US_05_01_VT\",\"demo\":true,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":99,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Congratulations on completing this course! Now, you're able to develop a roadmap for continuously incorporating AI technologies into your organization's learning strategy, ensuring relevance and effectiveness in skill development for the future workforce.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":4538141,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"Congratulations! You made it to the end of the course.\\nI hope you're excited to have new tools\\nto help your organization embrace a learning culture that thrives with AI.\\nThroughout this course you gained\\nvaluable insights that will empower you to use AI to tailor learning experiences\\ncatering to the unique needs and skills of your employees.\\nThis will enhance adaptability and agility in addressing the ever changing,\\nevolving demands of your business landscape.\\n\\nEmbracing AI will require time, patience, and testing.\\nMy advice is to attentively\\nlisten to your organizational needs and align your AI strategies accordingly.\\nEnriching your learning culture.\\nStay curious, open,\\nand responsible about the possibilities AI offers for advancing learning.\\nTo keep the curiosity alive,\\nI've included some vendors in your resource file\\nwho use AI to improve learning experiences.\\n\\nExploring new tools is a great way to envision the art of the possible.\\nEven if you choose not to adopt them immediately.\\nIf you're ever eager to dive deeper into AI learning tools or want to discuss more,\\nfeel free to reach out to me on LinkedIn.\\nAlso, consider exploring my other courses.\\nThank you for joining me on this exploration of AI\u2019s\\nimpact on learning.\\nHere's to a future where every strategy\\nand experience you implement changes lives and organizations daily.\\n\\n\"}],\"name\":\"Conclusion\",\"size\":4538141,\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentChapter:4273009\"}],\"size\":75249957,\"duration\":2184,\"zeroBased\":false},{\"course_title\":\"AI-Powered Career Development: Aligning Employee Growth with Business Strategy\",\"course_admin_id\":2032288,\"metadata\":{\"Locale\":\"en_US\",\"Course ID\":2032288,\"Project ID\":null,\"Course Name\":\"AI-Powered Career Development: Aligning Employee Growth with Business Strategy\",\"Course Name EN\":\"AI-Powered Career Development: Aligning Employee Growth with Business Strategy\",\"Activation Status\":\"ACTIVE\",\"Display to Public\":\"No\",\"Display to QA\":\"Yes\",\"Course Description\":\"Career development begins with a skills and personality assessment. Then it\u2019s a balancing act between what that employee wants in their career, and what the employer needs from them. The sweet spot is when you can be on the same page about those two considerations\u2014but what\u2019s the secret? In this course, instructor Don Phin shows you how to leverage the power of AI to align employee growth with business needs. Learn how to create supportive career paths with training, coaching, goal setting, and structured pathways. By the end of this course, you\u2019ll be equipped with the skills you need to enhance employee career development, engagement, retention, and business growth.\",\"Course Short Description\":\"Help HR managers establish structured career development programs that align employee aspirations with company needs.\",\"Content Type\":\"SKILLS\",\"Localization Type\":\"ORIGINAL\",\"Original Course Locale\":null,\"Original Course ID\":null,\"Equivalent English Course\":null,\"Instructor ID\":\"8857475\",\"Instructor Name\":\"Don Phin\",\"Instructor Transliterated Name\":null,\"Instructor Short Bio\":\"Speaker, Trainer, Coach, and Author\",\"Author Payment Category\":\"NON-LICENSED\",\"Delivery Mode\":\"ALL_AT_ONCE\",\"Series End Date\":null,\"Course Release Date\":null,\"Course Updated Date\":null,\"Course Archive Date\":null,\"Course Retire Date\":null,\"Replacement Course\":null,\"Has Assessment\":\"Yes\",\"Has Challenge/Solution\":\"Yes\",\"LIL URL\":\"https://www.linkedin.com/learning/building-career-development-programs-with-ai-aligning-employee-growth-with-business-needs,https://www.linkedin.com/learning/building-career-development-programs-with-ai-aligning-employee-growth-with-business-needs-text-role-play,https://www.linkedin.com/learning/ai-powered-talent-development-aligning-human-potential-with-business-strategy\",\"Series\":\"Learning\",\"Limited Series\":null,\"Manager Level\":\"Manager\",\"LI Level\":\"Beginner + Intermediate\",\"LI Level EN\":\"Beginner + Intermediate\",\"Sensitivity\":null,\"Internal Library\":\"Business\",\"Internal Subject\":\"HR\",\"Primary Software\":null,\"Media Type\":\"Video, Text\",\"Has CEU\":\"No\",\"Has Exercise Files\":\"Yes\",\"Visible Duration\":3352.0,\"Visible Video Count\":16.0,\"Learning Objectives\":\"Assess employee strengths, personality traits, and skill gaps using structured evaluations. ,Align employees\u2019 career goals with organizational objectives by facilitating meaningful career discussions and identifying future talent needs. ,Design clear career road maps that outline structured pathways for employee growth.,Build effective training, coaching, and mentorship programs to support employee career growth.\",\"Contract Type\":\"PERPETUAL\",\"Certifications\":null,\"Framework Topic\":\"Level 2: Applying, AI Upskilling Framework, AI Upskilling Framework Level 2: Applying, AI Framework Level 2: Applying\",\"Automatic Caption Translations\":null,\"Automatic Metadata Translations\":null,\"Gen AI Feature Flag\":null,\"Hands-On Practice\":null,\"Hands-On Practice Library\":null,\"Unlocked for Viva Learning\":null,\"Free Course\":null,\"Certification Library\":null,\"Github Codespace\":null,\"Skills Count\":5,\"Skills\":\"AI for Career Development,Career Development,Employee Learning & Development,HR Management,Talent Development\",\"Skills EN\":\"AI for Career Development,Career Development,Employee Learning & Development,HR Management,Talent Development\",\"Content Manager\":\"Rafranz Davis\",\"Acquisition Manager\":\"Rafranz Davis\",\"Framework Subject\":\"AI Upskilling Framework, AI Framework Level 2: Applying\",\"Suppress Upsells\":null},\"sections\":[{\"duration\":60,\"entries\":[{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4110020\",\"duration\":60,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":null,\"name\":\"Why career development matters\",\"fileName\":\"2032288_en_US_00_01_VT\",\"demo\":true,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":424,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"editingNotes\":\"Take 1 with 3 reads; use the 3re read -- it has a rollback for one word where Don got the name of the workplace report wrong (the first time he read it)\",\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Career development has become a necessity, but it's a challenge for both the employer and employee alike. This course is designed to help you use AI to create an effective career development program.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":3650297,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":true,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- Career development used to be a nice to have;\\ntoday it's a must have.\\nYour best employees want to know they're not just filling\\na role, they're building a future.\\nGallup's annual State of the Global Workforce reports\\nthat employees who have frequent development conversations\\nare almost three times more likely to be engaged.\\nWelcome, my name is Don Phin.\\nIn this course, I'll show you how\\nyou can help employees develop career goals and roadmaps.\\n\\nAlong the way, we'll discuss how AI can support you\\nand your employees on their career development journey.\\nAnd you're going to get a chance\\nto practice these career development conversations with AI.\\nWhen people see that their growth matters,\\nthey show up with better skills, more commitment,\\nand greater productivity,\\nand that's how everybody wins.\\nSo let's get this course started.\\n\"}],\"name\":\"Introduction\",\"size\":3650297,\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentChapter:2052065\"},{\"duration\":1024,\"entries\":[{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4103078\",\"duration\":284,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"The importance of career development\",\"fileName\":\"2032288_en_US_01_01_VT\",\"demo\":true,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":576,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"editingNotes\":\"Take 1 with rollbacks and an Insert Rollback\",\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Learn how career development programs align employee aspirations with business needs. Structured career growth improves engagement, retention, and company success.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":16655275,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- What makes employees stay?\\nWhat makes them go?\\nWhat makes you stay and what makes you want to go?\\nChances are there are some common themes.\\nWhile compensation always plays a role,\\ncareer development consistently ranks\\namong the top drivers of retention,\\nengagement and long-term performance.\\nWhen people perceive a clear path for growth\\nwithin your organization\\nand receive support to pursue it,\\nthey're more likely to stay\\nand contribute at higher levels.\\n\\nCareer development is more than just getting a promotion,\\nit encompasses learning new skills,\\nexposure to new roles or teams,\\nmentorship opportunities,\\nand aligning work with purpose.\\nMost employees seek a sense of progression,\\nnot just title changes.\\nFrom a business perspective,\\nthe benefits are evident.\\nLinkedIn's 2023 Workplace Learning Report\\nindicates learning and development professionals\\nbelieve proactively building employee skills\\nwill help manage the future of work.\\n\\nAnd as mentioned,\\nemployees who perceive\\nstrong career development opportunities\\nare almost three times more likely\\nto be engaged at work.\\nDespite these advantages,\\nmany organizations falter\\nin the execution of career development.\\nAt many companies,\\ncareer conversations often occur annually, if at all,\\nand development plans are neglected.\\nMany times this happens because managers\\nlack the time, training or tools\\nto provide meaningful guidance.\\n\\nIf you work at this type of company\\nand are not able to influence the decision makers\\nin that space,\\nthen you can focus on what Stephen Covey\\ncalled your, \\\"Circle of influence,\\\"\\nand see how you can help the people you manage\\nimprove their career development.\\nAnd as I'll continue to mention,\\nAI will be your best friend\\nin helping you to do just that.\\nFor example, talent platforms like Gloat,\\nSkyHive and LinkedIn Learning Hub\\nuse AI to map skills,\\nsuggest internal roles,\\nand recommend learning paths\\ntailored to each employee.\\n\\nEmployees no longer have to wait for somebody\\nto tap them on the shoulder.\\nThese tools help them to explore career paths,\\nidentify capability gaps,\\nand assess mentors or stretch assignments.\\nThe result, growth becomes a self-driven opportunity.\\nLeading companies are setting new standards.\\nFor example, AT&T's Future Ready Initiative\\noffers AI-based skills assessments,\\ncurated learning paths,\\nand transparent career planning.\\n\\nThe program has reskilled over 70,000 employees,\\nreducing external hiring needs\\nand enhancing internal mobility.\\nImportantly, such investments aren't exclusive\\nto large enterprises.\\nSmaller organizations leverage tools like ChatGPT\\nto assist employees in mapping career options,\\nidentifying skill gaps,\\nand exploring new paths through natural language prompts.\\n\\nThis democratizes development,\\nmaking it accessible\\neven without extensive HR infrastructures.\\nIntegrating AI into career development strategies\\noffers scalable personalized growth experiences.\\nAI-driven platforms can assess individual skills,\\nconsider personality assessments,\\nlike DISC and Maya Briggs,\\nrecommend tailored learning opportunities\\nand predict future role assignments.\\n\\nThis not only empowers employees\\nto take charge of their growth,\\nbut also enables organizations\\nto proactively address skill gaps\\nand succession planning.\\nUltimately, fostering a culture\\nthat prioritizes continuous learning and development\\nbenefits both employees and that organization.\\nWhen growth becomes an integral part\\nof the workplace experience,\\nit cultivates loyalty, drives innovation,\\nand positions the company for sustained success.\\n\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4103077\",\"duration\":221,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Assessing where you are before planning where you're going\",\"fileName\":\"2032288_en_US_01_02_VT\",\"demo\":true,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":249,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"editingNotes\":\"Take 1 clean\",\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"After watching this video you will understand the importance of assessing where you are before you plan on where you're going. You will be able to identify what's not working that needs to be fixed and what's working that can be improved upon.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":11082968,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- Before you can plan on where you're going,\\nyou need to understand where you are.\\nThat's the foundation\\nof any meaningful career development strategy,\\nboth for individuals and organizations.\\nIt's often a mistake to jump straight into solutions,\\nwhether they're tools, learning paths, mentoring programs,\\nwithout taking a proper inventory of the current situation.\\nFor individuals, this means reflecting on strengths,\\ninterests, motivations, and existing skill sets.\\n\\nFor companies, it means assessing workforce capabilities,\\norganizational needs, and the systems currently in place\\nto support development.\\nLet's start with the individual side.\\nSelf-assessment is a powerful tool.\\nIt helps employees clarify what they enjoy,\\nwhere they excel, and how they want to grow.\\nTools like CliftonStrengths, DiSC, TestGorilla,\\nand AI-based career insight platforms\\nnow enable deeper analysis by evaluating personality types,\\nskills, values, and role alignment.\\n\\nAt Cisco, employees participate\\nin personalized career conversations\\nsupported by AI-enabled digital tools,\\nincluding chatbots and internal skills mapping platforms,\\nwhich help to clarify goals\\nand employee readiness for new roles.\\nOrganizations, meanwhile, must ask themselves,\\nwhat developmental resources do we offer today?\\nAre they easy to find?\\nAre they being used?\\nAre managers equipped\\nto have quality development conversations?\\nDo we track skills, learning progress,\\nand role readiness, or just job titles?\\nThis kind of assessment doesn't require expensive systems.\\n\\nIt starts by asking questions like,\\ndo employees have visibility into internal opportunities?\\nAre there structured developmental pathways\\nor are career moves informal and ad hoc?\\nIs growth tracked, rewarded, and personalized,\\nor left to chance?\\nAI platforms now offer a sharper lens into these questions.\\nInternal tools like Gloat or Skyhive\\ncan analyze workforce-wide skills,\\nflag readiness for internal mobility,\\nand visualize development activity\\nby department, manager, or job family.\\n\\nSome even benchmark against market trends\\nto surface skills gaps and future needs.\\nFor example, MasterCard recently implemented\\nan internal skills intelligence platform\\nto assess career mobility\\nand align employee upskilling with strategic priorities.\\nTheir approach began with an audit of employee capabilities\\nand manager engagement with development,\\nmaking the AI rollout far more targeted and measurable.\\n\\nWhether you're leading a team or shaping HR policy,\\npausing to evaluate your starting point\\ncan unlock better planning.\\nIt reveals gaps, avoids wasted effort,\\nand amplifies the strengths already\\nworking in your culture.\\nAs ancient wisdom has it,\\nstart with diagnosis before prescription.\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4104061\",\"duration\":219,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Identifying critical roles and future talent needs\",\"fileName\":\"2032288_en_US_01_03_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":398,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"editingNotes\":\"Take 1 with rollbacks and an Insert Rollback\",\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Learn how to assess future talent needs and critical roles within your organization. Understanding workforce gaps helps managers proactively develop talent pipelines.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":12427652,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- Every organization has roles\\nthat are more critical than others.\\nNot because every employee isn't important,\\nbut because some roles create an outsized impact.\\nThese positions directly affect growth, operations,\\ncustomer experience, or innovation and if they go unfilled,\\nbusiness slows or even falters.\\nIdentifying these critical roles\\nis one of the most strategic things you can do\\nfor long-term success.\\n\\nThey could be technical experts, client facing leads,\\noperational linchpins, or cultural stewards,\\nbut too often companies don't realize\\nwhich roles are essential until they're vacant,\\nand then it's often too late.\\nHow do you identify critical roles and align them\\nwith future talent needs?\\nYou start by asking, if this role became vacant tomorrow,\\nwhat would the impact be?\\nThis forces a shift from focusing on hierarchy,\\nor job titles to evaluating actual business influence.\\n\\nNext, consider where your company's going.\\nStrategic growth requires workforce planning.\\nAre you entering new markets,\\nadopting new technologies? Scaling operations?\\nWhat capabilities will you need 12 to 36 months from now?\\nOrganizations like Nestle approaches proactively,\\nthey maintain live talent maps\\nthat connect business priorities to internal pipelines.\\n\\nThese maps track both critical roles,\\nand succession strength and are refreshed regularly\\nthrough their mobility and development programs.\\nAI is helping companies to go even further.\\nTools like Gloat and Visier use real-time data\\nto forecast future skill demand, flag at-risk roles,\\nand recommend internal successors based on experience,\\nperformance, and readiness.\\nThese platforms don't just highlight gaps,\\nthey suggest targeted learning paths\\nand development actions to close them.\\n\\nThey also provide analytics\\non which company teams have succession plans\\nand which don't.\\nAI can even simulate organizational changes.\\nWhat happens if you restructure, or scale or automate?\\nIf you hit with a recession, then what do you do?\\nThese tools help you to plan for the workforce\\nof the future, not just react to current needs.\\nBut identifying critical roles is only part of the equation.\\n\\nyou also need to evaluate who's ready\\nor could be with the right support.\\nThat's where development plans,\\ncoaching and stretch assignments come into play.\\nAsk yourself, which five roles, if left unfulfilled\\nwould create the greatest risk or opportunity\\nfor your business?\\nWho could step into these roles today?\\nWho might be ready because of the right career development?\\nNext up, you are going to have the opportunity\\nto practice identifying future talent needs\\nin career planning with the help of AI.\\n\\nThe fact is, when you align your career development program\\nwith your business strategy, you create a synergy\\nthat grows people and the company.\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:2051079\",\"duration\":0,\"visible\":false,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":null,\"name\":\"FAKE MOVIE Practice: Identifying future talent needs in career planning\",\"fileName\":\"2032288_en_US_01_04_FAKEVIDEO\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":300,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"editingNotes\":\"Role Play\",\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"After completing this role-play, you'll be able to analyze workforce trends and internal talent pipelines to proactively identify future leadership gaps. This is important for ensuring long-term business continuity and career growth opportunities for employees.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"NOT_AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"NOT_ATTEMPTED\",\"size\":0,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"NEW\",\"transcript\":null},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentArticle:357008\",\"duration\":300,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Practice Role Play: Explore career goals with a team member\"}],\"name\":\"1. Understanding the Big Picture of Career Development\",\"size\":40165895,\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentChapter:4103081\"},{\"duration\":999,\"entries\":[{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4109079\",\"duration\":214,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"The role of personality assessments\",\"fileName\":\"2032288_en_US_02_01_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":561,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"editingNotes\":\"Take 1 with rollbacks and a pickup (1a-1) for the close\",\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":true,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Learn how to use personality assessments to understand how employees work best. Recognizing individual work styles helps managers tailor development strategies that align with employees\u2019 strengths.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":11281795,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- What makes people tick?\\nWhat energizes them? What derails them under stress?\\nThese are the kind of questions.\\nPersonality assessments help us to explore.\\nWhen used thoughtfully,\\nthey can become powerful tools in career development,\\nboth for the individuals and organizations supporting them.\\nI've taken more than a dozen of these assessments,\\nand they've helped me to grow both\\npersonally and professionally.\\nI often use them when I train\\nand coach managers and leaders.\\n\\nPersonality assessments aren't new,\\ntools like DiSC, Hogan, and CliftonStrengths\\nhave been around for decades.\\nWhat's changed is how they're being used.\\nInstead of limiting them to hiring\\nor team building exercises.\\nMany organizations are integrating assessments into\\ncoaching, leadership development,\\nand long-term career planning.\\nThe value in an assessment comes from\\nunderstanding not labeling.\\n\\nThese assessments reveal how someone prefers to communicate,\\nprocess information, manage stress, and relate to others.\\nThat awareness leads to better career choices,\\nstronger teams, and more targeted support.\\nAt American Express Leadership Development programs use\\nHogan assessments\\nto help high potential employees identify\\nboth their strengths and their derailers.\\nParticipants work with trained coaches\\nto interpret the results,\\nwhich has helped increase internal mobility\\nand leadership readiness.\\n\\nThese tools also help managers lead more effectively.\\nOne team member might thrive\\nwith recognition while another values autonomy.\\nPersonality insights make coaching more relevant\\nand nuanced, but assessments do have limits.\\nThey shouldn't be used in isolation to make hiring\\nor promotional decisions.\\nIn fact, the EEOC says\\nthat anytime a tool like this is used in isolation\\nto make a significant employment decision,\\nit has to be validated according to strict criteria\\nso as to avoid a discriminatory impact.\\n\\nNew AI powered platforms are also emerging in this space.\\nFor example, plume uses machine learning\\nto build dynamic personality profiles\\nbased on workforce preferences and behavioral data.\\nIt then recommends roles\\nand development paths aligned to those profiles,\\nreducing bias and helping to match people to environments\\nwhere they're likely to thrive.\\nAI also enables more responsive,\\nscalable use of assessments.\\n\\nFor example, platforms like PeopleTransformation.ai,\\nTraitify or Humanic AI generate personality insights\\nin real time, enabling personalized learning\\nand growth experiences without waiting\\nfor formal evaluations.\\nIf you're just getting started, pick one validated tool,\\nintroduce it as a developmental resource, and offer coaching\\nor group debriefs to help people apply the insights.\\n\\nMany companies will provide you with a free assessment,\\nso try a few\\nand see which ones you think would work best\\nat your company.\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4106057\",\"duration\":0,\"visible\":false,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":null,\"name\":\"FAKE MOVIE Practice: Providing constructive feedback in a career assessment\",\"fileName\":\"2032288_en_US_02_02_FAKEVIDEO\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":300,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"editingNotes\":\"Role Play\",\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Complete this role-play to better evaluate assessment results and provide constructive career feedback that motivates employees to take action. This knowledge will help you understand your career potential and areas for growth.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"NOT_AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"NOT_ATTEMPTED\",\"size\":0,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"NEW\",\"transcript\":null},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentArticle:359008\",\"duration\":300,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Practice Role Play: Integrate AI tools into a career conversation\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:2051078\",\"duration\":216,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Skills testing for career development\",\"fileName\":\"2032288_en_US_02_03_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":430,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"editingNotes\":\"Take 1 with rollbacks\",\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Learn how to use skills testing to measure employee competencies and identify gaps. Understanding skill levels allows managers to provide targeted development opportunities.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":10632913,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- When it comes to career development,\\nassumptions can be dangerous.\\nWe assume somebody's ready for a new role\\nbecause they've been in their current role for a few years.\\nOr we assume someone lacks potential\\nbecause they're quiet in meetings.\\nBut without data,\\nwe're often just guessing,\\nand that's where skill testing comes in.\\nSkill testing gives you objective insight\\ninto what people can actually do,\\nnot just what their resume says\\nor how well they present in interviews.\\n\\nIt allows employees to better understand their growth areas\\nand helps organizations make smarter\\nand fairer decisions too.\\nHistorically, skill testing has been used primarily\\nduring hiring through coding challenges, writing examples,\\nindustry certifications or standardized tests,\\nbut its value extends far beyond hiring.\\nSkill testing now plays a central role in onboarding,\\nidentifying readiness for internal roles,\\ndesigning personalized learning plans,\\nand prioritizing company-wide upskilling efforts.\\n\\nTake PwC's digital fitness app as an example.\\nIt's an internal tool\\nthat assesses digital fluency across the organization.\\nEmployees complete a short diagnostic\\nand receive a personalized score\\nwith curated learning paths based on their results.\\nThis empowers individuals to take ownership of their growth\\nwhile helping PwC direct its re-skilling efforts\\nwhere they're needed most.\\n\\nModern skills testing is no longer about pass or fail,\\nit's about benchmarking where somebody is to today\\nand giving them the tools to grow.\\nWhen employees view it as developmental\\ninstead of judgemental,\\ntrust increases and engagement rises.\\nAI is dramatically enhancing the way skills are assessed.\\nAdaptive testing platforms adjust in real time\\nto user input.\\n\\nTools like Vervoe, Codility, and Filtered use AI\\nto simulate job-specific scenarios,\\ntrack cognitive and behavioral responses,\\nand provide instant feedback\\nthat supports career development.\\nAI is also being used\\nto analyze historical learning and work patterns\\nto predict how quickly somebody could pick up a new skill,\\nturning skill testing from a static snapshot\\ninto a dynamic forward-looking strategy.\\n\\nTransparency when using AI tools is critical.\\nEmployees should understand what's being measured,\\nhow it's used,\\nand how it benefits their development.\\nDone right,\\nskill testing becomes a growth catalyst, not a gatekeeper.\\nSo here's your challenge.\\nHave you clearly identified the critical skills\\nin your current or future role?\\nAnd are you measuring them in a meaningful way?\\nIf you want to dive into this topic further,\\ncheck out my course:\\nCreating a Skills-Based Organization,\\nbecause data beats guesswork.\\n\\nAnd when people know where they stand,\\nthey're far more likely to get where they want to go,\\nand that includes you.\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4107060\",\"duration\":269,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"AI's impact on skills and personality assessments\",\"fileName\":\"2032288_en_US_02_04_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":662,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"editingNotes\":\"Take 1 with lots of rollbacks\",\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Learn how AI-driven assessments and tests can help identify employee skill gaps and predict career potential. AI tools provide data-driven insights that enhance career planning.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":16060419,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- Artificial intelligence is transforming\\nthe way we understand people at work,\\nincluding how we assess\\nand understand their skills and personality traits.\\nHistorically, companies relied on static assessments.\\nEmployees completed multiple-choice questionnaires\\nor simulations,\\nand waited for results that were discussed\\nduring annual reviews or team-building exercises.\\nThese tools offered value,\\nbut they often lacked immediacy,\\ncontext and scalability.\\n\\nToday, AI changes that.\\nAI platforms can now analyze real-world behavior,\\ncommunication patterns and outputs\\nto assess both hard and soft skills.\\nInstead of asking employees to self-report\\nwhat they're good at,\\nthese tools observe what people do\\nand how they work.\\nTake Eightfold AI.\\nIt uses deep learning to scan millions of career paths\\nand generate a skills profile\\nfor every employee\\nbased on their experiences,\\nbehaviors and roles.\\n\\nIt doesn't just catalog skills,\\nit predicts which one somebody's likely to learn next.\\nIt helps companies map internal mobility\\nand recommend stretch assignments\\nwith greater precision.\\nWhen it comes to personality,\\nAI-enabled tools, like Humantic AI or Crystal,\\nuse natural languaging processing\\nto evaluate behavioral traits\\nbased on emails, bios and public writing.\\nThe goal isn't to replace self-assessments,\\nbut to compliment them with ongoing contextual data\\nthat supports realtime coaching and development.\\n\\nFor example, PeopleTransformation.ai\\nallows companies to incorporate personality assessments\\nand skill tests\\non top of doing an organizational network analysis.\\nThis allows for a more personalized experience\\nfrom the chatbots that support the developmental efforts.\\nThese tools bring speed, scale and personalization,\\nbut they can also raise ethical concerns.\\nTransparency is critical.\\n\\nFor example, employees should know\\nwhat data's being collected,\\nhow it's being managed\\nand how results will be used.\\nThere's also important discussions around bias,\\nespecially where AI is used in hiring\\nor promotional decisions.\\nLet's look at a real-world example.\\nHireVue, a video interviewing platform,\\nonce used AI to analyze facial expressions\\nand vocal tone.\\nAfter significant backlash around potential bias,\\nthe company discontinued facial analysis entirely\\nand refocused its platform\\non verbal responses and job-relevant assessments.\\n\\nOn the positive side,\\nAI can also reduce bias when used responsibly.\\nIt can uncover hidden potential,\\nrecommend development paths\\nand surface opportunities based on capability,\\nnot confidence or visibility.\\nPlatforms like SeekOut and Gloat\\nhelp organizations identify internal talent\\nwith high growth potential,\\nensuring fair access to stretch roles\\nand learning programs.\\n\\nAI tools, like ChatGPT,\\nalso empower individuals\\nto explore their growth paths.\\nEmployers can prompt it to summarize their skills,\\ngenerate role fit suggestions,\\nor simulate feedback based on goals,\\nhelping them take a more active role\\nin their development.\\nAI becomes their personalized career development coach.\\nSo what does this mean for you?\\nIt means using AI not to replace human judgment,\\nbut to enhance it.\\n\\nIt means embracing tools that provide richer insight,\\nbut always with fair, ethical and legal standards.\\nBecause when AI is used thoughtfully,\\nit helps us understand ourselves and others,\\nnot just faster, but better too.\\n\"}],\"name\":\"2. Skills and Personality Assessments\",\"size\":37975127,\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentChapter:4103082\"},{\"duration\":1421,\"entries\":[{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4103079\",\"duration\":302,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Helping employees define career goals\",\"fileName\":\"2032288_en_US_03_01_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":489,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"editingNotes\":\"Take 1 with rollbacks\",\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Learn how to guide employees in setting clear short- and long-term career goals. Well-defined goals improve motivation and alignment with company needs.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":16972552,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- Helping employees define career goals is one\\nof the most powerful things an organization can do,\\nand it's often an overlooked opportunity.\\nI recently worked with a company\\nthat had no career development goals\\nfor any of its employees\\nat any level of the organization.\\nPromotions were based primarily on longevity.\\nOn top of that, since it hadn't been growing lately,\\nyounger employees felt there were limited opportunities\\nfor growth and advancement.\\n\\nI helped the company to understand\\nthat there's always an opportunity for career growth\\nbecause that, in turn, creates business growth.\\nToo often, career planning is vague or formulaic.\\nWe challenge employees to think about where\\nthey see themselves in five years,\\nand then we don't offer the space, structure,\\nor support to figure that out.\\nWe assume that everyone wants a promotion,\\nwhen many want to deepen their craft,\\ntry something new, or simply find more meaning\\nin their work.\\n\\nSo how do you help employees define those goals?\\nYou start with a structured conversation.\\nInvite employees to consider what energizes them,\\nwhat skills they want to build,\\nreview their assessments,\\nand find out where they'd like to grow.\\nTools like individual development plans,\\nor IDPs, are useful,\\nbut only when integrated into ongoing conversations.\\nAdobe's approach offers a strong example.\\n\\nTheir check-in model replaced annual reviews\\nwith regular career conversations.\\nManagers are trained to explore goals based on impact,\\ninterest, and growth, not just job titles.\\nThe program has improved engagement\\nand boosted internal mobility across teams.\\nAI can now support this process in powerful ways.\\nPlatforms like PeopleTransformation.ai,\\nFuel50, and Gloat use skills data\\nand behavioral patterns to suggest career paths,\\nsurface role models,\\nand offer personalized development goals.\\n\\nThey help employees discover lateral\\nor upward moves that align with their experience\\nand preferences, something that's hard\\nto scale manually.\\nThe thing is, when given appropriate data,\\nAI can connect dots\\nand make recommendations\\nwe simply can't see for ourselves.\\nAI doesn't have time constraints,\\nand it's able to stay in touch with the employees\\nthrough their personalized chatbots.\\nEven tools like ChatGPT can play a role.\\n\\nEmployees might ask,\\n\\\"What are common transitions from my current role?\\\"\\nOr, \\\"What skills should I build\\nfor a productive management track?\\\"\\nAI responses provide ideas, frameworks,\\nand next steps that guide exploration.\\nIn fact, you can ask ChatGPT how it can support you,\\nand include information about your role,\\nthe company, industry trends, and anything else\\nto help stimulate its responses.\\n\\nAsk AI what questions you should ask it,\\nand it'll let you know the answer to that, too.\\nManagers also benefit from AI support.\\nChatGPT can generate sample goal-setting questions,\\ndraft follow-up emails,\\nor summarize goal-aligned development actions.\\nThis helps make conversations more consistent\\nand meaningful, especially for managers\\nwho aren't sure how to lead them.\\n\\nAt the company I mentioned earlier,\\nI took a few of their managers through ChatGPT\\nand showed them how it can immediately improve their jobs\\nas managers and support their teams.\\nI show them how AI is like a personal assistant\\nthat can free them up to do more strategic\\nand career-benefiting work.\\nWhile AI is truly amazing,\\ncareer goals are ultimately human.\\nTechnology should support, not replace,\\nthe conversations that help people to clarify\\nand act on their ambitions.\\n\\nSo the next time someone says, \\\"I'm bored,\\\"\\nor, \\\"I'm not sure what I want to do next,\\\"\\nsee it as a starting point,\\nbecause helping somebody define their future\\nis one of the most valuable things you can do\\nas a leader.\\nIn the exercise file, you'll find\\na blank career goal discovery worksheet,\\nas well as a completed example\\nfor a new nurse at a regional hospital.\\nI worked with ChatGPT to create both the blank form\\nand the nurse example.\\n\\nYou can input these documents into ChatGPT,\\nor another AI tool,\\nand tweak them for your situation very easily.\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4110021\",\"duration\":185,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Helping employees develop career roadmaps\",\"fileName\":\"2032288_en_US_03_02_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":419,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"editingNotes\":\"Take 1 with rollbacks\",\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Learn how to create structured career roadmaps that provide employees with clear pathways for growth. Defined career paths increase motivation, retention, and future talent planning.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":9271487,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- When we talk about helping employees grow,\\ntwo terms often come up:\\ncareer roadmaps and career development plans.\\nThey sound similar, but they serve different purposes.\\nA career roadmap is a big picture.\\nIt's about possibilities,\\nwhat path someone might take over the next five years,\\nwhat kind of roles they might grow into,\\nand how their skills could evolve along the way.\\nIt's directional, not prescriptive.\\nThink of it as a GPS view\\nof multiple routes and destinations.\\n\\nA career development plan, on the other hand, is tactical.\\nIt focuses on what somebody is doing now to move forward,\\nwhat skills they're building,\\nwhat stretch assignments they're taking on,\\nand what short-term goals they're working towards.\\nIt's the day-to-day navigation.\\nIn this lesson, we're going to focus on roadmaps,\\nhow to help employees explore where they might want to go\\nbefore they commit to how they're going to get there.\\nSo, how do you help employees create career roadmaps?\\nWhen I do career coaching,\\none thing I encourage clients to do\\nis to look at the company roster\\nand related LinkedIn profiles\\nand see what type of position\\nthey would like to have in the future.\\n\\nWhat career path did that person take to get there?\\nWhat you'll quickly see is there's more than one career path\\nto obtaining that position.\\nTechnology can help, too.\\nPlatforms like Fuel50 offer dynamic career pathing tools\\nwhere employees can set goals, identify skill gaps,\\nand explore lateral or vertical moves across the company.\\nAI-driven platforms personalize suggestions\\nbased on role, interests, and aspirations.\\n\\nUsing ChatGPT can support career clarity.\\nAn employee might ask,\\n\\\"What are common next steps\\n\\\"from a project coordinator role?\\\"\\nOr, \\\"What skills should I build to move into strategy?\\\"\\nThese tools give employees a starting point\\nand signal that the company cares about their growth.\\nCareer roadmaps don't have to be rigid or perfect,\\nbut they do need to exist,\\nbecause when employees can see the road ahead,\\neven in broad strokes,\\nthey're more likely to move forward with confidence.\\n\\nYour job isn't to define every turn,\\nit's to help them think about their future opportunities.\\nCareer development doesn't happen by accident,\\nit happens when people have a roadmap.\\nIn the exercise file,\\nyou'll find a blank Career Roadmap Builder,\\nas well as a completed example\\nfor a new nurse at a regional hospital.\\nI worked with ChatGPT to create both the blank form\\nand the example,\\nand you can input those documents into ChatGPT\\nor another AI tool\\nand tweak them for your situation very easily.\\n\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4108065\",\"duration\":212,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Creating and supporting career development plans\",\"fileName\":\"2032288_en_US_03_03_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":403,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"editingNotes\":\"Take 1 with a rollback and an insert rollback\",\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Learn how to co-create actionable development plans that align employee aspirations with business needs.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":11808519,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- A career development plan is not a wishlist.\\nIt's a working document.\\nIt helps employees focus their time, energy,\\nand learning in a way that's realistic, measurable,\\nand aligned with the business.\\nBy this point,\\nemployees may have explored different directions\\nand long-term ideas.\\nThey may have even developed a career development roadmap.\\nNow it's time to narrow the focus\\nand put a concrete plan in motion.\\n\\nA good development plan includes clear time-bound steps.\\nIt's tactical.\\nIt answers, what skill am I building?\\nHow will I build it?\\nBy when and how will we measure progress?\\nStart by identifying one or two priority skills\\nor competencies.\\nThese should be tied to the employee's role\\nor future readiness.\\nFor example, build project management skills\\nor improve client facing communication.\\n\\nThen define how the employee will build those skills.\\nThat might include taking a specific course\\nof certification, leading a stretch project,\\nshadowing a senior team member,\\nor practicing in day-to-day work and getting feedback.\\nEvery action item should have an agreement about\\nwhen it will get done.\\nWrite it down.\\nThis increases clarity and accountability.\\nAt Schneider Electric, development plans are created\\nthrough an internal platform\\nthat suggests learning resources\\nand mentors based on skill profiles.\\n\\nManagers revisit these plans quarterly to assess progress\\nand adjust as needed,\\nturning development into a rhythm,\\nnot a one-off task.\\nAI tools make this process easier.\\nPlatforms like Degreed, EdCast\\nand SkyHive generate learning paths tailored\\nto the individual's current role and career goals.\\nEven ChatGPT can be used to identify the gap\\nbetween two job descriptions\\nand suggest a structured action plan to bridge that gap.\\n\\nRemember, the best plans are flexible.\\nBusiness needs change.\\nInterest evolve, but planning doesn't mean rigidity.\\nIt means momentum and progress.\\nReview plans quarterly, celebrate progress,\\nadjust goals,\\nand most importantly, tie each item to real work.\\nIf employees are learning something new,\\nhelp them use it on the job.\\nSo here's your challenge.\\n\\nPick one employee this month, review their plan\\nor help them to build one from scratch.\\nFocus on one or two real skills\\nand schedule a 90 day follow up.\\nIn the exercise file,\\nyou'll find a blank career development action plan as well\\nas a completed example\\nfor a new nurse at a regional hospital.\\nI worked with ChatGPT to create both the blank form\\nand the nurse example.\\nYou can input these documents into ChatGPT\\nor another AI tool\\nand tweak them for your situation very easily.\\n\\nA career development plan is the ultimate tool\\nto ensure career development.\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4110019\",\"duration\":172,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Best practices for career development conversations\",\"fileName\":\"2032288_en_US_03_04_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":271,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"editingNotes\":\"Take 1 with rollbacks\",\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Learn how to use AI tools to facilitate structured career discussions. AI-driven insights improve the accuracy and effectiveness of career development planning.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":9192500,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- Career development conversations are one\\nof the most valuable ways managers can support employee\\ngrowth, but very often they're neglected entirely\\nor treated as something to get over with\\nwhen they do happen.\\nThese conversations are frequently tied\\nto performance reviews,\\nwhich can make them feel judgemental rather than exploratory\\nto be effective.\\nCareer conversations need to happen more regularly\\nand focus on the future, not just the past.\\n\\nA strong conversation starts with curiosity.\\nAsk open-ended questions like,\\nwhat kind of work do you see yourself\\ndoing in three years from now?\\nOr, what skills would you love to build next?\\nAvoid assuming that everyone wants to climb the ladder.\\nGrowth can include expanding influence, mastering a skill,\\nor exploring new directions.\\nYour role is to guide, not prescribe.\\nHelp employees articulate what they want,\\nidentify development opportunities,\\nand take ownership of their next steps.\\n\\nAtlassian offers a great example.\\nTheir managers are trained\\nto have forward focused development conversations as part\\nof their regular check-ins.\\nThese aren't one-off events.\\nThey're integrate it into team rhythms.\\nBy normalizing career discussions,\\nthey've strengthened internal mobility\\nand built trust in their growth culture.\\nFrameworks can add structure.\\nThe GROW model is one popular approach.\\n\\nGoal, what's a long-term outcome the employee wants?\\nReality, what's their current state?\\nOptions, what are the possibilities or blockers?\\nAnd will, what's the next step they're committed to?\\nAI tools can also support this process.\\nPlatforms like Fuel50 and Humu use behavioral data\\nto suggest conversational prompts\\nand development insights tailored to that individual.\\n\\nEven ChatGPT can help generate custom discussion questions\\nbased on an employee's job role or career interest.\\nThe secret to success, consistency.\\nCareer conversations work best when they're part\\nof a regular rhythm, not something safe for someday.\\nSo here's your challenge.\\nPick one person on your team\\nand schedule a career check in this week.\\nUse AI if it helps,\\nbut bring your full attention to the conversation\\nbecause when employees feel seen\\nand invested in, they don't just stick around,\\nthey grow into the talent your organization will need next.\\n\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4104060\",\"duration\":250,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"AI\u2019s role in career conversations\",\"fileName\":\"2032288_en_US_03_05_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":458,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"editingNotes\":\"Take 1 with rollbacks and an insert rollback\",\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Learn how AI tools can support more effective, frequent, and personalized career conversations between employees and managers.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":14184826,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- Career conversations are one of the most valuable tools\\nfor employee development,\\nbut they're often overlooked,\\nrushed, or done poorly.\\nDone well, they're game changers.\\nThese conversations build trust, uncover aspirations,\\nalign development with business needs,\\nand help employees to feel heard.\\nYet many managers don't feel equipped to lead them,\\nand many employees aren't sure how to start.\\nAnd that's where AI can help.\\n\\nNot by replacing human dialogue,\\nbut by making it easier to initiate\\nmore thoughtful in content\\nand more personalized for both parties.\\nFor employees, tools like ChatGPT\\noffer structure and confidence.\\nSomebody might prompt,\\n\\\"How do I talk to my manager about moving into a new role?\\\"\\nOr, \\\"What questions should I ask\\nduring a career development meeting?\\\"\\nThe tool provides suggestions,\\nlanguage, and sequencing,\\nmaking it easier to clarify intentions and frame requests.\\n\\nManagers benefit just as much.\\nAI can generate tailored discussion guides,\\ncoaching questions, and follow-up actions\\nbased on an employee's role, skills, and goals.\\nIt can even align these conversations\\nwith business priorities,\\nhelping managers connect growth discussions\\nwith organizational strategy.\\nRemember, the more data you provide AI,\\nthe more personalized the answer will become.\\n\\nUploading company information,\\njob descriptions, training options, etc.,\\ncan help give a better response.\\nSome companies are already doing this at scale.\\nIBM uses its internal AI platform\\nto support dynamic career conversations.\\nIt recommends learning paths, conversation starters,\\nand personalized development goals for employees,\\nwhile giving managers real-time insights\\nto guide their side of the dialogue.\\n\\nAI-powered tools like People Transformation.AI\\nare also helping companies surface hidden talent,\\nflag potential flight risks,\\nand suggest interventions.\\nTheir predictive insights make it easier\\nto know which conversations matter most\\nand when to have them.\\nAnother benefit is accountability.\\nAI can track what was discussed,\\nsuggest next steps,\\nand remind both manager and employee when to follow up.\\n\\nThis creates continuity between conversations\\nand helps ensure development doesn't get lost\\nin the daily shuffle.\\nIf you're a small company\\nor don't already have a software program deploying AI\\nin this space,\\nthere's always the opportunity\\nto use generative AI platforms like ChatGPT.\\nIt will help you to reflect on employee skills,\\ndraft development goals,\\nor simulate conversations ahead of one-to-one meetings.\\n\\nThese tools promote autonomy\\nand reduce the awkwardness of not knowing what to say.\\nStill, AI isn't a substitute\\nfor empathy or real-time responsiveness.\\nThe best career conversations\\nare grounded in deep listening.\\nAI simply reduces friction and supports consistency\\nso that more conversations happen,\\nand more of them have impact.\\nSo if career conversations have felt awkward,\\ninconsistent, or too infrequent,\\nlet AI help you to change that.\\n\\nNext up, you'll get an opportunity\\nto practice navigating a development conversation with AI,\\nbecause when conversations improve,\\ncareers move, and when people feel heard,\\nthey grow faster and with more purpose.\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:2051077\",\"duration\":0,\"visible\":false,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":null,\"name\":\"FAKE MOVIE Practice: Navigating a career development conversation\",\"fileName\":\"2032288_en_US_03_06_FAKEVIDEO\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":300,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"editingNotes\":\"Role Play\",\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Complete this role-play to better apply effective questioning and active listening techniques to guide employees in defining clear and actionable career goals. Career development discussions shape employee motivation, retention, and growth.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"NOT_AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"NOT_ATTEMPTED\",\"size\":0,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"NEW\",\"transcript\":null},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentArticle:358005\",\"duration\":300,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Practice Role Play: Turning goals and roadmaps into a development plan\"}],\"name\":\"3. Aligning Employee Aspirations with Career Development\",\"size\":61429884,\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentChapter:2052066\"},{\"duration\":970,\"entries\":[{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4103080\",\"duration\":215,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Stretch assignments and cross-training\",\"fileName\":\"2032288_en_US_04_01_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":344,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"editingNotes\":\"Take 1 with rollbacks\",\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Learn how stretch assignments and cross-training enhance employee skill development. Hands-on experience accelerates career growth and business adaptability.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":11407986,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- Stretch assignments and cross-training\\nare among the most effective yet underutilized tools\\nfor talent development.\\nThey're experiential, flexible, and scalable,\\nand best of all, they require little\\nor no budget to implement.\\nA stretch assignment is a task, project,\\nor responsibility that pushes somebody\\nbeyond their current skillset or comfort zone.\\nIt could be presenting to leadership,\\nleading a cross-functional team, managing a budget,\\nor solving a problem that no one else has tackled.\\n\\nThese experiences help employees to grow faster\\nby learning through real work.\\nCross-training, by contrast, exposes employees\\nto different functions, roles, or workflows.\\nIt's not about somebody changing careers,\\nit's about building range, systems thinking,\\nand collaborative capacity across the business.\\nTogether, these tools help build a resilient,\\nagile workforce.\\nStretch roles build leadership.\\n\\nCross-training improves alignment and flexibility.\\nBoth help employees to discover hidden strengths\\nand create deeper engagement.\\nAt AT&T, stretch roles are built\\ninto the company's career development strategy.\\nEmployees are encouraged to apply for temporary\\nor part-time projects outside of their formal job title.\\nManagers are trained to identify\\nand recommend stretch opportunities\\nduring regular development conversations.\\n\\nThis has helped AT&T create\\none of the strongest internal mobility cultures\\nin the Fortune 100.\\nAI makes this easier to scale.\\nPlatforms like Gloat, Fuel50, and Degreed use skills data\\nand role profiles to recommend internal gigs\\nand lateral training opportunities\\nthat might otherwise go unnoticed.\\nThey help employees match their current skills\\nwith temporary assignments\\nand allow managers to identify team members\\nready for cross-functional exposure.\\n\\nChatGPT can be a practical tool, too.\\nManagers can use prompts like,\\n\\\"Suggest three stretch assignments\\nfor a financial analyst interested in leadership,\\\"\\nor \\\"What cross-training roles\\nwould benefit a customer service agent\\nmoving into operations?\\\"\\nEven better, AI can assess readiness.\\nTools like SkyHive and Eightfold.ai\\ncan analyze skill adjacency and performance history\\nto predict who's in the best position\\nto take on new challenges\\nbefore those roles are even posted.\\n\\nAnd here's a real story.\\nAfter the pandemic, one of my clients\\nasked an entry-level HR administrator to help with hiring.\\nWithin three months,\\nshe became the organization's top recruiter.\\nHer performance wouldn't have shown up on a spreadsheet,\\nbut emerged through experience.\\nSo here's your challenge.\\nUse the AI coach immediately following this video\\nto have a practice conversation\\nencouraging participation in stretch assignments\\nbecause stretch assignments\\nand cross-training don't just prepare people for new roles,\\nthey reveal what they're truly capable of.\\n\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4107059\",\"duration\":0,\"visible\":false,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":null,\"name\":\"FAKE MOVIE Practice: Encouraging participation in stretch assignments\",\"fileName\":\"2032288_en_US_04_02_FAKEVIDEO\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":300,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"editingNotes\":\"Role Play\",\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Complete this role-play to learn how to create a compelling case for stretch assignments by addressing employee concerns and aligning opportunities with career goals. Strategic development experiences drive skill enhancement and career mobility.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"NOT_AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"NOT_ATTEMPTED\",\"size\":0,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"NEW\",\"transcript\":null},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentArticle:366002\",\"duration\":300,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Practice Role Play: Encourage someone to accept a stretch assignment\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4110018\",\"duration\":232,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"AI in employee learning and development\",\"fileName\":\"2032288_en_US_04_03_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":415,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"editingNotes\":\"Take 1 with rollbacks\",\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Learn how to leverage AI-powered learning tools to create personalized, responsive development experiences for employees.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":12606258,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- Artificial intelligence\\nis transforming how employees learn\\nand how organization deliver that learning\\nat scale and speed.\\nTraditional learning and development,\\nor otherwise known as L and D programs,\\noften rely on broad, one-size-fits-all offerings.\\nThese may look efficient,\\nbut they often miss the mark.\\nEmployees are assigned mandatory courses\\nthat don't exactly match their role, goals or interests,\\nand companies lose opportunities\\nto deliver timely, strategic upskilling.\\n\\nAI changes that.\\nIt enables learning that's personalized, relevant,\\nand embedded in the daily work.\\nIt helps to align employee aspirations\\nwith business priorities\\nwhile saving time and improving outcomes.\\nFor example, personalized learning platforms\\nlike Degreed, EdCast and LinkedIn Learning\\nuse AI to recommend courses and micro-learning content\\nbased on real-time data,\\nsuch as the employee's role, career interests,\\nskill assessments, and performance reviews.\\n\\nat Accenture, an AI-powered platform\\ntracks over 8,000 skills in its internal talent marketplace.\\nThis system connects employees to projects, roles,\\nand learning experiences\\nthat are aligned with their unique skill profile\\nand future career goals.\\nThe result is a highly-personalized growth pathway\\ndriven by data, not by guesswork.\\nAmazon uses a similar model.\\nIts machine learning university\\nprovides personalized learning experiences\\nusing AI recommendations\\nbased on job function and project needs.\\n\\nThe company credits this system\\nwith accelerating internal mobility\\nand filling hard-to-hire roles from within.\\nAI also helps employees learn in real time.\\nPlatforms like PeopleTransformation.ai, Humu and BetterUp\\ndeliver \\\"in-the-flow-of-work\\\" nudges or suggestions\\ntriggered by recent behavior, feedback, or milestones.\\nThese nudges might suggest a quick read, a coaching moment,\\nor a follow-up question based on what the employee just did.\\n\\nLearning becomes contextual, timely, and sticky.\\nManagers also benefit.\\nAI can flag team-wide skill gaps,\\nrecommend just-in-time training,\\nor suggest stretch assignments based on upcoming projects.\\nTools like SkyHive analyze market and internal data\\nto show which capabilities are rising in importance\\nand where each team stands today.\\nEven a tool like ChatGPT can help.\\n\\nManagers can use it to create customized development plans,\\ngenerate coaching questions,\\nor recommend free learning content based on team priorities.\\nEmployees can use it to identify their skill gaps\\nand explore role-specific growth strategies.\\nHere's your call to action.\\nChoose one AI-enabled learning platform available to you\\nor experiment with ChatGPT.\\nAsk it to help you create a growth plan\\nor identify three skills you need to move into a future role\\nbecause AI is no longer just a futuristic idea,\\nit's a practical tool for growing people, building careers,\\nand aligning learning and development\\nwith what the business needs next.\\n\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4104059\",\"duration\":223,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Supporting managers for career growth\",\"fileName\":\"2032288_en_US_04_04_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":353,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"editingNotes\":\"Take 1 with rollbacks (was wrongly slated as \\\"04_03 learning\\\" -- tail slated correctly as \\\"04_04 manager\\\")\",\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Learn how to support and equip managers to drive career development conversations and model growth culture within their teams.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":12857541,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- For career development to thrive,\\nit must be embedded into a company's culture,\\nnot just its HR systems.\\nAnd that starts with manager support managers,\\noften the gatekeepers to growth.\\nThey approve training,\\nsuggest stretch assignments,\\nand hold the conversations that shape careers.\\nBut not all managers feel confident doing this.\\nWell, I know this much.\\nHalf of managers lean into growth conversations\\nbetter than the other half.\\n\\nMany managers avoid these critical conversations\\nbecause they don't feel prepared\\nor they worry about saying the wrong thing.\\nThat's why building a culture\\nof development must include manager training,\\npractical tools, and clear expectations from leadership.\\nThe best companies make employee development part\\nof the manager's actual job.\\nAt Unilever, every manager is expected\\nto hold monthly development conversations.\\n\\nThey're trained to ask questions, give feedback,\\nand connect growth with both personal goals\\nand organizational strategy.\\nThat rhythm has helped make development part\\nof daily operations, not a bonus conversation.\\nSo how do you build that kind of support?\\nFirst, set expectations.\\nMake it clear that career development is part\\nof the manager's role.\\nAdd it to job descriptions and performance reviews.\\n\\nThen teach them basic coaching skills.\\nHow to ask open-ended questions,\\nlisten without fixing\\nand following up.\\nSecond, give them tools.\\nOffer frameworks for development conversations,\\nguidance on stretch assignments,\\nand access to mobility data.\\nSites like LinkedIn Learning offer\\nentire courses designed to help manage\\nand become better career coaches.\\nYou can create a video for your managers that shows them how\\nto use your existing AI programs\\nor program like ChatGPT to help\\nwith everything from career roadmap development\\nto one-on-one conversations.\\n\\nThird, role model it.\\nExecutives should share their own development stories\\nand talk about the managers who help them to grow.\\nWhen leaders model learning\\nand vulnerability managers are more likely to do the same.\\nAI can make this even more actionable.\\nPlatforms like PeopleTransformation.ai,\\nBetterUp, and Humu\\nprompt timely check-ins suggest coaching questions\\nand highlight skills gaps using real time behavioral data.\\n\\nTools like ChatGPT can help a manager generate tailored\\ncareer questions based on role goals or current performance.\\nSome systems even use AI\\nto predict which team members might be at the risk\\nof disengaging and recommend targeted support.\\nBut tech alone isn't enough.\\nGrowth conversation should happen in real time\\nin one-to-ones debriefs and in team meetings.\\n\\nThey need to be on the calendar,\\nnot just in a manager's head.\\nSo here's your challenge.\\nSchedule one development conversation\\nwith a manager this week.\\nAsk, how can you do a better job\\nof supporting your employees and their career development?\\nThen help them take a first step and follow through.\\n\"}],\"name\":\"4. Additional Career Development Opportunities\",\"size\":36871785,\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentChapter:4108066\"},{\"duration\":78,\"entries\":[{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4107058\",\"duration\":78,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":null,\"name\":\"Creating an actionable career development strategy\",\"fileName\":\"2032288_en_US_05_01_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":150,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"editingNotes\":\"Take 1 with rollbacks\",\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Learn how to develop a company-wide career development strategy. Structured programs ensure consistent employee growth and workforce readiness.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":4645800,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- These are exciting times\\nin the world of career development.\\nJob requirements are changing rapidly\\nand people need to adapt\\nor they're going to become irrelevant,\\nand it's your job to help them.\\nFortunately, AI can help both you\\nand your team with career management.\\nYou can start by downloading\\nthe exercise files from this course,\\nincluding the sample roadmap,\\nsample plan, AI prompts,\\nand a resource sheet with links\\nto many of the case studies I discussed in this course.\\n\\nUse the roadmap and plan as a starting point\\nand adapt them to fit your needs.\\nYou can also revisit the AI coach\\nin this course to get more practice\\nhaving various career development conversations\\nin a no-stakes environment.\\nIf you want to learn more about me and the work that I do,\\nyou can visit my website at donphin.com.\\nYou'll see that I have plenty of free tools, books,\\nand other resources.\\nAs challenging as AI can be,\\nthere is tremendous opportunity.\\n\\nWith the right career development plan,\\nyou and your employees can become your best selves\\nno matter what the future holds.\\n\"}],\"name\":\"Conclusion\",\"size\":4645800,\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentChapter:4103083\"}],\"size\":184738788,\"duration\":4552,\"zeroBased\":false},{\"course_title\":\"How to Use AI for Upskilling and Lifelong Learning\",\"course_admin_id\":3980811,\"metadata\":{\"Locale\":\"en_US\",\"Course ID\":3980811,\"Project ID\":null,\"Course Name\":\"How to Use AI for Upskilling and Lifelong Learning\",\"Course Name EN\":\"How to Use AI for Upskilling and Lifelong Learning\",\"Activation Status\":\"ACTIVE\",\"Display to Public\":\"No\",\"Display to QA\":\"Yes\",\"Course Description\":\"Traditional learning methods are time-consuming, expensive, and difficult to curate. This course teaches you how to use AI as your bespoke learning assistant by finding relevant and personalized learning topics, using AI to enhance retention, recall, and skill application, while maintaining motivation and curiosity. These skills can help you learn more effectively and efficiently, while simultaneously growing professionally, achieving learning goals, and staying relevant and competitive in the workforce. Check out this course to discover how you can leverage AI as a personalized learning assistant.\",\"Course Short Description\":\"Find out how to achieve your learning goals more effectively and efficiently, grow professionally, and stay relevant and competitive in the workforce with AI.\",\"Content Type\":\"SKILLS\",\"Localization Type\":\"ORIGINAL\",\"Original Course Locale\":null,\"Original Course ID\":null,\"Equivalent English Course\":null,\"Instructor ID\":\"20169001\",\"Instructor Name\":\"Ruth Gotian\",\"Instructor Transliterated Name\":null,\"Instructor Short Bio\":\"Learning Executive and Performance Coach\",\"Author Payment Category\":\"NON-LICENSED\",\"Delivery Mode\":\"ALL_AT_ONCE\",\"Series End Date\":null,\"Course Release Date\":null,\"Course Updated Date\":null,\"Course Archive Date\":null,\"Course Retire Date\":null,\"Replacement Course\":null,\"Has Assessment\":\"No\",\"Has Challenge/Solution\":\"Yes\",\"LIL URL\":\"https://www.linkedin.com/learning/how-to-use-ai-for-upskilling-and-lifelong-learning\",\"Series\":\"One-Off\",\"Limited Series\":null,\"Manager Level\":\"Individual Contributor\",\"LI Level\":\"Beginner + Intermediate\",\"LI Level EN\":\"Beginner + Intermediate\",\"Sensitivity\":null,\"Internal Library\":\"Business\",\"Internal Subject\":\"General Skills\",\"Primary Software\":null,\"Media Type\":null,\"Has CEU\":\"No\",\"Has Exercise Files\":\"No\",\"Visible Duration\":2346.0,\"Visible Video Count\":15.0,\"Learning Objectives\":\"Identify and engage with relevant and personalized learning topics.,Use AI to enhance retention, recall, and the application of skills.,Maintain motivation and curiosity throughout the learning journey.\",\"Contract Type\":\"PERPETUAL\",\"Certifications\":null,\"Framework Topic\":\"Level 2: Applying, AI Upskilling Framework, AI Upskilling Framework Level 2: Applying, AI Framework Level 2: Applying\",\"Automatic Caption Translations\":null,\"Automatic Metadata Translations\":null,\"Gen AI Feature Flag\":null,\"Hands-On Practice\":null,\"Hands-On Practice Library\":null,\"Unlocked for Viva Learning\":null,\"Free Course\":null,\"Certification Library\":null,\"Github Codespace\":null,\"Skills Count\":2,\"Skills\":\"Artificial Intelligence for Business,Learning\",\"Skills EN\":\"Artificial Intelligence for Business,Learning\",\"Content Manager\":\"Susan Williams\",\"Acquisition Manager\":\"Susan Williams\",\"Framework Subject\":\"AI Upskilling Framework, AI Framework Level 2: Applying\",\"Suppress Upsells\":null},\"sections\":[{\"duration\":285,\"entries\":[{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4104124\",\"duration\":58,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":null,\"name\":\"Why AI is a critical tool for lifelong learning\",\"fileName\":\"3980811_en_US_00_01_VT\",\"demo\":true,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":652,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Ruth Gotian introduces the course on how to use AI for upskilling and lifelong learning, and explains what to expect from the course.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":4560264,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":true,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- We need re-skilling and upskilling\\nin order to adapt to the rapidly changing global markets.\\nThe key to staying relevant\\nis likely powered by artificial intelligence, AI.\\nHi, I'm Dr. Ruth Gotian,\\na Social Scientist who studies high achievers,\\nincluding Nobel Prize winners, astronauts,\\nOlympic and NBA Champions.\\nDo you know one thing they all have in common?\\nThey crave new knowledge,\\nand never stop learning.\\nI've spent my career researching\\nand advising how each person can learn more effectively,\\nand apply knowledge to reach their full potential.\\n\\nAI is one of the most powerful tools to achieve this goal.\\nIt makes learning personalized to you.\\nIt can curate content, summarize complex ideas,\\nand even adapt to your preferred learning method.\\nIn this course,\\nwe'll explore how AI can supercharge your learning,\\nso as the world changes, you're ready.\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4104123\",\"duration\":167,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"How technology is changing lifelong learning\",\"fileName\":\"3980811_en_US_00_02_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":265,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Explore the benefits of AI and technology in pursuit of lifelong learning. This information will serve as the basis for the course.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":8992756,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- I remember when the internet went live for the masses.\\nWe were simultaneously confused and intrigued.\\nIt took a long time for people to agree to use it,\\nbut now, we can't imagine not having it.\\nJust the thought of losing Wi-Fi has us all jittery.\\nThat's same newness and learning curve\\nhas come again this time with AI.\\nAccording to a McKinsey & Company survey,\\n87% of executives say there is a skill gap in the workforce,\\nthat's nearly nine out of 10.\\n\\nThe challenge is that most organizations\\ndon't have a plan in place to address this issue.\\nIt might be up to each person to come up\\nwith their own plan for now.\\nAI is completely redefining how we learn\\nand what's possible.\\nIt's making it streamlined, accessible, and democratized.\\nI got my doctorate in adult learning and leadership,\\nand what's become obvious is that traditional\\nlearning models cannot keep up\\nwith the rapid rate of change.\\n\\nWhen I went to grad school, I was working all day\\nand then went to school in the evenings.\\nThere was a commute, long hours in a classroom,\\nand some, but not much,\\nflexibility in what courses I could take.\\nBut not everyone wants or needs a degree.\\nAnd with the world changing so quickly,\\nwe need courses that can keep up with the rate of change.\\nNow, with AI, that has completely changed.\\nCourses are on demand, curated,\\nand allow for micro learning,\\nshort bursts of learning\\ninstead of long sessions with endless lectures.\\n\\nAI can customize learning to what you need.\\nIt can be modified based on skill level,\\nlearning style, and goals.\\nNo more one-size-fits-all.\\nYou can tell AI what you want to learn\\nand how you prefer to consume new knowledge,\\nand it can scan millions of sources\\nand give you a curated list.\\nAdd AI powered chatbots and role playing,\\nand you can get interactivity and instant feedback.\\nLearning is no longer limited by ability,\\nmoney, or geography.\\n\\nAI can cut out the noise and only give you information\\non the specific topic you are looking for,\\nand it's all updated and relevant.\\nIt's not flawless yet, but it's close.\\nAI still has hallucinations\\nand what is called digital amnesia.\\nIt forgets or omits things, so a human needs\\nto carefully double check the output.\\nAI and technology are not just tools,\\nthey are revolutionizing lifelong learning.\\n\\nThose who will leverage them effectively\\nwill gain a competitive edge in their careers.\\n\"}],\"name\":\"Introduction\",\"size\":15012138,\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentChapter:4110071\"},{\"duration\":324,\"entries\":[{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4106101\",\"duration\":115,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"AI as the ultimate learning partner\",\"fileName\":\"3980811_en_US_01_01_VT\",\"demo\":true,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":183,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Learn how AI serves as a differentiator in transforming professional development and evaluate its impact on lifelong learning. Understanding the broader use of AI in learning helps you adapt strategies and consistently move forward in your career.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":5588866,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- Here's a forecast which may shock you.\\nAccording to the World Economic Forum,\\nyou can expect nearly 40% of your current skills\\nto be either transformed or outdated by 2030.\\nThat should be a wake up call.\\nUpskilling is no longer something that's nice to have.\\nIt's something you must do\\nif you wish to remain relevant and employed.\\nThe world of work is changing at lightning speed,\\nand AI is playing a central role in upskilling\\nand lifelong learning.\\n\\nAI has become the ultimate learning partner.\\nI am a huge believer in traditional learning methods,\\nsuch as books, articles, and lectures,\\nbut as an author,\\nI also know that from the time I finish writing a book\\nuntil the time it's on your shelf can take a year.\\nThat means some of the information will be outdated\\nbefore you see it.\\nThis is where AI is a game changer\\nfor your personal learning,\\nso that you can access the latest learning tools.\\nIt can help you develop your own learning plan,\\nidentify your career goals,\\nand recommend courses you can take,\\nbooks and articles you can read\\nand podcasts to listen to.\\n\\nIf you haven't already,\\nI recommend you try the AI Coach option\\nwithin LinkedIn Learning.\\nYou tell it what you want to learn,\\nand it will recommend courses for you.\\nIn some courses, you can even role play with AI.\\nAI can help you assess the gap between where you want to go\\nand what you are currently doing,\\nand then recommend resources to help you fill that gap.\\nWhether long form courses, micro courses, AI-driven chats,\\nwhich can emulate a meeting\\nwith a coach are all options\\nwhich are there to help you upskill.\\n\\nAI is not just a tool,\\nit's a learning partner,\\nwhich is enhancing\\nand helping you grow your career in real time.\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4108123\",\"duration\":209,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Using AI to learn faster, smarter, and more efficiently\",\"fileName\":\"3980811_en_US_01_02_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":232,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Learn how to be more efficient with your learning by applying AI-driven techniques and you'll be able to construct a bespoke learning plan by using AI. Leveraging AI for efficiency will help you maximize your time, focus on learning, and learn and do more due to time savings.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":8579066,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- In the past, when I would write a book, article,\\nor even develop a course, I would spend weeks\\nreading the business and academic literature\\nto find the latest statistics, case studies,\\nand thought leadership.\\nToday, I can put my query into AI\\nand get a list of all the resources.\\nOf course, I still need to read them and analyze them,\\nbut AI can curate that information for me,\\nsaving me hundreds of hours of research.\\nI can then upload my notes on each article\\nand ask AI to summarize them by theme,\\nagain, saving me hundreds of hours.\\n\\nI'm not alone in looking to save time on time-sucking tasks.\\nA McKinsey study determined that AI\\ncould increase productivity\\nby up to 40% by 2035.\\nThe automation will be everywhere.\\nHave you heard of the 10,000-hour rule?\\nMalcolm Gladwell coined the concept in his book, \\\"Outliers.\\\"\\nIt states that if you dedicate 10,000 hours\\nof deliberate practice to a field, it can lead to mastery.\\nI want you to forget the 10,000-hour rule.\\n\\nYou no longer have the benefit of time.\\nYou can no longer spend years mastering a topic\\nbefore attempting to apply it.\\nYou need to, metaphorically speaking,\\nbuild the plane as you're flying it.\\nAI can help you find, absorb, process,\\nand apply the knowledge\\nfaster and more efficiently than ever before.\\nHave you ever read books, articles, or taken courses\\nwhich were not aligned with what you wanted to learn?\\nDid you feel that you just wasted your time\\nand wish you could get it back?\\nAI can help.\\n\\nPrompt AI by explaining what you want to learn,\\nand it can find the resources for you, all within seconds.\\nIt can create worksheets, study sheets,\\nand quizzes to test your knowledge.\\nHere's an example.\\nImagine you need to give a presentation to the board.\\nIt is high stakes, so you want to get it right.\\nPrompt AI with the following description.\\n\\\"I am giving a high-stakes presentation to the board\\non topic X.\\nI want to be prepared, practice my keynote speaking skills,\\nmake sure the presentation drives the points home\\nwhile encouraging the board,\\nand I want to practice handling the high-pressure Q&A.\\\"\\nWithin seconds, AI returns a personalized learning toolkit.\\n\\nIt may include book recommendations on crafting a story,\\na TED Talk on your body language,\\na podcast episode on how to talk to executives,\\na customized learning plan\\noutlining what you should focus on each day\\nto prepare for your presentation,\\nscripts, ability to record and analyze your talk\\nfor unnecessary ums and ahs,\\na simulated question-and-answer session\\nwith questions generated by AI,\\na one-page message clarity worksheet,\\na checklist to assess vocal variety, and eye contact.\\n\\nWhew, that's a lot.\\nInstead of spending hours sifting\\nand Googling through irrelevant material,\\nyou can now get something that is specific to you\\nand your exact needs.\\nAI is making learning faster, smarter, and more efficient,\\nbut only if you use it strategically.\\nThe best way to get started is to simply start. Start small.\\nPick one AI tool,\\nand test how it optimizes your learning this week.\\n\"}],\"name\":\"1. AI Is the New Approach to Lifelong Learning\",\"size\":14167932,\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentChapter:4107113\"},{\"duration\":572,\"entries\":[{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4104122\",\"duration\":159,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Personalizing your learning using AI\",\"fileName\":\"3980811_en_US_02_01_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":232,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Learn how to assess AI's ability to create bespoke content for your individual learning plan and develop a strategy for regularly integrating AI-powered recommendations into your learning plan.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":6593557,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- Study after study have repeatedly come\\nto the same conclusion.\\nActive learning, where you are taught\\nhow to apply the learning,\\nbeats passive learning, where you absorb the information.\\nWhat do the different approaches look like?\\nWell, in passive learning,\\nyou are reading or hearing lectures.\\nIn active learning, you are having discussions,\\nproblem-solving, or working on collaborative projects.\\nNow, imagine those problems you were solving\\nwere on something you care about.\\n\\nMalcolm Knowles, the grandfather of adult learning,\\nstated that for adults to care about what they are learning,\\nthey have to know why they need to learn it,\\nand the motivation is internal,\\nwhat is known as intrinsic motivation.\\nThat's why a one-size-fits-all approach fits no one.\\nAI can help create bespoke learning plans for you.\\nOnce you start using it,\\nit analyzes your past learning behaviors\\nand can suggest next steps.\\nFor example, if you want to learn a new language,\\nyou might have looked at the app Duolingo.\\n\\nThe program adjusts its difficulty level\\nbased on your accuracy and response time.\\nHow many times have you taken a LinkedIn Learning course\\nand then see a message that\\n\\\"Since you've liked these courses on lifelong learning,\\nyou might enjoy these as well.\\\"\\nIf you're ready to start creating personalized,\\nAI-driven learning plans, tailor-made just for you,\\nhere are a few you can try.\\nStep one, define your learning goals.\\nThink carefully and identify which skills\\nyou wish to develop.\\n\\nFor example, do you want to improve your leadership skills,\\ntime management, excel proficiency, or AI literacy?\\nStep two, select your AI tool\\nwhich best matches your needs.\\nFor example, you might use Perplexity for realtime research,\\nResearchRabbit for literature search,\\nor ChatGPT for a general search\\non recommended learning options.\\nStep three, automate and schedule learning.\\nSet up reminders through your calendar\\nand automated content delivery to seemingly integrate\\ninto your daily routines.\\n\\nDid you know that in LinkedIn Learning,\\nyou can tell it how many minutes per week\\nyou want to spend learning on the platform?\\nIt will then send you gentle nudges\\nwith reminders in your app and email to watch courses,\\nand it will let you know how many minutes of learning\\nyou need to achieve your goal.\\nYou might also want to sign up for newsletters\\nthat feed you tips on a programmed schedule.\\nAI can be your learning concierge,\\ndelivering the right content at the right time.\\n\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4108122\",\"duration\":188,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Strategies to find high-quality content\",\"fileName\":\"3980811_en_US_02_02_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":528,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"A one-size-fits-all learning model doesn't work; personalized learning is more effective. This approach reduces information overload and ensures that the learning is relevant.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":7894749,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- When I was in school getting my doctorate,\\nthe professors kept insisting that if you make a claim,\\nyou better back it up.\\nYou need evidence and citations. That was non-negotiable.\\nThat's why every book I write is cited heavily.\\nI used to put the information into AI\\nand ask it to pull the citation for me,\\nbut there was a big problem.\\nThe citations were wrong.\\nIt didn't pull the original thought leader,\\nthe year was wrong,\\nor the journal was not where the breakthrough idea\\nwas first introduced.\\n\\nI knew enough about the topic that I could tell it was off.\\nThat's why you can't believe everything you read on AI.\\nA study out of Columbia University tested eight chat bots\\nand noticed that AI had trouble finding original sources.\\nThey produced the wrong sources 60% of the time.\\nDo you get that?\\nIt was wrong over half the time.\\nSo trust, but verify.\\nAI has a pivotal strength.\\nIt can scan large volumes of data\\nand give you a summary within seconds,\\nbut, and this is a big but,\\nAI is not yet sophisticated enough to differentiate\\nbetween high-quality sources, such as reputable journals,\\nand low-quality sources,\\nsuch as someone's opinion on a blog on their website.\\n\\nHere are a few ways you can safeguard\\nagainst what's called hallucinated data\\nand strategically find high-quality content.\\nStep one, in your prompt, ask for citations.\\nAI will give you citations if you ask for it,\\nbut then it's up to you\\nto check the reliability of the source.\\nStep two, check the source.\\nMake sure AI is pulling from a reputable source,\\nsuch as websites and journals you've heard of\\nand are respected, such as Harvard Business Review,\\nofficial government websites,\\nand top-tier academic journals.\\n\\nIf AI provides statistics,\\nalways look for the original source,\\nmeaning the original study\\nwhere this statistic was pulled from.\\nStep three, compare your sources.\\nUse multiple AI tools such as ChatGPT or Google's DeepMind\\nto compare the information and sources.\\nStep four, train AI.\\nHave you heard the phrase garbage in, garbage out?\\nIf you want quality information,\\nyou need to train AI as to what you deem is acceptable.\\n\\nBe very specific in your inputs.\\nMake your prompts clear, specific, and contextual.\\nInstead of saying, \\\"Teach me about AI and upskilling,\\\"\\nprompt AI by saying,\\n\\\"What are three more in-demand skills\\nrequired by organizations in my industry?\\\"\\nTell it what industry it is.\\nAsk for a summary and specific sources.\\nAI is only as reliable as the content it curates.\\nCritical evaluation is essential.\\nThe next time AI provides information,\\nrun the three-step credibility check,\\nsource verification, cross-checking, and citation review,\\nbefore accepting it as fact.\\n\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4109135\",\"duration\":225,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Leveraging AI summaries, recommendations, and curation\",\"fileName\":\"3980811_en_US_02_03_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":288,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Learn how to differentiate between high-quality and low-quality, AI-curated content and implement strategies to consistently refine your discovery process. Being able to critically evaluate what is generated helps prevent misinformation and misuse.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":9062535,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- Have you ever experienced information overload?\\nThat feeling when there is so much information,\\nyou don't know where to start and what to do with it?\\nAI can help with that.\\nIt can take volumes of information\\nand organize it for you within any parameters you tell it:\\nthemes, timelines, people, you name it.\\nIt can even take information from various mediums, books,\\narticles, podcasts, and video, and curate it for you.\\nAs with any AI search,\\ncompare the summary with the original content,\\ncheck for any missing context or oversimplification,\\nand cross verify with other AI tools\\nto check for any inconsistencies.\\n\\nIf you want to maximize the benefits of AI-driven learning,\\ncreating a structured workflow will be incredibly helpful.\\nIt will curate high quality content\\nand ensure you are efficient in your retention\\nand application of the material.\\nHere's a workflow to help you get started.\\nStep one, identify what you need to learn.\\nDo you need to know the latest industry trends,\\nbreaking research on a topic, emerging leadership skills,\\nor a new technology?\\nFor example, prompt AI by writing:\\nI need to learn how to lead cross-functional teams\\nin a hybrid work environment.\\n\\nStep two, use AI for summation and curation.\\nAny AI tool like Recall.ai, Notion.ai,\\nand Elicit can all create bespoke learning plans\\nand summaries for you.\\nPrompt AI with create a learning plan\\nto help me become a more effective hybrid leader.\\nYou will likely get curated articles\\nfrom \\\"Harvard Business Review\\\" and \\\"Forbes,\\\"\\nsuggested videos, TED Talks,\\nand LinkedIn Learning courses.\\nIf you want to go deeper, add to your prompt:\\nfind peer-reviewed research studies on effective leadership\\nin hybrid organizations.\\n\\nThis will explain why the ideas work.\\nStep three, organize and retain knowledge.\\nYou will likely get more information than you need.\\nStore it in a way that you can pull it out later.\\nUse AI-powered note-taking tools, such as Roam Research,\\nto track and connect ideas.\\nCreate a workspace,\\nand title it something like Leading Hybrid Teams.\\nTag content by category, add notes,\\nand highlight action items.\\nStep four, reinforce your learning.\\n\\nTaking in information is a great first step,\\nbut to remember it, you have to use it.\\nConsider AI tools such as Quizlet to create quizzes\\nand flashcards based on your AI-curated summaries.\\nPrompt AI to give you weekly five-minute quizzes,\\ntrack what I know and what needs reinforcement.\\nI know this all sounds amazing,\\nbut there are a few things you should watch out for.\\nFirst, AI can make it too easy,\\nand as a result,\\nit can reduce your critical thinking skills.\\n\\nIf AI is going to compare and contrast everything for you,\\nyou'll stop using that muscle,\\nand you will quickly lose that essential skill.\\nIt is so prevalent that there's even a term for this,\\ncognitive offloading, where you delegate your thinking\\nand problem-solving skills solving.\\nYikes!\\nSecondly, be aware that AI can introduce bias depending\\non the dataset it's been trained on.\\nAs long as you keep these two caveats in mind,\\nyou'll be better equipped to find a sweet balance\\nbetween your cognitive overload and offload.\\n\\nAI-driven summaries can accelerate your learning,\\nbut critical analysis by you ensures\\ndeep retention and application.\\n\"}],\"name\":\"2. Curating the Right Learning with AI\",\"size\":23550841,\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentChapter:2051130\"},{\"duration\":488,\"entries\":[{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:2052125\",\"duration\":195,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"AI for memory retention\",\"fileName\":\"3980811_en_US_03_01_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":530,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Learn how to analyze AI-generated summaries and create a basic design of an AI-driven workflow to create, absorb, and retain key learning ideas. This technique can accelerate learning when used effectively to enhance, not replace, comprehension and critical thinking.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":7895430,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- You've likely heard of a learning curve,\\nthe rate it takes you to progress and gaining new skills,\\nbut have you heard of the forgetting curve?\\nThe forgetting curve means that memory retention\\ndecreases as time increases, and this happens fast.\\nWithin one hour, you likely forget\\n50% of the information that was presented to you.\\nWithin 24 hours, you've forgotten 70%,\\nand within a week, that number climbs to 90%.\\n\\nThat means that you are at risk\\nof losing all of the information you learned.\\nIf you don't use the information, you will lose it.\\nThe new knowledge needs to be reinforced and quickly.\\nAI can counteract some of the forgetting curve\\nby leveraging review strategies and strengthening recall.\\nAI can help with repetition.\\nIf you're learning a new concept,\\nAI tools such as Anki and SuperMemo\\ncan schedule reminders for you\\nto review the content before you are likely to forget.\\n\\nAI tools like Quizlet can create\\na personalized question bank\\nbased on notes or articles you provide.\\nAI can also help with visualization tools and mind maps\\nso that you can connect concepts visually.\\nHere's how you can do this.\\nStep one, convert your learning materials\\ninto AI-driven flashcards\\nwith tools such as Quizlet or BrainScape.\\nUpload your notes or articles\\nand get autogenerated flashcards\\nthat you can use anytime from waiting in line or commuting.\\n\\nStep two, set up a repetition schedule.\\nRemember, the longer you wait, the more you will forget.\\nSo, use an AI tool such as RemNote or Anki\\nto remind you to interact with the material.\\nIt can adjust it based on your timing and performance.\\nStep three, prompt AI to give you real-world applications.\\nGetting a bunch of information is one thing,\\nbut knowing how to apply it, is higher order thinking.\\nPrompt AI chatbots such as Claude or ChatGPT\\nto give you case studies based on real-world scenarios\\nfrom your industry.\\n\\nStep four, automate your knowledge reinforcement.\\nIf you think you'll remember\\nsome nuanced piece of information, chances are you won't.\\nTools such as RewindAI can help curate\\neverything you've seen, learned, and heard\\nand resurface the main points when relevant.\\nPerhaps my favorite and most overlooked way of using AI\\nis to help you repurpose what you've learned.\\nAI can highlight past learning\\nwhen you're working on a new project\\nso that you are naturally reinforcing retention.\\n\\nSimply give it a prompt to utilize\\na previous learning into your new project,\\nand you're on your way to retaining that information.\\nRetaining knowledge requires strategic reinforcement,\\nand AI makes this process efficient and usable.\\nDon't worry about learning five different AI tools.\\nStart with one and then progress.\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4106100\",\"duration\":149,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Using AI for active learning\",\"fileName\":\"3980811_en_US_03_02_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":183,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Learn how to apply AI-based memory retention techniques. Recalling information when it's most needed helps you to apply knowledge, rather than store it or forget it shortly after learning the material.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":7050787,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- In adult learning,\\nthere is a concept called the Banking Theory\\ndeveloped by Paulo Freire.\\nHe stated that if a professor\\nis standing in front of the room lecturing,\\nthey are making deposits of knowledge into your brain.\\nBut if the knowledge is not organized\\ninto separate folders within your brain,\\nyou will have trouble finding and recalling it\\nwhen you need it.\\nWhat Paulo Freire is explaining is the difference\\nbetween passive and active learning.\\n\\nPassive learning methods like lectures and reading\\nhave lower retention rates, hovering around 10%.\\nThe more active learning approaches,\\nsuch as discussions, active practice, and teaching others\\ndramatically improves retention to 75 to 90%.\\nAI can bridge the gap by making learning interactive,\\nengaging, and application-driven so that you can\\nmore easily recall and apply the information.\\n\\nFor example, AI can help you generate discussion and debate.\\nYou can ask AI to be your conversation partner,\\nor roleplay in exercise.\\nThis can help you defend or refine your arguments.\\nThat's why I was so excited when LinkedIn Learning\\nintroduced AI-driven roleplay into some of their courses,\\nincluding some which I teach.\\nAI can also create realistic workplace scenarios\\nto apply your learning.\\n\\nFor example, you might be learning\\na new leadership communication skill,\\nand AI can generate\\na simulated difficult conversation for you.\\nAI can also generate a real world case study for you,\\nand you can go back and forth with AI\\nas you attempt various solutions.\\nYou can also learn the concepts by teaching them.\\nSummarize a topic and have AI provide feedback\\nor probing questions.\\nPrompt AI to challenge you.\\n\\nFinally, you can have group discussions\\nwhere AI creates a question which allows the group\\nto brainstorm and come up with use case scenarios.\\nEndless research has shown that active learning\\nimproves comprehension, recall, and application.\\nAI can enhance this process\\nby making learning interactive and dynamic.\\nSelect one active learning strategy and get started.\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:2051129\",\"duration\":144,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Tracking progress with AI\",\"fileName\":\"3980811_en_US_03_03_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":204,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Learn how to evaluate and differentiate between active and passive learning and create an active learning model that enhances your ability to apply the learned material. Active engagement with the learned material helps with understanding, recall, and the ability to use the material in the right setting.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":6907673,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- Did you know that people\\nwho track their learning progress\\nare three times more likely\\nto improve their skill retention as compared\\nto those who did not?\\nThis is important because most people engage in learning\\nwithout tracking their progress and what happens?\\nThis leads to a lack of motivation, forgotten skills,\\nand difficulty in applying knowledge.\\nAI can help by providing automated tracking,\\ninsights and reminders to ensure continuous improvement.\\n\\nAI features, such as those on LinkedIn Learning\\nalready provide personalized progress reports.\\nIf you've set a learning goal of how much time you want\\nto learn each week, I'm sure you've\\ngotten an encouraging email from LinkedIn\\nabout how close you are\\nto achieving your weekly goal,\\nor what new courses you might be interested in\\nbased on the areas you expressed interest in.\\nThere are countless AI tools that help you set\\nand track your learning milestones\\nand suggest ways to reinforce your knowledge,\\nso you don't forget!\\nHere's how you can get started.\\n\\nAs always, it starts with\\ndefining your learning goals and outcomes.\\nWhat do you want to learn?\\nWhat will improvement look like\\nand when do you want to achieve this goal?\\nSecond, use AI to track your daily and weekly progress.\\nCheck out Google Keep and Notion AI to track\\nand reflect on your completed tasks.\\nThird, use your favorite AI platform to set up milestones\\nand feedback loops.\\nHave it track the completion of your courses\\nand recommend real world application exercises.\\n\\nFinally, evaluate and adjust based on insights.\\nAI is masterful at analyzing your learning patterns\\nand suggesting adjustments.\\nIt can see if and where you are struggling\\nand offer more interactive exercises to try.\\nTracking your progress is not just\\nto earn a gold star when you complete a task.\\nAI converts what could be a passive consumption\\ninto a measurable, structured, and actionable tool.\\n\\nYou don't want to lose this knowledge.\\nYou want it to stick with you.\\nAs Peter Drucker famously said,\\n\\\"What gets measured gets managed.\\\"\\nSo, go start measuring your progress.\\n\"}],\"name\":\"3. Retaining Knowledge\",\"size\":21853890,\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentChapter:4108124\"},{\"duration\":490,\"entries\":[{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:2052123\",\"duration\":201,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Build good learning habits\",\"fileName\":\"3980811_en_US_04_01_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":293,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Learn how to design a plan to track progress and set milestones. Tracking and implementing what you learn helps ensure that you apply that knowledge in real-world scenarios.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":8679793,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- The last thing you want to do is forget most\\nof what you learned.\\nWell, if you do nothing\\nwith the information you just consumed,\\nI hate to break it to you, but you'll likely forget it.\\nTo improve your return on your learning investment,\\ntry microlearning.\\nYou see, what you do\\nafter you learn the material might be more important\\nthan what you do while learning it.\\nMultiple research studies have shown\\nthat microlearning improves focus, retention,\\nrecall, confidence in material,\\nand long-term memory support.\\n\\nIt also reduces cognitive overload.\\nForget cramming.\\nMastery is not about how much information you can consume\\nat once.\\nIt's about how you consistently engage with the learning\\nover time.\\nAI can help you build good learning habits\\nto ensure you steadily progress.\\nAs always, your first step should be\\nto identify your learning goal.\\nLet AI know what you want to master.\\nIs it communication skills, delegating skills,\\nor developing effective leadership in turbulent times?\\nBe specific.\\n\\nSecond, implement microlearning with AI.\\nUse AI to break topics into short, digestible lessons\\nwhich are better for retention.\\nConsider this prompt.\\nBreak down the topic of managing hybrid teams into a series\\nof short, five minute lessons I can learn\\nover the next seven days.\\nInclude a key concept, a quick example, and a reflection\\nor action step for each day.\\nThird, prompt AI to practice implementing these skills\\nwith you.\\n\\nTry different scenarios.\\nHere's a suggested prompt.\\nAct as a team member on my hybrid team.\\nI'm the team leader, and I want\\nto practice addressing performance concerns\\nduring a virtual one-on-one meeting.\\nRole play it with me.\\nPlease respond as the team member would.\\nMake him increasingly frustrated,\\nand give me feedback afterwards\\non how I could improve the handling of the conversation.\\nFourth, use AI to automate learning prompts,\\nschedule learning sprints, reminders, and learning paths.\\n\\nFor example, create a two week learning sprint\\nfor me on leading hybrid teams.\\nBreak it into daily 15 minute tasks.\\nInclude links to curated content, rapid reflection prompts,\\nand reminders for review days.\\nFormat it like a calendar I can follow.\\nFinally, track your progress and adjust accordingly.\\nIf it's too easy, prompt AI for more challenges.\\nIf you have information overload, ask AI\\nto break it down further.\\n\\nCommit to a set amount of time each day for your learning,\\ndoing it while you are doing something else.\\nWhat I call making time in time is helpful.\\nI like to learn something new during my commute.\\nI ask AI to generate articles and podcasts\\non a particular topic I want to learn about\\nduring a one hour commute.\\nUltimately, consistent AI powered learning leads to mastery,\\nand your professional growth.\\nTake that first step.\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4103137\",\"duration\":168,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Staying ahead as AI evolves\",\"fileName\":\"3980811_en_US_04_02_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":484,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Learn how to develop useful learning habits that help you achieve your learning goals and develop professionally. Learning small amounts consistently, rather than attempting to learn large amounts in bursts, leads to better recall, use, and mastery of the material.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":8261084,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- If I had a dollar\\nfor every time someone told me they will get replaced by AI,\\nI'd be a very wealthy woman.\\nBut lost jobs are only half the story.\\nThe World Economic Forum stated\\nin their 2025 Future of Jobs Report\\nthat \\\"while 85 million jobs will be displaced by automation,\\n97 million new roles will emerge.\\\"\\nThis underscores the fact that we need a workforce\\nthat can adapt, re-skill,\\nand learn to use AI\\nbecause AI is transforming industries\\nat record-breaking speed,\\nand those who don't continuously adapt\\nwill risk losing their jobs.\\n\\nSo what does staying ahead look like?\\nIt means proactively evolving your skills,\\nleveraging AI for real-time learning\\nand being ready for new opportunities.\\nThe half-life of skills is shrinking.\\nWhat was cutting-edge five years ago may be obsolete today.\\nHere are some ways you can stay ahead as AI evolves.\\nFirst, stay on top of AI trends in your sector.\\n\\nSet up Google Alerts for AI in your industry\\nor emerging AI skills in your industry.\\nSecond, consider and make note\\nof which transferable skills you have,\\nsuch as critical thinking, adaptability, and leadership,\\nthat will remain relevant and needed\\nregardless of AI advancements.\\nThink about how you can use and showcase those skills\\nas the workplace and workforce evolves.\\nThird, audit and update your learning goals.\\n\\nRead reports such as the LinkedIn Workplace Learning Report\\nto identify in-demand skills,\\nand consider adjusting your learning plans\\nin a way that aligns with your interests\\nand the future of work.\\nFourth, identify any gaps\\nor areas for enhancement you could focus your learning on.\\nFinally, practice, practice, practice.\\nUse AI-powered projects, simulations,\\nand role-playing exercises\\nto apply your learning in real-case scenarios.\\n\\nThis way, when it comes up, you're ready.\\nYou need to be nimble and comfortable with change.\\nAI will evolve, and so should you.\\nTreat learning as a habit, not a one-time effort.\\nRemember, AI is powerful,\\nbut human insight and experience remain irreplaceable.\\nAs a first step, I encourage you\\nto identify one AI-powered emerging trend in your industry\\nand commit to reviewing it weekly.\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:2052124\",\"duration\":121,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Using AI to enhance human connection\",\"fileName\":\"3980811_en_US_04_03_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":232,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Learn how to analyze trends in AI learning and be nimble in your adaptation of strategies so that they can remain relevant in this fast-changing world. Technology is advancing rapidly, and you'll have to update your skills in real time. Doing so can give you a competitive edge.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":5146237,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- I do a lot of executive coaching\\nand one recurring theme is that no matter their career,\\nindustry, or rank, people are lonely\\nand crave human connection.\\nThat's not just me saying it.\\nThe US Surgeon General put out an entire report\\non what he called the Loneliness Epidemic.\\nThere's no question\\nthat AI can improve efficiency and productivity,\\nbut AI cannot replace the growing need\\nand desire for human connection.\\n\\nAI has its strengths,\\nit can process a huge amount of information quickly\\nand does repetitive tasks for you, but it also has limits.\\nIt lacks emotional intelligence\\nand the ability to fully understand human motivation.\\nSo how can you use AI\\nand still get the human connection you need?\\nFirst, find a mentor, a human one.\\nUse AI to gather insights and organize your talking points\\nbefore you meet with your mentor.\\n\\nSecond, use AI to gather information on a topic\\nand then ask your mentor for their perspective\\nso that you can leverage their context and wisdom.\\nThe mentor should help you make sense of the information.\\nThird, if you are meeting with your mentor,\\nuse AI to take meeting notes, summarize them,\\nand give you an action list.\\nYou focus on the conversation.\\nFinally, ask AI to handle the administrative tasks\\nsuch as note taking and scheduling,\\nso that you can have more time for mentoring\\nand human interactions.\\n\\nAI helps with learning,\\nbut human relationships offer wisdom.\\nPrioritize mentorship and peer learning,\\nand regularly engage with your mentors and colleagues.\\nAI can certainly enhance and make your learning efficient,\\nbut human connection makes it meaningful.\\nThe best learners use a mixed approach\\nof both AI and mentorship.\\n\"}],\"name\":\"4. Future-Proof Your AI-Powered Learning\",\"size\":22087114,\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentChapter:4109136\"},{\"duration\":247,\"entries\":[{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4107112\",\"duration\":125,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Reflecting on the role of AI in lifelong learning\",\"fileName\":\"3980811_en_US_05_01_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":329,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Learn how to use both human connections through mentorship and AI to enhance your learning and critical thinking. While AI is extremely powerful, it is the human relationships that pick up on nuances, feelings, and emotions, and can guide you long-term.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":6871594,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- According to a study by PwC, by 2030,\\nAI is expected to contribute $15.7 trillion\\nto the global economy.\\nThat's trillion with a T.\\nAn enormous impact on education\\nand workforce development is expected.\\nLook, AI is not some vision far into the future.\\nIt's here now and completely re-imagining how we learn,\\nwork, and professionally develop.\\nThere's no question that those who embrace AI\\nwill stay ahead.\\n\\nWhile those who ignore it, risk falling behind.\\nAI has enormous benefit over traditional learning models.\\nYou see, adults take in and process information differently.\\nSome like to hear lectures, other prefer reading quietly.\\nThere are those who prefer to watch videos,\\nand there are those who like to roll up their sleeves\\nand try applying the knowledge as they are learning it.\\nThose are all correct options.\\nThere is no right answer,\\njust different variations of normal.\\n\\nYou don't need to settle for passive learning.\\nYou can now partake in active learning.\\nYou are in the driver's seat now,\\nbut that's just the beginning.\\nAI can summarize the information for you,\\nhelp you reinforce your learning through quizzes\\nand repetition, and send you nudges to keep going.\\nAI can't replace human guidance\\nand is void of emotional intelligence.\\nIt works based on past experiences.\\nWhile it can give you career guidance,\\nit is the human mentor that can offer nuanced\\nand contextual advice.\\n\\nAI is constantly evolving\\nand will become more and more woven into education\\nand professional development.\\nIt's not if, it's when.\\nIt's coming, you can count on it.\\nAI is an enhancement, the ultimate accelerator\\nthat empowers lifelong learners who want to upskill.\\nAre you ready to get started?\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:4106099\",\"duration\":122,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Resources\",\"fileName\":\"3980811_en_US_05_02_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":270,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Review key takeaways and explore how AI is a useful and powerful tool to enhance lifelong learning.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":6970587,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- Congratulations, you did it.\\nYou finished the course,\\nbut I like to think that the end of one thing\\nis the beginning of another.\\nI know that you are a lifelong learner\\nand take upskilling seriously,\\nit's why you selected and watched this course.\\nI want to leave you with some additional resources\\nso that you can enhance your learning\\nwhen you choose to do so.\\nAnd since I told you that\\nadults take in and process information differently,\\nI am sharing resources in various mediums,\\nso pick what works best for you.\\n\\nIf you are interested in any of the topics we discuss today,\\nsuch as professional development,\\nleadership development, AI, or mentoring,\\nI have several additional LinkedIn Learning courses\\nthat you can watch,\\njust click on my name below the course player\\nto see all of my other courses.\\nIf you prefer long form reading or listening,\\nlook into my two books,\\n\\\"The Success Factor,\\\"\\nand \\\"Financial Times Guide to Mentoring.\\\"\\nIf you prefer shorter form reading,\\nI have hundreds of articles on these topics\\nin Harvard Business Review,\\nFast Company, Forbes,\\nPsychology Today, and many other journals.\\n\\nIf you want bite-sized information\\nwhere I teach one topic each time\\nand give you an action plan,\\nI have two newsletters you can subscribe to.\\nOne is my LinkedIn Learning newsletter\\ncalled \\\"The Success Factor,\\\"\\nand the other is on my website, ruthgotian.com,\\nwhere you will find lots of other resources,\\nincluding assessments, articles and scorecards,\\nboth share completely different information.\\nSo if you're committed to your professional development,\\nfeel free to sign up for both.\\n\\nI hope you'll follow me on LinkedIn\\nas I share professional development tips\\nseveral times a week.\\nAnd if you found value in this course,\\nI encourage you to share it on your LinkedIn\\nso people can see that you are committed to your growth.\\nHappy learning.\\n\"}],\"name\":\"Conclusion\",\"size\":13842181,\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentChapter:4107114\"}],\"size\":110514096,\"duration\":2406,\"zeroBased\":false},{\"course_title\":\"Workforce Skill-Building with AI\",\"course_admin_id\":5960110,\"metadata\":{\"Locale\":\"en_US\",\"Course ID\":5960110,\"Project ID\":null,\"Course Name\":\"Workforce Skill-Building with AI\",\"Course Name EN\":\"Workforce Skill-Building with AI\",\"Activation Status\":\"ACTIVE\",\"Display to Public\":\"Yes\",\"Display to QA\":\"No\",\"Course Description\":\"Learn how to use AI to help solve the challenge of organizational skill-building. By first recognizing the gap in skills needed by every organization to remain competitive,   Margie Meacham reveals how to use AI to help address some of these challenges, such as identifying the skills gap, mapping skills to roles, developing personalized learning plans, and how employees can develop power skills. Finally, Margie discusses bias in AI and how to mitigate it as well as leadership's role in fostering AI-driven organizational change.\",\"Course Short Description\":\"Use AI to identify the exact skills needed to be successful in a particular role.\",\"Content Type\":\"SKILLS\",\"Localization Type\":\"ORIGINAL\",\"Original Course Locale\":null,\"Original Course ID\":null,\"Equivalent English Course\":null,\"Instructor ID\":20889000,\"Instructor Name\":\"Margie Meacham\",\"Instructor Transliterated Name\":null,\"Instructor Short Bio\":\"Founder and Chief Freedom Officer, Learningtogo\",\"Author Payment Category\":\"NON-LICENSED\",\"Delivery Mode\":\"ALL_AT_ONCE\",\"Series End Date\":null,\"Course Release Date\":\"2025-01-08T00:00:00\",\"Course Updated Date\":null,\"Course Archive Date\":null,\"Course Retire Date\":null,\"Replacement Course\":null,\"Has Assessment\":\"No\",\"Has Challenge/Solution\":\"No\",\"LIL URL\":\"https://www.linkedin.com/learning/workforce-skill-building-with-ai\",\"Series\":\"Deep Dive (X:Y)\",\"Limited Series\":null,\"Manager Level\":\"Senior Manager\",\"LI Level\":\"Advanced\",\"LI Level EN\":\"Advanced\",\"Sensitivity\":null,\"Internal Library\":\"Business\",\"Internal Subject\":\"HR\",\"Primary Software\":null,\"Media Type\":\"Video\",\"Has CEU\":\"No\",\"Has Exercise Files\":\"Yes\",\"Visible Duration\":5956.0,\"Visible Video Count\":22.0,\"Learning Objectives\":\"Identify the gap between today's skills and the needs of tomorrow.,Forecast the skills of tomorrow's workforce.,Build personalized learning plans with AI.,Identify bias in skills management.,Nurture skills leadership.,Build power skills using AI.\",\"Contract Type\":\"PERPETUAL\"},\"sections\":[{\"duration\":48,\"entries\":[{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:2133167\",\"duration\":48,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":null,\"name\":\"The gap between today's skills and the needs of tomorrow\",\"fileName\":\"5960110_en_US_00_01_VT\",\"demo\":true,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":193,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"editingNotes\":\"Use TK2\",\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Adopting a skills mindset to talent development requires a new skillset for the talent professional. The ability to formulate a personal vision of recruiting, engaging, and managing skills in the workplace is essential so that powerful AI tools can be leveraged to bring that vision to life. In this video, learn how to apply your own values and priorities to choose AI tools so that you can lead the skills approach through example and best practices.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":2785940,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":true,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- Imagine your organization\\nstanding on the edge of a chasm.\\nOn the other side lies the future.\\nA landscape transformed by AI\\nand rapidly evolving technologies.\\nBut the skills that brought us here\\nwon't be enough to get us there.\\nThe gap is widening and we need to build a bridge fast.\\nI'm Margie Meacham, and this course\\nis your blueprint for that bridge.\\nWe'll explore how AI is reshaping recruitment,\\nemployee engagement, performance management,\\nand skill development.\\n\\nAre you ready to start building?\\nLet's bridge the gap between today and tomorrow,\\nensuring that your organization\\ndoesn't just survive the AI revolution, it leads it.\\n\"}],\"name\":\"Introduction\",\"size\":2785940,\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentChapter:5212002\"},{\"duration\":918,\"entries\":[{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:5211212\",\"duration\":328,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Why skills matter in the modern organization\",\"fileName\":\"5960110_en_US_01_01_VT\",\"demo\":true,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":661,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"In a climate of rapid change, the status quo organization struggles to remain competitive and loses sight of essential skills that are needed to adapt to and benefit from disruptive change. In this video, learn how to foster a skills focus to talent development, accelerated by AI tools and human insight, so that you can help the organization leverage technology by developing the skills of tomorrow today.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":14254249,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- Philosopher Eric Hoffer once said\\nthat, \\\"In a world of rapid change,\\nthe educated find themselves perfectly equipped\\nto deal with a world that no longer exists.\\\"\\nThis quote resonates deeply\\nwith the challenges facing modern organizations,\\nparticularly in talent development.\\nLet me share a story that illustrates this point.\\nMeet Sarah, an experienced talent development manager\\nat a large tech company, Red30 Tech.\\nFor years, Sarah has expertly crafted curricula\\nfor new employees,\\nensuring that they have the knowledge\\nand abilities needed to excel in their roles.\\n\\nBut this year, as Sarah sits down to plan,\\nshe realizes something is different.\\nMany roles now require proficiency with AI tools,\\na trend that's only accelerating.\\nMarketing needs to understand AI-driven analytics.\\nCustomer service is implementing AI chatbots,\\nand even HR is exploring AI for resume screening.\\nSo Sarah finds herself in a dilemma.\\nHow can she plan a curriculum\\nwhen the required skills are rapidly evolving?\\nHow can she prepare employees for tools and technologies\\nthat might not even exist yet?\\nThis is where the focus on skills becomes crucial.\\n\\nA skill is a measurable ability to perform a specific task\\nor set of tasks that contributes value to an organization.\\nBut it's so much more than just technical proficiency,\\nit encompasses cognitive abilities,\\nsocial competencies, and adaptive capacities\\nthat enable an individual to effectively navigate\\nand contribute in an evolving AI-driven workplace.\\n\\nLet's use the bridge metaphor again.\\nWe're standing on the cliff of today,\\nlooking across to the misty uncertain future.\\nThe bridge we need to build isn't made of concrete facts\\nor specific tool knowledge.\\nThose might be outdated before we even finish construction.\\nInstead, our bridge is built with skills,\\nflexible, adaptable building blocks\\nthat can be reconfigured as the landscape changes.\\n\\nBy focusing on core skills like critical thinking,\\nadaptability, digital literacy, and continuous learning,\\nwe create a foundation\\nthat can support whatever specific knowledge\\nor tool the future requires.\\nWe're not just teaching employees\\nhow to use today's AI tools,\\nwe're cultivating their ability to understand,\\nadapt to, and leverage any new technology that comes along.\\nThis skills-focused approach\\ndoesn't solve all of Sarah's problems,\\nbut it does provide a framework for moving forward.\\n\\nIt allows her to design a curriculum that prepares employees\\nnot just for the known challenges of today,\\nbut for the unknown opportunities of tomorrow.\\nIn our rapidly changing world,\\nit's these skills that truly matter now,\\nand will lay the foundation of the bridge\\nthat carries your organization safely into the future.\\nNow it's time to pause the video\\nand complete a short practice activity.\\n\\nThis exercise will help you envision the skills bridge\\nbetween today and tomorrow.\\nHere's what you're going to do.\\nTake out a sheet of paper or open a digital document.\\nDraw a line down the middle, creating two columns.\\nLabel the left column today's world\\nand the right column future world,\\nsay 5-10 years ahead.\\nIn the today's world column,\\nlist 5-7 key skills\\nthat are currently in high demand\\nin your organization or industry.\\n\\nIn the future world column,\\nimagine the landscape 5-10 years from now.\\nConsider advancements in AI,\\nchanging work environments, and evolving business needs,\\nand list 5-7 skills you believe will be crucial\\nin the future scenario.\\nNow draw lines connecting related skills\\nfrom today's world to the future world.\\nThese connections represent your skills bridge.\\nReflect on the following questions,\\nwhat new skills appear in the future world column?\\nWhat current skills might become less important?\\nWhat core competencies remain valuable across both columns?\\nAnd how can you start developing\\nthe future world skills today?\\nBased on your reflection,\\nnow identify three skills you believe are most critical\\nto develop or strengthen to prepare for the future.\\n\\nYou should take about 5-10 minutes\\nto complete this activity.\\nThis exercise will help you start thinking\\nabout the skills bridge your organization needs to build.\\nRetain the results of your reflection\\nbecause we'll continue to build on these ideas\\nthroughout the rest of the course.\\nWhen you're satisfied with your vision,\\nhead to the next video to continue our exploration\\nof skills development in the age of AI.\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:5210164\",\"duration\":272,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"The gap analysis: Identifying critical skills for success\",\"fileName\":\"5960110_en_US_01_02_VT\",\"demo\":true,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":721,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"One of the risks of new technology is the temptation to follow the trend, simply because everyone else is doing it. In this video, learn how to scan your own environment so that you can identify and focus on the skills needed to ensure individual and organizational success.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":9547612,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- Welcome back to our journey of building the skills bridge.\\nIn our last session,\\nwe explored why skills matter in the modern organization.\\nNow, let's focus on a crucial step in bridge construction,\\nthe gap analysis.\\nImagine our skills bridge spanning from today to the future.\\nThe gap analysis is like a structural survey,\\nidentifying where our bridge is solid\\nand where it needs reinforcement.\\nIt's a systematic process\\nof determining the difference between the skills we have now\\nand the skills we'll need to succeed in the future.\\n\\nLet's break down the steps to perform a skills gap analysis.\\nStep one, define future goals.\\nClearly articulate your organization's future objectives.\\nStep two, identify future skills.\\nDetermine the skills needed to achieve these goals.\\nStep three, assess current skills.\\nTake stock of the skills your workforce currently possesses.\\nStep four, analyze the gaps.\\nCompare current skills to future needs\\nto identify discrepancies.\\n\\nAnd step five, prioritize skills development.\\nFocus on the most critical skills gaps first.\\nLet's see these steps in action.\\nIn our previous video, we met Sarah,\\nan experienced talent development manager\\nat a large tech company.\\nSarah needs to develop a new plan\\nthat will help her organization develop the new skills\\ndemanded by the explosion of new tools\\nthat leverage artificial intelligence.\\nHere's how she used these same steps\\nto plan her gap analysis.\\n\\nSarah met with senior leaders and other stakeholders\\nto help her identify her company's technology roadmap\\nfor the next five years,\\nfocusing on how technology will support\\nthe organization's strategies and goals.\\nThen, Sarah took this information to her team\\nand matched these goals to the future skills\\nthat will be needed to achieve them.\\nNext, Sarah implemented two surveys to complete this task.\\nOne survey asked each leader\\nto evaluate their current team\\nin terms of those future skills that will be needed\\nto support the organization's vision of the future.\\n\\nThe second survey asked individuals\\nto rate themselves on this same set of skills.\\nSarah then compared the results of the two surveys\\nusing an AI assistant to help her detect\\nwhere leaders and their teams\\nagree and disagree on their current abilities.\\nFinally, Sarah returned to her panel\\nof senior leaders and stakeholders\\nto present her findings,\\nand together, they identified a set of foundational skills\\nthat must be developed first,\\nfollowed by more advanced skills that will be needed later.\\n\\nRemember, the skills identified\\nwill vary depending on your organization and its people.\\nSo for example, what's critical for a tech startup\\nmight differ from what's needed in a manufacturing firm.\\nTo make the most of your gap analysis,\\nconsider these best practices.\\nInvolve diverse stakeholders in the process,\\nuse both quantitative and qualitative data,\\nand regularly update your analysis as the landscape evolves.\\n\\nYou also need to watch out for these common pitfalls.\\nFocusing only on technical skills\\nwhile ignoring soft skills,\\noverlooking emerging skills\\nthat aren't yet in high demand,\\nand assuming all employees need the same skill set.\\nTo help you get started,\\nI've provided a gap analysis template\\nin the course materials.\\nAfter this video,\\ntake some time to process this template\\nand begin a preliminary gap analysis for your organization.\\n\\nRemember, this analysis is your blueprint\\nfor building a robust skills bridge.\\nIt will guide your talent development strategies,\\nensuring that your organization is prepared\\nfor whatever the future holds.\\nIn our next video, we'll explore how to use the results\\nof your gap analysis\\nto create targeted skill development plans\\nby using AI-enabled tools.\\nUntil then, happy analyzing.\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:2133166\",\"duration\":318,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Leveraging AI for efficient gap analysis\",\"fileName\":\"5960110_en_US_01_03_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":642,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"handoutNotes\":\"Activity 1.3 Comparing AI-Enabled Tools.pdf\",\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Choosing AI tools can be overwhelming, given the explosion of vendors and models available. In this video, learn how to select from available AI tools by applying a methodical series of questions to find the right tool so you can conduct an effective skills gap analysis for your organization.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":16027821,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- In our last video,\\nwe introduced the concept of a skills gap analysis,\\na crucial step in identifying the skills\\nyour organization needs to thrive in the future.\\nNow, let's explore how we can harness the power of AI\\nto streamline this process,\\nmaking it more efficient and insightful.\\nAI can transform each step of your gap analysis.\\nLet's take a closer look. Step one, data collection.\\nAI powered surveys and chatbots\\ncan gather information from employees\\nabout their current skills and career aspirations.\\n\\nThese tools can adapt questions based on responses,\\nproviding deeper insights.\\nFor example, a large tech company uses an AI chatbot\\nto conduct skills assessments.\\nThe chatbot asks engineers about their proficiency\\nin various programming languages\\nand adapts its questions based on their responses,\\ndiving deeper into areas where they claim expertise.\\nStep two, skills mapping.\\nNatural language processing can analyze job descriptions,\\nperformance reviews, and industry reports\\nto identify emerging skills\\nand map them to your organization's rules.\\n\\nFor example, one multinational corporation uses AI\\nto analyze thousands of job postings across its industry.\\nThe AI identifies trending skills\\nlike data visualization and agile project management,\\nhelping HR update job descriptions and training programs\\naccordingly to remain competitive in the marketplace.\\nStep three, data analysis.\\nMachine learning algorithms\\ncan process vast amounts of data,\\nidentifying patterns and trends\\nthat might be missed by human analysts.\\n\\nThey can predict future skill needs\\nbased on market trends and your organization's trajectory.\\nUsing these techniques,\\na consulting firm uses AI to analyze client projects,\\nemployee performance data, and industry forecast.\\nThe AI, for example, predicted a growing need\\nfor blockchain expertise in financial consulting,\\nallowing the firm to proactively upskill their consultants.\\nStep four, report generation.\\n\\nAI can compile the analyzed data\\ninto comprehensive, visually appealing reports,\\ntailored to different stakeholders,\\nfrom executive summaries\\nto detailed departmental breakdowns.\\nThe training department for a retail company\\nuses their proprietary AI system\\nto generate monthly skills gap reports, for example.\\nFor the CEO, it provides a high level overview\\nof critical skills gaps across the organization.\\nFor the head of customer service,\\nit offers a detailed analysis of skills needed\\nto implement new omnichannel support strategies.\\n\\nAnd step five, personalized recommendations.\\nAI can suggest personalized learning paths for employees\\nbased on their current skills\\nand your organization's future needs.\\nSo a pharmaceutical company's AI powered learning platform\\nanalyzes each employee's current skills,\\nrole requirements, and career aspirations.\\nIt then recommends tailored learning paths,\\nsuggesting specific courses\\non emerging biotechnologies for researchers\\nand leadership development programs\\nfor high potential managers.\\n\\nBy leveraging AI in these ways,\\nyou can conduct more frequent in-depth analysis\\nwithout overburdening your human team.\\nThis allows for a more agile approach to skill development,\\nhelping your organization stay ahead of the curve,\\nand stay on top of emerging trends\\nand changes in your industry.\\nNow it's time for you to explore AI tools for gap analysis.\\nAfter this video, complete the following activity.\\n\\nFirst, research three AI powered tools\\ndesigned for skills assessment or workforce analytics.\\nYou can choose from the list provided for this activity,\\nor find these tools on your own.\\nSecond, for each tool list its key features\\nand how it could enhance your gap analysis process.\\nThird, consider your organization's\\nspecific needs and constraints.\\nWhich tool seems most suitable and why?\\nThis exercise will help you start thinking concretely\\nabout how to implement AI in your gap analysis process.\\n\\nHowever, remember that AI is a tool,\\nnot a replacement for human insight.\\nYour expertise in interpreting results\\nand making strategic decisions remains crucial\\nso that you can identify the right skills\\nand the most effective strategies for building a bridge\\nto those skills for your organization.\\nWhen you're ready, head to the next video.\\nWe'll discuss how to use your insights\\nto drive your skill development strategy.\\n\\n\"}],\"name\":\"1. What Skills Matter and Why\",\"size\":39829682,\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentChapter:2135002\"},{\"duration\":962,\"entries\":[{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:2132169\",\"duration\":350,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Skills pipeline strategies\",\"fileName\":\"5960110_en_US_02_01_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":703,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"In a world where skills are emerging and evolving rapidly, traditional methods of recruiting employees may not meet current needs. A robust and dynamic pipeline, constructed to acquire skills, rather than headcount, is essential to navigate this new environment. In this video, learn how to choose from several effective pipeline strategies so you can plan how your organization will maintain a robust pipeline of candidates with varied and targeted skills.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":16080460,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- Developing your skills pipeline strategy\\nis a crucial component in building your AI skills bridge.\\nAs we construct this bridge\\nto lead today's talent to tomorrow's skills,\\nwe need to ensure a steady flow of capable individuals\\nready and willing to cross it with us.\\nSo think of your skills pipeline as the scaffolding\\nthat supports your bridge building efforts,\\nproviding stability\\nand resources as you work towards the future.\\n\\nIn today's rapidly evolving business landscape,\\ntraditional talent acquisition methods often fall short.\\nWe need innovative pipeline strategies\\nthat not only fill immediate gaps,\\nbut also prepare our workforce for the challenges ahead.\\nLet's explore three effective pipeline strategies\\nthat maintain a human-centered approach\\nto talent development.\\nFirst, focus on skills-based hiring.\\n\\nThis strategy focuses on a candidate's abilities\\nrather than their formal qualifications or job history.\\nIt's like selecting the right materials for your bridge\\nbased on their strength and flexibility,\\nnot just their appearance.\\nFor example, a tech company might hire\\na self-taught programmer\\nwith an impressive portfolio of projects,\\neven if they lack a computer science degree.\\nThis approach widens your talent pool\\nand often leads to more diverse\\nand capable, adaptable teams.\\n\\nAI can enhance this strategy\\nby using natural language processing\\nto analyze resumes and portfolios,\\nidentifying relevant skills that might be overlooked\\nby organizations employing\\na more traditional screening process.\\nWhile skills-based hiring is very effective\\nin widening the external pool of candidates,\\nmany organizations will have better luck\\nfinding their best candidates\\nwith an internal talent marketplace.\\n\\nThese platforms allow employees\\nto explore and apply for different roles\\nor projects within the organization.\\nIt's like repurposing materials from one part of your bridge\\nto strengthen another.\\nSo imagine a large retailer creating an internal platform\\nwhere employees can volunteer for short-term projects\\noutside their usual roles.\\nAI can support this process\\nby using machine learning algorithms\\nto match employees' skills and interests\\nwith available projects,\\neven suggesting development opportunities\\nthey might not have considered.\\n\\nOur third strategy is a modernized apprenticeship program.\\nNow apprenticeship was a means in the Middle Ages\\nfor a commoner to learn a trade,\\nand this modernized strategy, on the job training,\\ncombines with formal education,\\nensuring that graduates enter the workforce\\nwith a combination of academic\\nand practical expertise in their field.\\nThis approach allows the employer\\nto create a steady stream of skilled workers\\ntailored to their organization's needs.\\n\\nConsider a manufacturing company\\npartnering with local community colleges\\nto create an industry 4.0 Apprenticeship.\\nParticipants learn advanced manufacturing skills\\nwhile working part-time in the business,\\nand this work also earns them credits towards their degrees.\\nWhen these graduates join the job market,\\nthey're already predisposed\\nto seek jobs where they served their apprenticeships,\\nensuring a renewable pipeline of talent ready for work.\\n\\nWhile there are some differences between these strategies,\\neach supports a human-centered approach\\nby focusing on individual skills and potential,\\nrather than rigid qualifications.\\nThey also provide opportunities for growth and development,\\nrecognizing the unique contributions\\neach person can make to your organization.\\nAs we build our AI skills bridge,\\nit's crucial to remember that technology is a tool,\\nnot a replacement for human talent.\\n\\nThese pipeline strategies help us harness the power of AI\\nwhile keeping people at the center of our organizations.\\nSo now it's time for you to apply what you've learned.\\nPause this video and take a moment\\nto reflect on the three pipeline strategies we've discussed.\\nSkills-based hiring, internal talent marketplaces,\\nand apprentice programs.\\nChoose one of these strategies that you believe\\nwould be most effective for your organization.\\n\\nIn a brief paragraph,\\nexplain why you've selected this strategy\\nand how it could help bridge the gap\\nbetween your current talent and the needs of the future.\\nConsider your organization's culture, current challenges,\\nand long-term goals in your response.\\nAnd when you come back,\\nwe'll explore how to implement these strategies effectively,\\nensuring they align\\nwith your organization's overall talent development goals.\\n\\nUntil then, keep building those bridges.\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:5211211\",\"duration\":318,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Choosing the right skills pipeline strategy\",\"fileName\":\"5960110_en_US_02_02_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":709,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"handoutNotes\":\"Activity 2.2 Recruiting and Hiring Skills.pdf\",\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"The temptation to hire anyone who can do the job today misses the opportunity to curate roles that leverage the full breadth of human potential. In this video, learn how to design a recruiting and hiring process that leverages AI so that you can match the total package of individual candidate skills with current organizational needs and future opportunities.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":13045715,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- Now that we've studied\\nthree effective pipeline strategies,\\nhow do we ensure that our workforce is ready\\nfor tomorrow's challenges?\\nIt's a question that keeps many professionals up at night.\\nBut here's the thing,\\nthere's no one-size-fits-all answer.\\nThe right skills pipeline strategy depends\\non your unique organizational needs, culture, and goals.\\nLet's explore\\nhow three different companies tackle this challenge head-on.\\n\\nFirst, meet Sarah from Red30 Tech.\\nSarah faced a constant struggle to find developers\\nwith the specific leading edge skills she needed.\\nHer solution, a grow-your-own strategy.\\nRed30 Tech implemented an AI-powered learning platform\\nthat identified high-potential employees\\nand created personalized upskilling paths.\\nThe result, a 40% reduction in external hiring costs\\nand a much more engaged workforce.\\n\\nNext, we have Miguel from Landon Hotel.\\nMiguel's challenge was different.\\nA large workforce spread across multiple countries\\nwith varying skill levels.\\nHe opted for a partnership strategy,\\ncollaborating with local institutions\\nto develop tailored curricula in an apprentice framework.\\nBy leveraging AI to analyze skills gaps\\nand predict future needs,\\nMiguel's team created a steady stream\\nof job-ready graduates.\\n\\nFinally, there's Aisha from Globe Bank International.\\nWith strict regulatory requirements\\nand a need for specialized skills,\\nAisha chose a targeted acquisition strategy.\\nUsing AI-driven talent analytics,\\nshe identified small companies\\nwith the exact skill sets her organization needed.\\nThis approach allowed Globe Bank International\\nto quickly integrate new capabilities\\nwhile maintaining compliance.\\n\\nHow will you choose the right strategy\\nfor your organization?\\nHere's a step-by-step process I use with my clients.\\nFirst, assess your current state.\\nUse AI tools to analyze your existing workforce skills\\nand identify the gaps.\\nNext, define future needs.\\nLeverage predictive analytics\\nto forecast the skills your organization will require\\nin the coming years.\\n\\nThird, evaluate your resources.\\nConsider your budget, time constraints,\\nand available technology.\\nAfter that, analyze your culture.\\nDetermine if your organization is more suited\\nto developing internal talent or integrating external hires.\\nYou also need to consider industry trends.\\nResearch how similar companies in your sector are addressing\\nthe skills gaps.\\n\\nOnce you've done that, weigh the pros and cons.\\nList the advantages\\nand disadvantages of each strategy\\nfor your specific situation.\\nAnd finally, align with business goals.\\nEnsure that your chosen strategies\\nsupport your organization's long-term objectives.\\nRemember, as AI expert Gary Marcus pointed out,\\nthere are known knowns and known unknowns,\\nbut what we should be worried about most\\nis the unknown unknowns.\\n\\nThis is especially true when it comes\\nto future skills needs.\\nYour chosen strategy should be flexible enough to adapt\\nto unforeseen changes in your industry,\\nand leave room\\nfor unexpected developments in AI capabilities.\\nNow it's your turn to apply this process.\\nUsing the handout provided,\\nselect the best strategy for your organization\\nand explain your reasoning.\\nConsider the unique challenges you face,\\nthe resources at your disposal, and your long-term goals.\\n\\nAs you work through this exercise, keep in mind\\nthat ethical considerations should be at the forefront\\nof your decision-making.\\nSo ask yourself,\\n\\\"How will this strategy impact our current employees?\\nAre we creating equitable opportunities\\nfor skill development?\\nAre we using AI tools responsibly in our assessment\\nand implementation processes?\\\"\\nBe careful selecting\\nand implementing the right skills pipeline strategy.\\n\\nYou're not just solving today's talent challenges.\\nYou're building a resilient, adaptable workforce\\nready for whatever the future may bring.\\nBy completing this activity, you're drawing a blueprint\\nfor your skills bridge.\\nWhere does it begin for you?\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:2135000\",\"duration\":294,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Implementing your skills pipeline strategy with AI\",\"fileName\":\"5960110_en_US_02_03_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":476,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"handoutNotes\":\"Activity 2.3 Skills Pipeline Strategy Implementation.pdf\\n\\nHandout 2.3 AI Tools.pdf\",\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"While AI represents a powerful new way to manage and develop talent in the organization, it comes with significant risks and unanswered questions. Ignoring these risks can expose the organization to legal penalties and declining credibility. In this video, learn how to recognize the benefits and risks associated with AI models so that you can monitor and govern candidate screening and matching processes in the organization.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":12497037,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- We've been designing a bridge that could take\\nyour organization from the world of today\\nto the challenges of tomorrow.\\nNow it's time to turn that blueprint into reality.\\nBut here's the catch.\\nWe're not just using bricks and mortar.\\nWe're leveraging the power of AI to construct a pipeline\\nthat's smart, adaptive, and future-ready.\\nSo how do we bring our skills pipeline strategy to life\\nwith AI as our chief architect?\\nLet's break it down step by step.\\n\\nFirst, you need to map your current landscape.\\nWe need to understand our starting point.\\nUse AI-powered skills assessment tools to create\\na detailed map of your organization's current skill sets.\\nThis isn't just about job titles.\\nIt's about uncovering hidden talents\\nand identifying precise skill gaps.\\nNext, we should forecast future skill demands.\\nLet's gaze into the crystal ball,\\nor rather, let AI do it for us.\\n\\nEmploy predictive analytics tools\\nto forecast future skills needs\\nbased on industry trends, technological advancements,\\nand your organization's strategic goals.\\nWith our current and future landscapes mapped,\\nit's time to plot the course.\\nAI can help design personalized learning pathways\\nfor employees considering their current skills,\\ncareer aspirations, and your organization's needs.\\n\\nIf you want to learn more about this step in the process,\\ncheck out my course \\\"Using Gen AI to Develop\\nPersonalized Learning Plans\\\".\\nOnce that's done, select your AI-powered learning tools.\\nChoose AI-enabled learning platforms\\nthat align with your strategy.\\nWhether it's adaptive learning systems,\\nvirtual reality training modules, or AI writing assistants,\\nselect tools that will effectively deliver\\nand reinforce new skills.\\n\\nSo now you've launched your chosen tools\\nand started building that pipeline.\\nBut remember, implementation isn't a set it\\nand forget it affair.\\nUse AI analytics to monitor engagement, track progress,\\nand measure the impact of your skills gap.\\nNext, don't forget to iterate and optimize.\\nThe beauty of AI is its ability to learn\\nand improve over time.\\nSo regularly review the data insights\\nprovided by your AI tools.\\n\\nAre certain learning pathways more effective than others?\\nDid anything change in your industry\\nthat isn't accounted for?\\nAnd use these insights to refine your strategy.\\nFinally, use AI to nurture a learning ecosystem.\\nImplement AI-driven recommendation systems\\nthat suggest relevant learning opportunities to employees\\nbased on their roles, interests and career trajectories.\\n\\nNow it's time to put these steps into action.\\nRefer to the handout titled, \\\"AI-Enabled Tools\\nfor Skills Pipeline Implementation\\\".\\nYou'll find a curated list of AI tools\\ncategorized by function, from skills assessment\\nto personalized learning delivery.\\nChoose one of these tools, or find one that you prefer\\nto complete your next assignment.\\nYour task is to develop an implementation plan\\nfor your organization.\\nFollow the steps we've outlined,\\nselecting appropriate tools for each stage.\\n\\nConsider your organization's unique needs,\\nculture, and resources as you craft your plan.\\nWe've provided a template to help you\\nkeep track of the details.\\nBut unlike a bridge built of brick and mortar,\\nyou're building a bridge comprised\\nof artificial intelligence and human ingenuity,\\nso be ready to stay flexible as you implement\\nyour AI-powered skills pipeline.\\nMake sure your plan has enough built-in options\\nto adapt as new technologies emerge,\\nand unforeseen challenges arrive.\\n\\nBy leveraging AI in your skills pipeline strategy,\\nyou're not just bridging a gap,\\nyou're building a dynamic, intelligent pathway\\nthat evolves with your organization's needs.\\nI'm so excited for you as you approach\\nthis important milestone.\\nThe future of your team is waiting on the other side.\\n\"}],\"name\":\"2. Skills in the Talent Pipeline\",\"size\":41623212,\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentChapter:5211213\"},{\"duration\":816,\"entries\":[{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:2133165\",\"duration\":272,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Anticipating tomorrow's skills with AI\",\"fileName\":\"5960110_en_US_03_01_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":398,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"With so much focus on changes taking place in real time due to AI advances, it can be easy to become reactive, rather than planning for the future, placing the organization at risk as technology brings new and unexpected challenges to the organization. In this video, learn how to scan the environment and identify future needs that must be sourced today so that you can prepare the organization for anticipated skills gaps before they happen.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":9990489,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- Imagine an engineer standing at the edge of a vast chasm,\\nenvisioning a bridge that doesn't exist yet.\\nWhat factors must they consider?\\nThe distance to span.\\nThe winds that will buffet their creation.\\nThe weight this bridge must bear.\\nAnd what about the unknowns?\\nThe geological shifts beneath the surface,\\nthe advancements in material science\\nthat could revolutionize design,\\nthe unforeseen needs of future travelers.\\n\\nThis is exactly the challenge you face\\nas an HR professional\\nin today's rapidly evolving workplace.\\nYou're tasked with building a bridge to tomorrow's skills,\\noften without a clear view of the other side.\\nBut here's the exciting part.\\nYou're not just a bridge builder.\\nYou're a visionary, shaping the future of your organization.\\nAnd this is a job\\nonly you are uniquely qualified to handle.\\n\\nSo how do we harness AI\\nto become the engineers of tomorrow's workforce?\\nLet's break it down.\\nStep one, scan the horizon.\\nUse AI-powered trend analysis tools\\nto monitor industry publications,\\npatents, and startup activities.\\nThese can provide early signals of emerging technologies\\nand required skills.\\nStep two, listen to the wind.\\n\\nImplement AI-driven social listening tools\\nto track conversations in your industry.\\nWhat skills are people talking about?\\nWhat challenges are they facing?\\nStep three, map the terrain.\\nUtilize AI to create a detailed map\\nof your current workforce skills.\\nThis isn't just about job titles,\\nit's about uncovering hidden talents and potential.\\nStep four, forecast the weather.\\nEmploy predictive analytics\\nto model various future scenarios.\\n\\nHow might different economic, technological,\\nor societal changes impact your skill needs?\\nStep five, design flexible structures.\\nUse AI to create adaptable learning pathways.\\nThe goal isn't just to train for specific skills,\\nbut to build a workforce that's agile and ready to learn.\\nStep six, test the materials.\\nImplement AI-powered assessment tools\\nto continuously evaluate the effectiveness\\nof your training programs and adjust in real time.\\n\\nAnd step seven, collaborate with other engineers.\\nUse AI to facilitate knowledge sharing\\nacross your organization and industry.\\nThe future is far too complex\\nfor any one person to predict alone.\\nRemember, as you embark on this journey,\\nyou're not just preparing your organization for the future,\\nyou're actively shaping it.\\nYour insights combined with AI's analytical powers\\ncan turn uncertainty into opportunity.\\n\\nSo the next time you're in a meeting with stakeholders,\\nyou have an opportunity to explain\\nthat AI is your telescope,\\nyour seismograph, your weather vane,\\nall the tools that help you anticipate the shifts\\nin your industry's landscape.\\nShow them how you're not just reacting to change,\\nbut proactively building the skills\\nthat will drive your organization's success.\\nYou are the architect of your organization's future,\\nand with AI as your trusted assistant,\\nyou're more equipped than ever\\nto build that bridge to tomorrow's skills,\\nno matter how wide the chasm or how misty the far shore.\\n\\nAs the great management thinker Peter Drucker once said,\\n\\\"The best way to predict the future is to create it.\\\"\\nAnd that's precisely what you're doing with the help of AI.\\nSo are you ready to put on your hard hat\\nand start engineering the future?\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:2132168\",\"duration\":250,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Skills trend analysis with AI\",\"fileName\":\"5960110_en_US_03_02_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":571,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"handoutNotes\":\"Handout 3.2 AI Tools for Conducting Workforce Trend Analysis.pdf\",\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"The difference between a trend and a fad can be hard to see in the midst of disruption, but knowing the difference is an essential skill for the strategic talent development professional. In this video, learn how to separate significant trends from fashionable, short-term solutions. Learn how to apply a simple methodology for identifying and categorizing relevant trends, so that you can focus on the critical skills for the organization.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":13305158,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- So, we've talked about how workforce planning\\nis a lot like building a bridge\\nbetween the present and the future.\\nWell, imagine if the materials, the tools,\\nand even the laws of physics kept changing\\nwhile you were mid-construction.\\nThat's the challenge we face\\nin today's rapidly evolving workforce landscape.\\nBut now we have a tool that can serve\\nas both an early warning system and a crystal ball,\\nand it comes from the very disruptive technology\\nwe're all trying to figure out.\\n\\nEven though it feels like we're the first generation\\nto go through this massive change,\\ndisruption is really nothing new for we humans\\nand our relationship to technology.\\nNew technologies have always demanded\\nboth technical and soft skills to remain competitive.\\nFor example, when the automobile emerged,\\nit didn't just create jobs for mechanics,\\nit revolutionized logistics,\\nspawned new industries like roadside diners,\\nand even changed dating culture.\\n\\nThe advent of air travel required\\nnot just pilots and engineers,\\nbut also air traffic controllers,\\nflight attendants, and diplomats\\nto navigate international airspace regulations.\\nThe telecommunications boom\\ndidn't stop at creating network engineers,\\nit gave rise to social media managers, digital marketers,\\nand cyber security experts.\\nIn the age of AI,\\nHR professionals are facing similar seismic shifts.\\n\\nThis is where AI-powered skills trend analysis\\ncomes into play.\\nIt's like having a team of tireless researchers\\nconstantly scanning the horizon for you.\\nAI can analyze job postings, industry reports,\\nacademic papers, and even social media chatter,\\nall to identify emerging skills\\nbefore they become mainstream.\\nRemember, Sarah the HR director,\\nstruggling to find data scientists for her company?\\nA role that barely existed five years ago.\\n\\nOr Michael, a training manager,\\ngrappling with how to upskill warehouse workers\\nas automation transforms logistics.\\nThen there's Priya, a recruitment specialist,\\nrealizing that the so-called soft skills\\nher company once considered optional,\\nlike adaptability and continuous learning,\\nare now essential for almost every role.\\nSome tools use AI\\nto track labor market data in real time,\\nspotting new skills as they emerge.\\n\\nOthers can model how different technologies\\nmight impact your workforce,\\nhelping you stay ahead of your competition.\\nLinkedIn's economic graph leverages AI\\nto map the changing skills landscape\\nacross industries and geographies.\\nHere's what's most exciting.\\nAI isn't just helping us adapt to new technologies,\\nit's helping us work better with AI itself.\\nSo, by conducting trend analysis\\non AI-related skills,\\nthese tools can help you anticipate\\nwhat your team needs to learn\\nto thrive in the age of AI.\\n\\nJust as modern bridge builders use AI\\nto simulate stress tests and predict maintenance needs,\\nyou can use AI to stress test your workforce plans\\nand predict future skill gaps.\\nIt's not about replacing human insight,\\nit's about augmenting it.\\nIn our next video, I'm going to ask you\\nto select some tools you might want to use\\nto predict the AI skills you'll need in your organization.\\n\\nSo, now is a great time\\nto download the handout titled\\n\\\"AI Tools for Skills Trend Analysis\\\",\\nand give a few of them a try.\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:5211210\",\"duration\":294,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Building an AI toolbox for predicting future skills\",\"fileName\":\"5960110_en_US_03_03_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":608,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"handoutNotes\":\"Activity 3.3 Framework for Predicting Future Skills with AI.pdf\",\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"There are many vendors that claim to hold the secret to forecasting the future, but technology without human judgment will likely fail to develop an effective skills forecast. In this video, learn how to select AI tools that are people-friendly so that you can create specific, effective, and people-focused forecasts that lead to effective workforce development plans.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":15039294,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- Just as a builder selects the right tools\\nfor each phase of construction,\\nHR professionals must choose the appropriate AI tools\\nto forecast the skills their organization is going to need\\nto span the gap between today and tomorrow.\\nBut how do you select the right tools from the vast\\narray available?\\nLet's construct a toolbox\\nthat will help you build your own skills prediction model.\\nDefine your destination.\\n\\nClearly articulate your organization's long-term goals.\\nWhat skills will you need to achieve these objectives?\\nAssess your current capabilities.\\nEvaluate your existing technology infrastructure,\\nand in-house expertise.\\nWhat kind of tool can your organization realistically\\nimplement and maintain?\\nIdentify key features.\\nCreate a list of must have and nice to have features.\\n\\nConsider factors like data integration capabilities,\\nvisualization tools and customization options.\\nSet your budget.\\nDetermine how much your organization is willing\\nto invest in this tool,\\nincluding potential hidden costs like training\\nand ongoing support.\\nCreate evaluation criteria.\\nDevelop a scorecard with weighted criteria,\\nsuch as ease of use, accuracy of predictions, integration\\nwith existing systems and vendor reputation.\\n\\nResearch available tools.\\nUse the handout from our previous video as a starting point.\\nResearch each tool's capabilities, strengths\\nand limitations.\\nMatch tools to criteria.\\nScore each tool against your evaluation criteria.\\nThis will help you create a short list\\nof the most suitable options.\\nRequest demos and trials.\\nReach out to vendors for demonstrations.\\n\\nIf possible, arrange for free trials\\nto test the tools in your specific context.\\nGather stakeholder input.\\nInvolve key stakeholders in the evaluation process.\\nTheir buy-in will be crucial for successful implementation.\\nMake your decision.\\nBased on your evaluation,\\nstakeholder input and trial results,\\nselect the tool that best fits your organization's\\nneeds and constraints.\\n\\nPlan for implementation.\\nDevelop a rollout strategy, including training, for users\\nand a plan for integrating the tool into your\\nexisting workflows.\\nFinally, establish metrics for success.\\nDefine how you'll measure the effectiveness\\nof your chosen tool.\\nSet up a system\\nfor regularly reviewing its performance and impact.\\nRemember, selecting the right AI tool is just the beginning.\\nYour human insight\\nand industry knowledge will be crucial in interpreting\\nand applying the AI-generated forecast.\\n\\nSo don't be dazzled by flashy features you may never use.\\nInstead, focus on tools that align\\nwith your organization's culture and processes,\\nand be wary of vendors promising 100% accuracy.\\nThe future is inherently uncertain\\nand healthy skepticism is your friend.\\nDon't underestimate the importance of user friendliness.\\nA powerful tool that no one wants\\nto use is no tool at all.\\n\\nWatch out for hidden costs like data preparation, training\\nor API calls that can blow your budget.\\nAnd most importantly, don't expect AI to do all the work.\\nThese tools are incredibly powerful,\\nbut they're really not magic.\\nThey're here to augment your expertise, not replace it.\\nYour industry knowledge\\nand human insight will always be the secret sauce\\nin predicting future skills.\\n\\nSo approach this process with enthusiasm,\\nbut also with a healthy dose of pragmatism.\\nSo we've talked about a lot of steps here,\\nand now that you've established a framework\\nfor choosing the right forecasting tools, it's time to apply\\nthat framework to your own organization.\\nThe handout provided in the previous video\\nis a great place to start.\\nHappy tool hunting.\\n\"}],\"name\":\"3. Forecasting the Skills of Tomorrow\",\"size\":38334941,\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentChapter:5211214\"},{\"duration\":864,\"entries\":[{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:5208168\",\"duration\":303,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Moving from continuous learning to continuous skilling\",\"fileName\":\"5960110_en_US_04_01_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":440,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"While continuous learning is often difficult to achieve in practice, targeted, continuous skilling is easily justified by the financial benefits of retaining skilled and motivated employees versus constantly replacing valuable, but under-utilized talent. In this video, learn how to explain the benefits of continuous skilling so that you can influence stakeholders to build a framework that supports and automates human development.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":14087739,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- Imagine our bridge-building project once again.\\nIn the past, we might have painstakingly calculated\\neach measurement, tested every material,\\nand plotted every angle with slide rules\\nand paper blueprints.\\nSure, we could build bridges that way,\\nbut in today's fast-paced world, would we want to?\\nThis is the difference between continuous learning\\nand continuous skilling.\\nSo, continuous learning\\nis like constantly reading bridge-building manuals.\\n\\nSure, it's valuable,\\nbut it doesn't necessarily translate into immediate action.\\nContinuous skilling is like having a real-time\\nadaptive blueprint that updates as you build,\\nsuggesting more efficient techniques\\nand materials on the fly.\\nIt's about acquiring and applying new skills rapidly\\nin response to changing needs.\\nAI accelerates this process exponentially.\\n\\nIt can analyze vast amounts of data, identify skill gaps,\\nsuggest personalized learning paths,\\nand even predict future skill needs\\nfaster than any human team.\\nSo, what might have taken months of analysis\\ncan now be done in hours or even minutes.\\nImagine AI as your tireless assistant,\\nconstantly scanning the horizon for new technologies,\\nindustry trends, and emerging skill requirements.\\n\\nBut remember, AI is not replacing your expertise,\\nit's augmenting it, allowing you\\nto focus on strategic decisions\\nrather than getting bogged down and data crunching.\\nSo, let's talk about repurposing existing talent.\\nIt's often quicker and more cost-effective\\nto retain your current workforce than to hire externally.\\nThis approach not only saves time and resources,\\nbut also boosts employee morale and retention.\\n\\nFor example, let's take a look at banking.\\nA major bank retrained its tellers\\nin digital customer service and basic coding\\nas more transactions moved online.\\nSo, instead of layoffs, they created a more versatile,\\ntech-savvy frontline team.\\nAI-powered assessments helped identify employees\\nwith aptitudes for these new roles,\\nensuring a smoother transition.\\n\\nIn manufacturing, an auto parts manufacturer used AI\\nto identify workers with aptitudes for robotics,\\nand retrained them to operate and maintain\\nnew automated systems,\\nsmoothing the transition to industry 4.0.\\nThe AI system not only identified suitable candidates,\\nbut also created personalized learning paths\\nfor each employee.\\nIn healthcare, a hospital system used AI-powered\\nskill mapping to identify nurses with leadership potential\\nand data analysis skills, retraining them\\nto be health informatics specialists.\\n\\nThis move helped the hospital better utilize patient data\\nfor improved care while providing\\ncareer growth opportunities for their staff.\\nIn each case, AI played a crucial role\\nin identifying transferable skills,\\ncreating targeted upscaling programs,\\nand tracking progress in real time.\\nIt's not just about filling immediate skill gaps,\\nbut about creating a culture of adaptability\\nand continuous improvement.\\n\\nAnd here's a crucial reminder.\\nDon't forget to include yourself in these re-skilling plans.\\nAs HR professionals,\\nwe're not immune to the changing landscape.\\nCould you benefit from a deeper understanding\\nof data analytics or maybe sharpen your management skills\\nto lead these transformation efforts?\\nRemember, in the world of skills development,\\nyou're not just building a bridge,\\nyou're creating an ever evolving network of pathways,\\nconstantly adapting to new destinations.\\n\\nAnd with AI as your co-pilot\\nand a commitment to continuous skilling,\\nyour employees will be ready to travel\\nwherever the future leads them.\\nAre you ready to transform your organization\\nand yourself into agile future-ready powerhouses?\\nThe journey of continuous skilling is ongoing,\\nbut with each step, you're building a more resilient,\\nadaptable, and innovative workforce.\\nAnd in today's fast-changing world,\\nthat is the ultimate competitive advantage.\\n\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:2135001\",\"duration\":280,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Envisioning personalized skill paths with AI\",\"fileName\":\"5960110_en_US_04_02_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":458,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Because each employee is unique, continuous skilling is not a one-size-fits-all approach, but requires a nuanced approach that adapts to each employee and their needs, interests, and abilities. In this video, learn how to construct a plan to bridge the gap between current individual skills and future opportunities by using AI so you can accelerate personalized skill development.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":13391720,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- Imagine if every beam, cable,\\nand rivet in our skills bridge\\nwere custom-designed for its specific place and purpose.\\nThat is the power of personalized learning\\napplied to skill development.\\nPersonalized learning tailors the content, pace,\\nand style of instruction\\nto everyone's unique needs, abilities, and goals.\\nWhen we apply this concept to skill paths,\\nwe're not just building\\na one-size-fits-all bridge to the future.\\n\\nWe're crafting individual pathways\\nthat maximize each person's potential.\\nAI is the architect\\nthat makes this level of personalization possible at scale.\\nIt can analyze an individual's current skills,\\nlearning preferences, career aspirations,\\nand organizational needs\\nto create a unique skill development journey.\\nLet's look at how this plays out in real-life scenarios.\\nMeet Lisa, a marketing specialist\\nwith a background in traditional advertising.\\n\\nHer company, though, is pivoting\\ntowards digital-first campaigns,\\nand Lisa needs to upskill quickly.\\nAI creates a personalized path\\nthat starts with data analytics basics,\\nmoves through digital marketing strategies,\\nand culminates in AI-driven campaign optimization.\\nThe AI adapts as Lisa progresses,\\nslowing down when she struggles with data concepts\\nand speeding up when she breezes\\nthrough familiar marketing territory.\\n\\nSix months later, Lisa is leading\\nthe company's most successful digital campaign to date.\\nNow consider Tom,\\na software developer exploring blockchain technology.\\nThe AI-driven learning system\\nassesses Tom's strong programming foundation\\nand his preference for hands-on learning.\\nIt designs a skill path\\nthat begins with blockchain fundamentals,\\nquickly progresses to smart contract development,\\nand includes a set\\nof increasingly complex coding challenges.\\n\\nWithin three months, Tom has developed a prototype\\nfor a blockchain-based application\\nthat attracts new investors to his startup.\\nLastly, there's Maria, a human resources manager\\nlooking to leverage AI in her role.\\nMaria has a humanities background\\nand is a little apprehensive about technology,\\nso the AI system recognizes this\\nand creates a gentle learning curve,\\nstarting with basic AI concepts\\nexplained through real-world HR scenarios.\\n\\nA year later,\\nMaria's implementing several AI-driven initiatives\\nthat have significantly improved her department's efficiency\\nand strategic impact.\\nIn each case, AI didn't just provide content.\\nIt crafted a journey.\\nIt considered each person's starting point,\\nlearning preferences, pace, and goals,\\nadjusting in real time based on their progress and feedback.\\nThe result: faster, more effective skill development\\ntailored to both individual and organizational needs.\\n\\nThis is the broader vision\\nof AI-driven personalized skill paths.\\nWe're not just building a single bridge\\nto the future of work.\\nWe're constructing an intricate network of pathways,\\neach uniquely designed to carry an individual\\nfrom where they are to where they need to be.\\nOur metaphorical skills bridge\\nis becoming a living learning structure.\\nEach person's journey strengthens and expands it,\\ncreating new connections and possibilities.\\n\\nAI is the tireless engineer\\nconstantly analyzing, adjusting, and optimizing these paths,\\nand you are the leading architect.\\nAs HR professionals, we set the destinations,\\ndefine the broader architecture,\\nand ensure that each individual path\\naligns with our organizational goals.\\nWith AI as our partner, we can create a learning ecosystem\\nthat's as dynamic and diverse as our workforce.\\n\\nIn our next lesson,\\nwe'll show you how to start mapping out an ecosystem\\nthat focuses on skills\\nand leads your organization into the future.\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:5208167\",\"duration\":281,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Building the AI-driven skill development ecosystem\",\"fileName\":\"5960110_en_US_04_03_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":634,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"handoutNotes\":\"Activity 4.3 Designing Your AI-driven Skill Development Ecosystem.pdf\",\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Personalized learning has long been a goal of talent development professionals, but implementation via traditional methods proves too costly and labor-intensive to apply at scale. In this video, learn how to use AI tools to compare internal trends to individual performance so you can recommend effective, accelerated, and hyper-personal paths towards new skills and opportunities.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":13501638,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- You've probably noticed\\nthat something extraordinary has been happening\\nas we've walked through the practical task\\nto build our skills bridge.\\nIt's no longer a single static structure,\\nbut a living, evolving network of interconnected pathways\\nwith the learner at the very center,\\nactively navigating and shaping their journey.\\nThis is what we mean by a comprehensive learning ecosystem,\\na dynamic environment where various elements work in harmony\\nto empower continuous skill development.\\n\\nIn this AI-driven skill development ecosystem,\\nthe learners aren't passive travelers.\\nThey are the navigators of their own paths\\nfrom where we are today\\nto where we need to be in the future.\\nAI serves as an intelligent support system\\nproviding personalized blueprints, real-time analysis,\\nand adaptive scaffolding along the way.\\nSo what does this learner-centric ecosystem look like?\\nWell, at its core,\\nyou might have an AI-powered learning experience platform\\ncalled an LXP that serves\\nas a personalized command center for each learner.\\n\\nThis platform doesn't just display the root.\\nIt learns from the user's journey,\\nhelping them draft and refine their blueprints\\nbased on their goals, preferences, and organizational needs.\\nBranching out from this core,\\nyou could have AI-driven skills assessment tools\\nthat learners can use\\nto continually survey their progress, identify gaps,\\nand find potential new roots.\\nThese self-assessments feed back into the LXP,\\nhelping learners adjust their development plans.\\n\\nNext, consider integrating AI-powered content curation tools\\nand a recommendation engine that learners can leverage\\nto discover new building materials and techniques,\\nall tailored to their specific\\nbridge building needs and style.\\nSocial learning becomes a part of this ecosystem\\nwith AI facilitating connections between bridge builders.\\nLearners can seek out mentors\\nor collaborators based on complimentary skills and goals,\\ncreating a community of practice.\\n\\nPerformance support tools can be seamlessly integrated too,\\nallowing learners to apply new techniques\\ndirectly to their bridge building\\nwith AI providing real-time feedback\\nand suggestions for improvement.\\nAnd let's not overlook the potential\\nof virtual and augmented reality\\nfor immersive skill practice with AI adjusting scenarios\\nbased on the learner's choices and progress,\\nallowing them to test their bridges\\nin simulated future environments.\\n\\nThe beauty of this ecosystem is its adaptability.\\nAs learner's goals and organizational needs evolve,\\nAI can help recalibrate the entire system,\\nensuring that each bridge\\nalways leads to the most valuable destinations.\\nNow it's time for you to design your own learner-centric,\\nAI-driven skill development ecosystem.\\nIn the following activity,\\nyou'll design an ideal ecosystem for your organization.\\n\\nDownload the activity template.\\nLet your imagination have some fun with this one.\\nRemember, the goal is to create an environment\\nwhere learners are the pilots of their own careers\\nwith AI as their intelligent assistant,\\nactively driving their own skill development journey\\nalong paths that align with the organization's goals.\\nAs you work through this activity,\\nimagine the potential impact on your workforce.\\nPicture employees confidently constructing their bridges\\nto future skills,\\ndeveloping the capabilities they need when they need them.\\n\\nWe're really talking about a network of bridges,\\neach unique, yet interconnected,\\nforming a robust infrastructure\\nof continuous learning and adaptation.\\nYou know, this is so much more\\nthan just a collection of tools.\\nIt's a vision for learner-centric development\\nin your organization.\\nAnd who knows, as we continue to innovate\\nand push the boundaries of what's possible,\\nthese bridges might just lead us\\nto something even more extraordinary.\\n\\nAnd it starts with you.\\n\"}],\"name\":\"4. Upskilling and Reskilling Existing Employees\",\"size\":40981097,\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentChapter:2134169\"},{\"duration\":802,\"entries\":[{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:5212000\",\"duration\":303,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Understanding bias in AI-driven skills management\",\"fileName\":\"5960110_en_US_05_01_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":558,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Humans struggle to reduce their own bias in the workplace and can often transfer these biases to the AI systems they build. Without careful design and constant vigilance, these biases can perpetuate and grow throughout the organization. In this video, learn how to demonstrate how AI can help identify and mitigate human and institutional bias so you can improve skills assessment processes and drive stronger talent development results.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":12501319,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- Before we can complete our bridge\\nto the future of skills management,\\nwe need to address a critical issue, bias.\\nJust like a bridge needs to be stable\\nand accessible for everyone,\\nour AI-driven skills management systems\\nmust be fair and inclusive.\\nAnd here's our challenge.\\nAI systems can inadvertently perpetuate\\nor even amplify existing human biases.\\n\\nBias is not only a fact of life,\\nit's a result of how our brains work to keep us alive.\\nBias is an indication that we are responding\\nconsciously or not\\nto a perceived threat to our own survival,\\nbut our brains evolved slowly across thousands of years\\nin response to genuine dangers\\nto the survival of our species.\\nIn today's world, those same dangers are long gone,\\nbut the biases often remain.\\n\\nIn skills management,\\nbiased AI could lead to unfair hiring decisions,\\nskewed performance evaluations,\\nor unequal learning opportunities.\\nThe consequences?\\nA less averse workforce, untapped potential,\\nand a weaker organization.\\nNow let's break down the types of biases\\nwe might encounter in our organization.\\nFirst, there's algorithmic bias.\\nThis occurs when the AI's decision-making rules\\nare inherently biased.\\n\\nFor example, an AI algorithm might inadvertently favor\\ncertain educational backgrounds over others\\neven when they're not relevant to job performance.\\nThen there's data bias.\\nRemember, AI learns from data,\\nso if that data reflects historical biases,\\nthe AI will perpetuate them.\\nImagine a resume screening tool\\ntrained on a company's historical hiring data.\\nIf that company previously hired mostly men\\nfor leadership roles,\\nthe AI might conclude the desirable characteristics\\nare those typically presented by males,\\nsuch as leading a sports team\\nor membership in certain organizations.\\n\\nAnd then there's human bias.\\nWe can't forget that humans design, implement,\\nand interpret AI systems,\\nso our own biases can creep in at any of these stages.\\nWe have to look no further\\nthan the earliest days of AI generated-images,\\nwhich were often plagued\\nby hypersexualized portrayals of female subjects,\\nor a preponderance of white male images\\ncreated for the request of a manager or a leader.\\nLet's look at some real-world examples.\\n\\nAn AI recruitment tool developed by a major tech company\\nwas biased against women\\nbecause it was trained on successful resumes\\nsubmitted over a 10-year period mostly from men.\\nA healthcare algorithm used on millions of patients\\nallocated less care to patients of color\\nthan white patients with similar conditions.\\nAn AI-powered performance review system\\nconsistently rated women lower than males in tech roles,\\nreflecting and amplifying existing gender biases\\nin the industry.\\n\\nThese examples underscore why addressing bias is crucial\\nfor effective diversity, equity, and inclusion initiatives.\\nIf we're not careful,\\nAI could undermine our DEI efforts,\\ncreating a veneer of objectivity\\nwhile reinforcing systematic biases.\\nWhile AI can be part of the problem,\\nit can also be part of the solution.\\nWith careful design,\\ntesting, implementation, and monitoring,\\nAI can actually help us identify\\nand mitigate biases that might go unnoticed by humans.\\n\\nIt can even analyze vast amounts of data\\nto spot patterns of unfairness and suggest corrections.\\nIt's not just about avoiding pitfalls,\\nit's about leveraging AI's potential\\nto create fairer more inclusive systems.\\nIn our next video, we'll explore specific ways\\nAI can be used to promote diversity, equity, and inclusion\\nin skills management.\\nFor now, remember this.\\n\\nAwareness is the first step\\ntowards creating a more inclusive future.\\nBy understanding the types and impacts of bias in AI,\\nwe're already on the path\\nto building a better, fairer bridge to the future.\\nAnd through a skills-based approach,\\nwe can make sure our bridge to the future\\nis open to everyone.\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:2132167\",\"duration\":264,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Leveraging AI to promoted DEI in skills management\",\"fileName\":\"5960110_en_US_05_02_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":544,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"handoutNotes\":\"Activity 5.2 DEI Audit.pdf\",\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Simply teaching AI principles is not enough to drive consistent behavior change across an organization, but individual programs may take too long to implement meaningful change. In this video, learn how to design an AI-based program to gradually change behavior through nudge learning, so that you can help employees adopt more productive and positive behaviors that support diversity, equity, and inclusion.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":13530927,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- In our last video, we explored the challenges\\nof bias in AI,\\nbut now let's see how AI, when used thoughtfully,\\ncan be a powerful ally in promoting diversity, equity,\\nand inclusion in our organizations.\\nWe'll focus on three key areas:\\nassessment, recruiting, and career progression.\\nLet's start with Skills Assessment.\\nAI tools can help us identify\\nand mitigate bias in this crucial area.\\nFor instance, AI-powered language analysis tools\\ncan scan performance reviews for possible bias language,\\nflagging words or phrases\\nthat might unfairly disadvantage certain groups.\\n\\nImagine an AI tool highlighting\\nthat female employees are more often described\\nas supportive, while male employees are called leaders.\\nThis insight allows us to recalibrate our assessments\\nand ensure we're evaluating skills,\\nnot the unconscious bias of human evaluators.\\nMoving to Recruiting,\\nAI can help create more inclusive job descriptions.\\nTools like Textio or Gender Decoder use machine learning\\nto analyze job postings\\nand suggest more inclusive language\\nthat can also identify words\\nthat might discourage certain groups from even applying\\nand propose alternatives.\\n\\nThe result is a wider, more diverse applicant pool.\\nAI-powered blind screening\\nand resume review techniques are already revolutionizing\\nhow we select candidates.\\nThese tools can anonymize resumes,\\nremoving names, photos, and other potential sources of bias.\\nSome can even mask indicators of age or gender\\nand work histories.\\nThis allows recruiters to focus solely\\non skills and qualifications,\\ngiving every candidate a fair shot.\\n\\nNow let's talk about Career Progression\\nwhere AI-driven predictive analytics can be a game changer.\\nAI can analyze patterns in promotions, pay raises,\\nand career trajectories across your organization.\\nIf it spots discrepancies,\\nsay a certain demographic consistently being passed over\\nfor leadership roles,\\nit can alert you to potential bias\\nin your progression systems.\\nThis foresight allows you\\nto address these issues proactively,\\nensuring equitable growth opportunities for all\\nand making it easier to keep talented individuals\\nin your talent pipeline.\\n\\nBut don't just take my word for it.\\nLet's look at some real-world success stories.\\nUnilever used AI to diversify its workforce,\\nparticularly in management roles.\\nThey implemented an AI-powered recruitment system\\nto assess candidates based on skills rather than background.\\nAnd result is they've achieved gender balance\\nin management roles globally\\nwith women representing 50% of managers.\\nAnother example is Gap Incorporated.\\n\\nThey used AI to analyze their job descriptions\\nand identified subtle biases in language.\\nBy rewriting these with AI assistance,\\nthey saw a 60% increase in female applicants\\nfor their engineering roles.\\nAccenture implemented AI-based gamified assessments\\nfor campus recruiting.\\nThis approach helped Accenture increase its diversity\\nof new hires by 20%,\\nwhile reducing time to hire by 50%.\\nThese success stories show us that AI,\\nwhen used thoughtfully,\\ncan be a powerful force for promoting DEI\\nin skills management.\\n\\nIt can help us cast a wider net,\\nevaluate more fairly,\\nand create more equitable paths for career progression.\\nBut remember, AI is a tool, not a magic wand.\\nIts effectiveness depends on how we use it.\\nIn our next video, we'll discuss best practices\\nfor implementing these AI tools effectively.\\nThe future of fair and inclusive skills management\\nis getting closer all the time,\\nand it's right over our AI skills bridge.\\n\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:5212001\",\"duration\":235,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Best practices for ethical AI in skills management\",\"fileName\":\"5960110_en_US_05_03_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":366,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Discover guidelines and best practices related to ethical AI in skills management.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":12033429,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- In previous videos, we established an understanding\\nof bias in skills management\\nand how AI can help mitigate that bias.\\nSo now, let's focus on best practices\\nto ensure our AI systems are ethical, fair, and effective.\\nFirst, we need a robust framework for ethical AI use in HR.\\nSo, let's define core principles\\nlike fairness, transparency,\\naccountability, and privacy.\\nThese principles conserves\\nthe foundation of our skills bridge,\\ngiving us a sound basis for everything\\nfrom data collection to deployment.\\n\\nLet's start with diversity,\\nyour secret weapon to ensure fairness.\\nDiverse teams are more likely to spot potential biases\\nand propose inclusive solutions,\\nso our first best practice is\\ninvolve people from various departments, levels,\\nand demographic groups in all your AI initiatives.\\nHow do you achieve fairness?\\nRegularly audit your AI tools for bias.\\nLook for unexpected patterns\\nor outcomes that might indicate unfairness.\\n\\nYou might also consider using AI to monitor AI\\nbut don't rely solely on automated checks.\\nAlways combine these with tools\\nwith human-led audits\\nand real-world impact assessments.\\nNow let's talk about transparency.\\nThere's a common saying that AI is like a black box\\nand we can't see what's inside that makes it work.\\nBut the trend towards transparent explainable AI\\nis gaining traction, making it easier to understand\\nhow AI reaches its conclusions.\\n\\nThis approach could allow us to build more comprehensive,\\nless biased AI systems\\nby leveraging a diverse data set.\\nAnother pillar of ethical AI is privacy.\\nThroughout the AI lifecycle,\\nfrom development and testing to implementation,\\nsafeguarding employee privacy is paramount.\\nWe must ensure that personal data is protected,\\nanonymized where possible,\\nand used only for its intended purpose.\\n\\nThe last pillar is accountability.\\nAI systems cannot judge\\nwhether their actions are ethical or not.\\nThat's why accountability is always a standard\\nby which we evaluate the humans involved in AI systems.\\nTrain your HR team to interpret AI insights critically\\nand consider contextual factors that AI might miss\\nand audit their results\\nto be sure they are making the right decisions.\\n\\nNow it's time to put these insights into practice.\\nWe've prepared an AI audit template for you to assess\\nyour organization's current DEI practices\\nfor skills management.\\nThis template will guide you through\\nevaluating your AI system's ethical framework,\\ndiversity and development teams, monitoring processes,\\nand the balance between AI and human decision making.\\nTo access the template, click the link below this video.\\nWork through each section,\\nconsidering how your organization measures up\\nto the best practices we've discussed.\\n\\nThis audit will help you identify areas for improvement\\nand develop an action plan\\nfor implementing ethical AI\\nin your skills management processes.\\nRemember, ethical AI and skills management\\nis not just about avoiding harm,\\nit's about actively doing good.\\nThe bridge to the future is right in front of us.\\nLet's make sure that everyone gets across together.\\n\"}],\"name\":\"5. Bias in Skills Management\",\"size\":38065675,\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentChapter:2132170\"},{\"duration\":732,\"entries\":[{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:2134168\",\"duration\":237,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"How power skills keep us safe from AI\",\"fileName\":\"5960110_en_US_06_01_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":366,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"handoutNotes\":\"Activity 6.1 AI Implementation Scenario.pdf\\n\\nHandout 6.1 Questions to Ask Stakeholders about AI Transparency and Fairness.pdf\",\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"With increased focus on AI technology and the skills required to leverage these skills effectively, it is easy to forget that many essential skills are best performed by humans. In this video, learn how to identify transferable \\\"power skills\\\" across the organization so you can ensure effective and safe AI implementations throughout the talent development organization.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":10095071,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- We've been talking a lot about the technology of AI,\\nand to use that technology most effectively,\\nwe need human skills at the center.\\nLet's see how Sarah's doing these days.\\nAs we fast forward a few years,\\nshe's the newly appointed HR Director at Red30 Tech.\\nShe was asked to sit in on a high stakes meeting\\nand the conversation left her feeling a little uneasy.\\nHer CEO announced that they're implementing an AI system\\nto evaluate all incoming resumes.\\n\\nHe explained that this move will save time\\nand eliminate human bias,\\nbut Sarah knows it isn't quite that simple.\\nShe's worried that training the new system\\non the resume's past employees\\nwill only teach the AI to replicate the human biases\\nthat already exist in the organization.\\nBut she didn't have the communication skills\\nto express her concerns,\\nand now she knows she missed an opportunity\\nto influence an important decision in her organization.\\n\\nLet's rewind and see how this scenario\\ncould have played out differently\\nif Sarah and her colleagues had a stronger foundation\\nin power skills.\\nNow, power skills\\nare those essential, transferable abilities\\nthat help us navigate complex situations.\\nThey include critical thinking, communication,\\ndigital literacy, and adaptability.\\nThese skills form the pillars of our skill bridge,\\nconnecting our current capabilities with future challenges.\\n\\nNow, let's go back to Sarah.\\nWhat if she said something like this?\\n\\\"I have some concerns about implementing an AI system\\nfor resume evaluation without proper safeguards.\\nCan we discuss the potential risks\\nand how we might mitigate them?\\nAI systems have been shown\\nto inadvertently perpetuate biases\\npresent in their training data.\\\"\\nBy raising her concerns,\\nSarah was able to form a diverse team\\nto oversee the AI's development and implementation.\\n\\nBecause she applied her digital literacy\\nto identify a problem and propose a solution,\\nshe helped her organization implement a much better solution\\nfor their problem\\nand avoid a potentially disastrous implementation of AI.\\nWhen we leverage power skills in this manner,\\nwe become recognized for our value to the organization\\nand become an essential part of the leadership team.\\nAs AI becomes more prevalent in our workplaces,\\npower skills become increasingly important.\\n\\nThey help us critically evaluate\\nAI solutions before implementation.\\nEffectively communicate complex AI concepts\\nto diverse stakeholders.\\nAdapt to rapidly changing technological landscapes.\\nAnd ensure ethical and inclusive use of AI technologies.\\nThe skills bridge is built on these power skills.\\nThey provide a stable foundation\\nas we venture into the unknown territories of AI.\\n\\nBy cultivating power skills across your organization,\\nyou can create a robust skill bridge\\nconnecting your team's current capabilities\\nwith the challenges of tomorrow's AI driven world.\\nThis bridge ensures that as we embrace AI,\\nwe do so safely, ethically, and effectively.\\nLet's explore how to develop these crucial power skills\\nin the age of AI.\\nBut before we do,\\npause the course and download the handout;\\nQuestions to Ask Stakeholders\\nAbout AI Transparency and Fairness,\\nand complete the first activity for this lesson,\\nThe Room Where it Happened.\\n\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:2132166\",\"duration\":201,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Identifying and prioritizing power skills in the age of AI\",\"fileName\":\"5960110_en_US_06_02_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":381,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"handoutNotes\":\"Handout 6.2 Power Skills Survey.pdf\",\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"With an emphasis on technical skills common in the workplace, it can be difficult to obtain the stakeholder will and support necessary to nurture power skills, yet these skills are more important than ever before due to the heightened risks of the age of AI. In this video, learn how to present a compelling case for specific power skills that are essential for your organization so that you can influence and guide stakeholder decisions for talent development.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":8185036,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- One of my favorite quotes when I talk about AI\\nis from the Spider-Man comics.\\n\\\"With great power comes great responsibility.\\\"\\nWhile powerful AI tools are amplifying\\nour human capabilities, they can also magnify our mistakes.\\nNew technologies have always come with unanticipated risks,\\nbut with AI, the risks are elevated\\nand often hard to predict.\\nLet's see how some people are handling it.\\nMeet Luisa, a research scientist.\\n\\nWhen her lab implemented an AI system for data analysis,\\nshe used her critical thinking skills\\nto question the AI's conclusions.\\nYou see, the AI had flagged\\nan unusual pattern in her research data.\\nInstead of accepting it blindly, she dug deeper.\\nHer critical analysis revealed a flaw in the AI's algorithm,\\npreventing a potentially misleading publication.\\nHere's Marcus, a project manager at a tech startup.\\n\\nHis company's AI project management tool\\nsuggested an unrealistic timeline.\\nRecognizing this error, Marcus adapted the process,\\ncombining the AI's efficiency with human expertise\\nto complete the project on time\\nwithout burning out the team.\\nAnd then there's Sophia, a customer service team leader.\\nWhen her team first introduced an AI chat bot\\nfor customer service, customers were frustrated\\nby the perceived lack of human support.\\nSo Sophia reworked the bot to offer\\nthe first line of support\\nbut made sure that unresolved issues\\nwere referred immediately to a human worker\\nfor further attention.\\n\\nThis approach improved both the AI's performance\\nand customer satisfaction.\\nThese stories illustrate\\nhow power skills like critical thinking, adaptability,\\nand communication form the essential components\\nof our skills bridge.\\nBut every organization's bridge will be unique.\\nTo build yours, you need to identify and prioritize\\nthe power skills most crucial for your team.\\nOne way to identify the power skills\\nyou'll need in your organization\\nis to conduct a survey across all groups and departments.\\n\\nIn the first round, ask questions like these.\\nWhich tasks will be changed, enhanced,\\nor replaced by AI in your role?\\nWhat challenges do you face when working with AI tools?\\nWhich human skills do you rely on most when using AI?\\nWhat skills do you think will be most valuable\\nas AI becomes more prevalent?\\nOnce you have those results, you can prioritize these skills\\nby thinking about how each skill can help you thrive\\nin the age of AI.\\n\\nRemember, the goal isn't to compete with AI\\nbut to complement it.\\nTo get you started, I've provided\\na suggested survey as a handout.\\nPlease feel free to revise it to suit your needs,\\nand let me know what you learn\\nabout the power skills in your organization.\\nOur power skills are the mortar\\nthat hold the bricks of AI capabilities together,\\ncreating a skills bridge\\nthat's greater than the sum of its parts\\nand built to last a long, long time,\\nwhatever the future brings.\\n\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:5210163\",\"duration\":294,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Striking a balance between AI skills and the people we serve\",\"fileName\":\"5960110_en_US_06_03_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":612,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Rather than continually re-establishing the relevance of power skills in a changing organization, building a set of talent development principles can help keep the organization on track and build a culture of continuous skilling in the age of AI. In this video, learn how to write guiding principles so you can help your organization focus on essential power skills that will help maintain an ethical balance of AI technology and human judgment.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":12495893,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- We've journeyed through the landscape\\nof AI and power skills,\\nand now you face your ultimate challenge,\\nstriking the balance between AI capabilities\\nand the people we serve.\\nAs we integrate AI into our organizations,\\nwe must remember, technology is a tool,\\nnot a replacement for human judgment.\\nLet's explore some cautionary tales\\nthat highlight the importance of this balance.\\nMeet Leaf and Mortar,\\na company that implemented an AI-driven recruitment system\\nto streamline hiring.\\n\\nThe AI promised to find the best candidates\\nquickly and efficiently.\\nSounds great, right?\\nYeah, not quite.\\nThe AI, trained on historical data,\\nbegan systematically rejecting qualified candidates\\nfrom underrepresented groups.\\nThe lack of critical thinking in implementing this system\\nled to a significant diversity problem\\nand potential legal issues.\\nNow, let's visit H+ Sport,\\na company that replaced its entire customer service team\\nwith AI chatbots.\\n\\nThe decision was driven by cost-cutting\\nwithout considering the full spectrum of customer needs.\\nThe result?\\nA surge in customer complaints\\nabout the lack of empathy and understanding\\nin resolving complex issues.\\nThe absence of emotional intelligence\\nand effective communication skills\\nled to a sharp decline in customer satisfaction.\\nThese examples underscore a critical point,\\nto implement AI effectively,\\nwe must consider both the skills gaps\\nand the human needs associated\\nwith acquiring or developing those skills.\\n\\nIt's not just about what AI can do,\\nbut how it integrates with human capabilities\\nto expand on what our human employees can do.\\nSo how do we strike this balance?\\nLet's develop some guiding principles.\\nTake a human-centered approach.\\nAlways start with the people you serve.\\nConsider ethical issues.\\nRegularly assess the ethical implications\\nof AI implementations.\\nEncourage continuous learning.\\n\\nFoster a culture of ongoing learning in your organization.\\nDeploy complementary skills together.\\nIdentify and develop human skills\\nthat complement AI capabilities.\\nPractice transparent communication.\\nClearly communicate the role of AI in your processes.\\nConduct regular audits.\\nCheck AI systems for biases or unintended consequences.\\nAnd set up feedback loops.\\n\\nEstablish mechanisms for humans\\nto provide feedback on AI performance.\\nBy following these principles,\\norganizations can create a symbiotic relationship\\nbetween AI and human skills.\\nLet's see how this might look in practice.\\nBack at Leaf and Mortar,\\nthey've redesigned their recruitment process.\\nThe AI now works alongside human recruiters,\\nproviding initial screenings,\\nwhile humans conduct nuanced evaluations\\nand make final decisions.\\n\\nRegular audits ensure the AI isn't perpetuating biases.\\nAt H+ Sport, AI chatbots now handle routine inquiries,\\nfreeing up the agents to tackle complex issues\\nrequiring empathy and creative problem-solving.\\nContinuous training helps those agents develop the skills\\nto work effectively alongside AI.\\nAs we conclude our journey across the SkillBridge,\\nremember, the strongest organizations of the future\\nwill be those that harness the power of AI\\nby nurturing uniquely human skills.\\n\\nBy striking this balance,\\nwe create workplaces that are not just efficient,\\nbut also ethical, empathetic,\\nand truly serve the people at their heart.\\nIn our first lesson, I asked you to create a vision\\nof your organization in the future.\\nGo back to that vision now and ask yourself,\\n\\\"What needs to happen now to make that vision come true?\\\"\\nThis is the start of your SkillsBridge plan.\\n\\nWrite your ideas down\\nand share them with your team and stakeholders.\\nI hope you also share these ideas on LinkedIn,\\nso we can start a discussion\\nabout the skills we're developing\\nto face the challenges and opportunities of the future.\\n\"}],\"name\":\"6. Building Power Skills With AI\",\"size\":30776000,\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentChapter:2133168\"},{\"duration\":814,\"entries\":[{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:5210162\",\"duration\":267,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"What is skills leadership?\",\"fileName\":\"5960110_en_US_07_01_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":585,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"handoutNotes\":\"Activity 7.1 AI Leader of the Year.pdf\",\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Adopting a skills approach to talent development requires a new set of leadership skills throughout the organization, to maintain and grow essential leadership practices. In this video, learn how to define skills leadership so you can implement a skills leadership program in your organization.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":8877287,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- In today's evolving business landscape,\\nthe concept of skills leadership\\nhas become really important.\\nBut what exactly is skills leadership,\\nand what new skills will leaders need to navigate a future\\nthat is populated by AI assistants\\nworking side by side their human coworkers?\\nWell, here's my definition.\\nSkills leadership is the ability to guide an organization\\nthrough the complex process of identifying, nurturing,\\nand deploying the right skills at the right time.\\n\\nThese future leaders, many of whom\\nare already on their way up inside your organization,\\nmust be able to connect your current talent pool\\nwith the skills needed for future success.\\nAnd they will do this\\nthrough the help of artificial intelligence.\\nWhile traditional leadership\\nfocused on managing people and processes,\\nSkills leadership requires a fundamental shift\\nin mindset and approach.\\nLeaders must now become skills architects.\\n\\nThey need to design and implement strategies\\nthat align workforce capabilities\\nwith future business needs.\\nAct as talent catalysts.\\nLeaders must create environments\\nthat foster continuous skill development\\nto meet continuously changing challenges in the workforce.\\nEmbrace data-driven decision making.\\nUnderstanding and leveraging skills data\\nis crucial for informed workforce planning.\\n\\nDemonstrate adaptability.\\nThe skills landscape is constantly changing,\\nand leaders must cultivate organizational agility\\nthrough example.\\nFoster a skills-first culture.\\nThis means prioritizing skills\\nover traditional qualifications in hiring,\\ndevelopment, and promotion decisions.\\nAnd practice critical thinking.\\nLeaders must sharpen their ability\\nto analyze complex skills data, evaluate emerging trends,\\nand make sound judgements about future skill needs.\\n\\nTraditional leadership programs often fall short\\nin preparing leaders for this skilled-centric future.\\nHere are some steps I recommend.\\nImplement AI-powered leadership development.\\nUse AI to personalize learning paths,\\nand provide real-time feedback\\non skills leadership behaviors.\\nCreate immersive learning experiences.\\nUse virtual and augmented reality\\nto simulate complex skill scenarios\\nand decision making processes.\\n\\nEstablish cross-functional skills councils.\\nEncourage leaders to collaborate across departments\\nto identify and develop critical skills.\\nAdd skills mapping to leadership KPIs.\\nMake skills forecasting and development\\na key performance indicator for leaders.\\nAnd develop skills empathy.\\nTrain leaders to understand and value diverse skill sets\\nand their potential applications.\\n\\nBy adopting these new tactics,\\nskills leaders will guide their teams across the gaps\\nbetween our current capabilities and our future challenges.\\nLet's look at this list again.\\nNotice there is no programming language on this list,\\nno technical requirements, or degrees.\\nThese are all very human skills, the kind that come from\\nthe most powerful intelligent machines\\nthe world has ever known, us.\\n\\nJournalist Sydney J. Harris once said that \\\"The real danger\\nis not that computers will begin to think like men,\\nbut that men will begin to think like computers.\\\"\\nLet's hope we never do.\\nIn our next video,\\nwe'll delve deeper into the specific strategies\\nand AI power tools that can help you\\nbecome an effective skills leader in the age of AI.\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:5208166\",\"duration\":280,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Cultivating a skills mindset across the organization\",\"fileName\":\"5960110_en_US_07_02_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":408,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"In a skills-based organization, everyone is a skills leader, driving their own skills development while sharing their skills with others. In this video, learn how to modify messaging and training programs so you can cultivate a skills leadership mindset for all employees.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":12106280,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- Let's look at how you cultivate a skills mindset with AI.\\nImagine three HR managers are facing unique challenges.\\nBethany oversees a tech firm\\nwhere half the staff views AI as a threat.\\nJose is struggling to integrate AI tools\\ninto his manufacturing company's outdated training programs,\\nand Sheila must upskill a diverse workforce\\nin a rapidly evolving financial services landscape.\\n\\nSound familiar?\\nDid you see yourself in any of these situations?\\nHR leaders everywhere are asking,\\nhow do we prepare our people not just to adapt,\\nbut to thrive in the age of AI?\\nThe answer lies in cultivating a skills mindset,\\nviewing AI not as a replacement,\\nbut as a powerful ally in our endless quest for growth\\nand innovation.\\nLet's break it down into actionable steps.\\n\\nStep one, demystify AI.\\nPull back the carton on it.\\nAs Gary Marcus puts it,\\n\\\"There are known knowns and known unknowns,\\nbut what we should be worried about most\\nis the unknown unknowns.\\\"\\nSo let's eliminate as much of the unknown as possible.\\nOrganize AI awareness workshops\\nand showcase real world applications that will resonate\\nwith your employees.\\n\\nStep two, identify AI enhanced skills.\\nPinpoint the human skills in your organization\\nthat AI can amplify, not replace.\\nStart with a company-wide skills audit.\\nMap those current skills against future needs,\\nhighlighting areas where AI can boost human capabilities.\\nStep three, personalized learning journeys.\\nUse AI to tailor learning paths for each employee\\nwith an AI-driven learning platform that adapts\\nto individual learning styles, pace, and career aspirations.\\n\\nYou can learn more about this step in my course\\nUsing Gen AI to Develop Personalized Learning Plans.\\nStep four, foster an experimentation culture.\\nEmbrace the fail fast, learn faster mentality.\\nCreate sandboxes where employees can play\\nwith AI tools without fear.\\nStep five, lead by example.\\nShow your team how you are using AI\\nto enhance your own skills and decision making.\\n\\nBe sure to share your successes and stumbles alike.\\nStep six, develop an AI Ethics playbook.\\nAs Aldo Leopold said,\\n\\\"Ethics is doing the right thing\\neven when no one else is watching.\\\"\\nBut here's a little tip, when it comes to implementing AI,\\nsooner or later, everyone is watching,\\nso let's get it right.\\nNow let's circle back to our HR managers\\nand see how they're facing their own challenges.\\n\\nBethany organized an AI MythBuster series\\ninviting employees to explore AI's potential,\\nand the result was a 40% increase\\nin voluntary AI training participation.\\nJose gamified the AI learning process,\\ncreating a company-wide AI skills olympics.\\nThose outdated training programs transformed\\ninto exciting challenges with teams\\nsolving real business problems using AI tools.\\n\\nAnd Sheila implemented an AI powered skill matching platform\\nallowing employees to discover new career paths\\nbased on their unique skill sets and AI-augmented potential.\\nThe common thread through all of this\\nis they all cultivated a skills mindset,\\nviewing AI as a catalyst for growth.\\nAs we stand at the frontier of the AI age,\\nremember this, technologies come and go,\\nreplaced by newer shinier tools,\\nand the most powerful tool isn't today's version\\nof artificial intelligence.\\n\\nIt's our uniquely human ability to learn,\\nadapt, and grow.\\nBy embracing AI as a partner,\\nwe're not just preparing for the future of work,\\nwe're building it.\\n\"},{\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentVideo:2134167\",\"duration\":267,\"visible\":true,\"requiredForCertificateOfCompletion\":true,\"name\":\"Cultivating a skills framework with AI\",\"fileName\":\"5960110_en_US_07_03_VT\",\"demo\":false,\"videoCreationMetadata\":{\"rawDurationSeconds\":858,\"solutionVideo\":false,\"handoutGraphicsIncluded\":false,\"assignedBy\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesPickups\":false,\"challengeVideo\":false,\"handoutNotes\":\"Additional Resources.pdf\",\"hasSlides\":false,\"graphicsIncluded\":true,\"assignedTo\":\"urn:li:member:-1\",\"includesAlternateFootage\":false},\"description\":\"Skills are not a trend or a \\\"flavor of the month\\\" management style. Skills form the foundation of individual and organizational success at all levels. In this video, learn how to illustrate a framework that works for your organization so you can use AI to identify, nurture, and accelerate the development of essential skills across the organization.\",\"captionsStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"cdnStatus\":\"AVAILABLE\",\"size\":11701326,\"solution\":false,\"welcomeContent\":null,\"challenge\":false,\"assetStatus\":\"COMPLETE\",\"transcript\":\"- As science fiction author William Gibson aptly put it,\\n\\\"The future is already here.\\nIt's just not evenly distributed.\\\"\\nAs an HR leader,\\nyour role is to find those pockets of the future\\nin the present\\nand nurture them into maturity with your organization.\\nThink of these as sections of the AI skills bridge\\nthat are already completed.\\nLike these.\\nMeet Elena, a mid-level manager at a global logistics firm.\\n\\nShe remembers when AI was just a buzzword\\nand now it's the backbone of her company's operations.\\nAs she sips her morning coffee,\\nshe reflects on her journey\\nto become the leader she is today.\\nElena recalls her first AI project,\\na chat bot for customer service.\\nShe didn't code it herself,\\nbut she learned to speak the language of her tech team.\\nNow, she confidently discusses machine learning models\\nwith data scientists and user experience with designers.\\n\\nYou see, you don't need to be a tech guru,\\nbut you do need to speak their language.\\nWhen the AI started making biased decisions in hiring,\\nElena didn't panic.\\nShe had prepared for this.\\nHer team quickly identified the issue in the training data\\nand corrected course.\\nIn the AI world,\\nethics isn't just a department, it's everybody's job.\\nRemember the global supply chain crisis? Elena does.\\nWhile competitors floundered,\\nher team's AI-powered simulation helped them pivot quickly,\\nturning potential disaster into opportunity.\\n\\nIn an AI world, change isn't just constant.\\nIt's exponential. So adapt or be left behind.\\nEvery Friday, Elena blocks off an hour for learning.\\nSometimes it's a new AI tool.\\nOther times it's a leadership book.\\nHer team has caught on, creating a culture of curiosity.\\nIn the AI age, your skills have an expiration date.\\nSo my advice, keep learning or risk becoming obsolete.\\n\\nWhen automation made some roles redundant,\\nElena didn't just hand out pink slips.\\nShe worked with each team member to find new opportunities,\\nleveraging their strengths\\nin this new AI augmented workplace.\\nAs AI handles more analytics,\\nour human skills like empathy become our superpowers.\\nElena remembers when she used to make decisions\\nbased solely on her gut feeling.\\n\\nNow she balances intuition with AI-driven insights.\\nIt's how she convinced the board\\nto enter a new market last quarter,\\na move that's already paying dividends.\\nBecause data and intuition aren't enemies,\\nthey're dance partners, and you are the choreographer.\\nBut Elena's proudest moment is when her human team\\nand AI systems worked together in perfect harmony\\nduring last year's product launch,\\nthe AI crunched data and predicted trends\\nwhile her team provided the creative spark\\nand emotional intelligence.\\n\\nYou see, it's not humans versus ai, it's humans and AI,\\nand that is a beautiful thing.\\nSo now it's time for you to envision your future.\\nIn our final practice activity, you're going to imagine\\nthat it's five years ahead in your future.\\nYou've just won the AI Leader of the Year Award.\\nLet's map out your journey, download the template,\\nand let your imagination run wild.\\nHow will you apply what you've learned in this course?\\nI encourage you to share it on LinkedIn\\nand other social media platforms,\\nand I can't wait to see it.\\n\\nI'd love to see a world full of skills bridges,\\nall meeting the future in their own unique ways,\\npowered by the combined forces of AI-driven solutions\\nand the humans who build, maintain, and govern them.\\nWhat will you build?\\n\"}],\"name\":\"7. Nurturing Skills Leadership\",\"size\":32684893,\"urn\":\"urn:li:learningContentChapter:2133169\"}],\"size\":265081440,\"duration\":5956,\"zeroBased\":false}]}"